  ('zcrm_1579374000123674069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120922012', 'Kaitlyn Kirkham', NULL, '8-11-23 I have bad news and good news. Here''s the bad news first.
__________

Primary Insured Name: Kaitlyn Kirkham

Dear WENDY SCIPIONE,

Thank you for the opportunity to consider Kaitlyn Kirkham for coverage with National Life Group.

Unfortunately, we are unable to offer coverage on Kaitlyn Kirkham due to Medical History in Application indicating a history of anxiety with recent suicidal thoughts and Consumer Report from Milliman IntelliScript confirming a history of anxiety and depression in the past. We regret we cannot provide a more favorable decision.

Robin Jackson
(802) 229-3127

___________

Now the good news is I have another option that I believe you will easily qualify for to protect you in case of cancer, heart attack, stroke, accident and/or ICU. The Hope Institute will still offer you a $25 reimbursement towards this option as well. We will need to give you a quick education about how it works.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-17 13:50:21', '2023-08-17 13:50:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123719003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111241002', 'Joseph Pascoe', NULL, 'Colleen called in and said she reached out to Zion initially asking about what to do next now that she has billing to submit for sharing with a Need that she needs to start. When she explained to Zion what type of medical care she had, which was a follow-up appt. and other lab work her provider requested she have after Colleen gad her regular wellness visit. Which I confirmed for her is indeed Zion''s area of assistance. Colleen said the lady she spoke to at Zion said her situation sounds preventative and not Zion''s support. And for her to contact us at MPB. I got further clarification to make sure Colleen wasn''t being thrown around in loops and is directed to the 100% correct place from Patti Baron here. Indeed this is a Zion situation and she needs to start a Need with Zion. I transferred Colleen over and lastly told her if she is told the same thing or anything other than what we discussed and had confirmed is correct, then she should ask to speak to a supervisor or higher up employee at Zion. She thanked me and I reassured her she in fact did the correct thing/process with calling Zion first and collection bills after her IUA was met. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-08-17 13:35:08', '2023-08-17 13:35:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123700085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060578403', 'Jill Mehlhaf', 'Member aging into Medicare eff 10/1/2023', '1st notice sent to member &amp; advisor - 8/17 via outlook
