  ('zcrm_1579374000123486137', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107496002', 'Rebekah Liberty', NULL, '8-14-2023:  Rebekah & I talked.  She found a doc she likes, but she''s a concierge doctor.  We talked about the possible differences, so she to get details & pricing from that office.  She also had questions about a DPC doc she found as another source who is $79 per mo.  She wanting to figure out her Thyroid issue (which may be considered pre-x.  They''ve tested her for the last 5-yrs or so & although it''s been a little off, have never diagnosed her or felt she needs to do anything, so they''ve left it alone.  However, she''s starting to "feel" it and wants to pursue it.)  We disc the phase in-period if it is pre-x (my thought, if they''ve tested it for 5 years, it prob will be & I shared that w/her) and that it will be Dec 2023 before she''s past the 1yr waiting period.  She seemed to understand, but will call if she has further questions.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-14 18:44:33', '2023-08-14 18:44:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123486129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005676955', 'Hillary Harris', NULL, '8-14-2023:  Hillary e-mailed me upset she rec''d a bill from Planstin for srvcs in 3/2022.  My response via Outlook e-mail:
     Hi Hillary,
          It is odd they are sending this so far past the original date.  
          However, this isn''t a bill, it''s an explanation of benefits and shows what was paid by Planstin on your behalf.  
          The only ones that could tell you why this was sent would be Planstin.  Their claims customer service number is listed at the top left of the sheet if you want to call them.
          Sometimes, the provider, UWH of North Carolina LLP, inadvertently rebill for the service and it sparks this notice showing the services were previously paid.  
          Regardless, this is not a bill.  You owe nothing.
          Hope this helps!     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-14 18:20:44', '2023-08-14 18:20:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123486124', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104457002', 'Normandie Rainwater', NULL, '8-14-2023:  Normandie sub tckt #: 2918 = 
Normandie Rainwater     11 Aug 02:25 PM     ( 3 days ago = a Saturday )
     HI, Our daughter (Violet), who is on our plan is leaving for college in California. I''m wondering how this impacts how she should access care and our care plan. Thank you!
     - I called & LM for Normandie re: question = nothing really changes.  She can access care in CA, the same way she does at home.  Please call the concierge line M-F 9-8eastern & gave her the ph # so we can go over it w/her.  But, basically, the chg is location doesn''t impact much.  [Did NOT go into how counseling in CA may be impacted.  Can talk to her about that if we discuss this further.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-14 17:51:41', '2023-08-14 17:51:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123486110', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120972012', 'ELA RAMCHANDANI', NULL, '8-14-2024:  Kelly Frederickson created ticket #: 2919.
     - Deepak:  Got new "ins" w/us, but when he & his wife say Dr Nibha Mediratta a few weeks ago, they are now receiving a $500+ bill to cover their annual wellness.  He''s going to call & let them know he is an ''Our Primary Doc Memb'' & a memb w/the doc, so the annual wellness & off visit are pd thru his mo memb fee.  He knows Mitesh Desai & has his ph # if they still do not understand.
     - Wife given a few referalls.  He asked how to decide who to see.  Sounds like his wife has several issues to take care of & it''s all diff docs.  Told him they can select the doc (no ntwk for specialties), $2500 IUA is issue spec.  Once they see a doc reg the issue (each issue) to call us & we will guide him is sub a ''med need'' if it looks like it will be >$2500 because to include the early expenses 6mos deadline, so may not be near IUA yet.  
     - Disc pre-x on wife''s issue(s) too because they''ve only been members since July 1 & reminded him the the first yr is a waiting period.  He was in a hurry & w/the language barrier I think he understood.  He agreed as if he did.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-14 17:12:17', '2023-08-14 17:45:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123486090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107280002', 'Bibi Frederick', NULL, '8-14-2023:  Bibi''s advisor, Kirk Bennett, submitted a ticket #: 2921.   
     - Bibi contacted her advisor saying the concierge wasn''t picking up even though she tried 4 times.  We''ve been shorthanded today and I''ve been on the phone a good portion of it.  When we are on the phone, it does not notify us that someone is/has called, so I cannot see any calls in my log from her - but, that just means I was probably on the phone.  Nahla''s been on the phone most of the day too, so, we were prob just already working w/members and that''s why we didn''t answer.
     - ILM for Kirk that IUD are sometimes cov by Planstin, but it''s only certain ones, not all of them.  That in the past it''s been the less expensive ones, but I didn''t see Bibi specifically asked about the IUD.  [I do see she asked about lab work around the IUD...]  We always advise people: to connect w/Planstin to see if the IUD in question is a benefit of the MEC.    
     - Called & tt Bibi:  She''s calling because Planstin is declining the $1044 & she doesn''t know why.  I explained the EOB should tell her why and Planstin can go over it w/her if she has further questions.  However, seeing the price, I told her I hadn''t seen anything that expensive covered.  She will ck the letter to see why they declined coverage and knows her Planstin card has their phone # if she has further questions.
         I see where we tt Bibi regarding a blood test the doctor wanted to run before inserting the IUD, and we told her we did not think that would be cov, but Planstin could conf.  I remember the conversation & thinking it was weird she wasn''t asking about the IUD itself.  The whole interaction was odd in my recollection.    
     - Ticket closed.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-14 15:46:20', '2023-08-14 17:10:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123465111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122122001', 'Elizabeth Bay', NULL, '08.14.2023 Elizabeth put in an RX request for Advair Diskus * 100-50 mcg. In her form she placed Brand as her preference, but it was over $300 vs. the generic under $20. I called Elizabeth and I left her a message, letting her know the above and to confirm that she prefers Brand over Generic for Advair Diskus, or HFA. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-14 15:41:00', '2023-08-18 11:39:45'),
