  ('zcrm_1579374000123286028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080021001', 'Amy Fowler', NULL, '8-9-2023:  Amy called.  Her son needs some neuro diversity testing &amp; she wanted me to look up the medical codes to see if it was shareable.  I went over who we are &amp; how Zion''s ''med need'' dept would be the only ones who might be able to help.  I trans her to them &amp; she know to tt that dept.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-09 13:18:54', '2023-08-09 13:18:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123286023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108050001', 'Jennifer Anderson', NULL, '8-9-2023:  Nahla & I called Planstin together, they''ve given her a hard time in the past, but then I forgot to bring her into the call.  Here''s the information I rec''d (sent this to Nahla so she can help Jennifer):

tt Hillary at Planstin - Jennifer Anderson is showing effective on their end, however, they do not show any record of this claim coming through.  Nahla, please have Jennifer call the billing office to make sure they sent the claim to the correct address:  PO Box 21747, Eagan, Minn  55121  Also, let her know her Group #: G1200313-17 isn''t on the letter, so they may not have taken all the information they need off of her Planstin ID card.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-09 12:42:50', '2023-08-09 12:42:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123277029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080021001', 'Amy Fowler', NULL, '08.09.2023 Amy called to inquire about the tiny amount billed by her provider that Planstin DID NOT cover (under $10). Although they are small amounts, Amy found it unusual, as it is, because it is usually covered. 
