  ('zcrm_1579374000123164179', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120906098', 'Janice Hinds', NULL, '8/8/23 - Called Janice to do her welcome call. She had to reschedule because she was getting ready to eat lunch. I made an exception for Tuesday the 15th at 4 PM. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-08-08 13:05:32', '2023-08-08 13:05:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123177087', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109512002', 'Gabrian McPhail', NULL, '08.08.2023 Gabe wants to go see an annual check up. Preventative. She wants to make sure she is going about the steps the right way. I walked her through the process, including the verbiage to use and how to separate anything NONpreventative from the preventative appointment. 
**************************************************************************************
Gabe called back asking for guidance on how to search/find a provider/facility in the PHCS network. I asked if she was using the MultiPlan link and she said yes. I offered her other choices to email her to deepen her research: Healthcare BlueBook & Healthgrades. I emailed it to her with instructions via Outlook. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-08 12:44:34', '2023-08-08 15:07:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123217025', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089149002', 'Daniel Connelly', NULL, '8-8-2023:  Cynthia called.
     - Having trouble w/Zion - daughter was diagnosed after their membership started. 
 The chiropractic care has helped the curve, but Zion says chiropractic care not considered twds scoliosis treatment.  They declined it while they were moving & only gave her 30-days to appeal, which w/everything going on was not enough time.  I reminded her that all chiro care req''s prior approval.  That maybe, if she could submit before & after x-rays to prove it''s working, or get a treatment plan & ask for approval ahead of time, maybe they would make an exception on both the time limit to appeal (due to moving circumstance) and would allow some chiro treatment.  We did discuss how chiro care is lmtd at best due to the stability of the community, which she seemed to understand.  That took us into the HSA & HMA conversations (see below).
     - Trying to sub another ''med need'' using old instructions, so we walked thru the curr req for an invite twds a ''memb portal''.  She''ll conf if each memb 18+ needs their own, etc.  We did not discuss what she''s trying to sub, but I did mention the 6mos deadline from DOS for expenses to be considered.
     - HSA: They''ve funded this, but have so many expenses, it''s runny quite low.
     - HMA: She will call her advisor Melissa Blatt to see if she offers.  I was very clear completely diff than the HSA.  Gave quite a few details & this could be a good fit for them.  She really did not want to call her advisor Melissa Blatt because she hasn''t heard from her since they signed up.  I got to her to understand it was a good time to reconnect & if afterwards she''s still frustrated, or Melissa doesn''t offer the HMA, to let me know we could go from there.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-08 12:22:37', '2023-08-08 12:55:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123177079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017126041', 'Steven Strehlow', NULL, '08.08.2023 Julie aging out. Wants to be removed.
