  ('zcrm_1579374000123015019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091136002', 'Thelma Dillon', NULL, '08.04.2023 Thelma called to get to see if she wants to go to the preventative appt TODAY. She was already on the fence whether to go or not.
In the end Thelma decided she will go to the appointment. She asked what questions can she ask to maintain a preventative appt. I guided her to let them know that the appt needs to remain preventative as well, for their boundaries. 
I guided her to the HEALTHCARE.GOV site, via CRM email, to peruse the topics expected/safe to discuss at a preventative appointment. She asked about the previous site I mentioned to her the other day, and I remember sharing HEALTHCARE BLUEBOOK. We found that link in her Summary of Care Email, she copied and pasted it in a spreadsheet, along with the Healthcare.gov one. After that I waited on line while she organized her sites, and I added the HEALTHGRADE.COM, and explained how to use that one as well.
Thelma was more at ease today, and more receptive and open to talk to. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-04 12:01:11', '2023-08-04 12:01:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123019003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111992001', 'Lars Ensign', NULL, '8-4-2023:  Lars called back.  He''s incredibly frustrated & feeling like MPB is bouncing him around.  He says he''s talk to several people at the FL office and finally rec''d an e-mail from JK with a link to create a ticket, but even then the link did not work (I''m not sure why they did not try to trans him to the concierge line.  Maybe we were all on the phones?)
     I worked with him to guide him in asking for a Zion Memb Portal invite and how/what to do for starting a ''med need''.  By the time he got to me, he was sure we are just taking his money.  I assured him I will get him thru this.  I made sure he knows to call the concierge line, NOT the corp office as we will be able to help him.  (He was mad the office didn''t know Zion just chg''d their sub process so their instructions were wrong.  I let him know they do not deal with that on a daily basis & I only know from dealing w/it day in and day out.)  He now has the concierge ph #, knows our days & hours, and I told him although any of us can help him, he can ask for me.  He''s on the west coast, so this may happen naturally anyway.
     He seemed relieved to realize he can pay cash upfront & get reimb.  I reminded him of the 6mos from the DOS deadline & let him know as the ''med need'' proceeds he may find getting estimates & using their money more convenient, but it is up to him.  He kept saying he''s going to go to "reg ins".  As an ER doc, I let him know that''s what he''s used to, but that I think he will find this is wonderful once he sees how it works.  Either way, open enrollment is a few months off, so let''s try to get this going and he can try it until then. 
     Hopefully, his having the accurate ph # for the concierge line will help.  I don''t know if he''s not connecting w/us due to us being shorthanded or what, but when we got off the phone he seemed better.

He''s been diagnosed with cancer and has a catscan soon, then a urologist surgical proceedure early Sept.  He lives in the mtns, so the price is dbl near him, but has a cheaper option ~35 minutes away.  I let him know if the further location works, it helps protect the community.  He seemed to understand, although he was so upset, it''s diff to know what he was retaining.
     He wanted off the phone, but at some point, I think HCBB would be great for him.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-04 11:47:50', '2023-08-04 14:11:40'),
