  ('zcrm_1579374000122937043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079141002', 'Timothy Church', NULL, '08.03.2023 Rebecca called to cancel the membership. I asked her if it is due to a job with benefits, and she said yes. Due to my previous coaching on this matter, the job with benefits being the reason to cancel that is, I guided her to the cancellation form on our Member Portals and Updates page. I reminded her to click submit and she was good to go. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-03 11:38:45', '2023-08-03 11:38:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122937029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108891001', 'Sarah Stokes', NULL, '08.03.2023 Sarah has receipts to submit to Zion. She called asking "I have receipts to submit to you guys. Do you have an email for me to send them with?" I said that sounds like you have receipts for Zion to share for you, let me help you do that. I confirmed her account, and went over the instructions on what is going on with Zion and what to expect from them through the beginning of this process. I reminded her about the 6 mos deadline and fulfilling her IUA, $1000. I gave her their number and direct transferred her when her and I were done talking. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-03 11:11:05', '2023-08-03 11:16:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122939058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122133002', 'Paul Szotek', NULL, 'Welcome call complete with Paul and Sarah. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-08-03 11:08:53', '2023-08-03 11:08:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122937021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109380034', 'Tim Nickles', NULL, '08.03.2023 Tim called trying to log into his portal, but going about it by wanting to change his passcode. So I asked him to take a step back, to start over, and I will give him his log-in information.
I did that, and he was able to log in. Then attempted to change his passcode, and asked if this is where to change it. I said I assume so, but I''m not sure. I told him that I have been coached not to have members change the alpha-numeric passcode due to numerous challenges that has propelled the member into.  He said ok, I''ll leave it like that for now. 
*******************************************************************************************
Tim called back saying that he updated his banking/billing information, but it is not giving him the option to delete the previous information. I told him that sounds like an Administration action, and proceeded to guide him to the change form on the Member Portal and Updates Page, so admin would see what he wants/trying to do. Tim seemed in a hurry or filled with anxiety, and was talking over me. So I asked him to not cut me off, so I can get him to where he needs to be. He was kind and receptive and followed the instruction concisely to get to the the form and save the page for another time when needed. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-03 11:01:32', '2023-08-03 11:19:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122962003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '8-3-2023:  Andrew called.  He had his physical this week & the doc needs him to have a diagnostic catscan on his abdomen.  Unfortunately, the UHC system in Steamboat Springs, CO (where they live in the summer) is also where their PCP is, so the billing office is accusing them of fraud, because they do not want to use their Planstin on the catscan.
     Andrew has been in the medical field for years & is very competent when it comes to billing, med codes, etc.  It sounds like he''s a psychologist & was saying how horrible it is that she would accuse anyone of fraud over the phone.  I let him know this seems to be happening nationwide & I think it''s linked to the "ins" industry.
     He was using the term ''submit'', so I suggested he try to stay away for any "ins" terms: submit, "ins", copay, ded, etc.  He seemed to hear that.
     I also let him know that having the "superbill" Wendy always suggests is ideal, however, we are seeing issues w/the billing offices.  To try to get detailed invoices instead & we''ll deal w/the medical codes later if needed.  That it can''t just say scan, or office visit, it must be detailed for this to possibly work.
     He knows he can offer to pay the first 1k and ask them to bill him the balance.  Or, he may see if they are just willing to bill him.  They gave him a verbal estimate of ~$1800, he may either get a written estimate or the actual inv since Tues is just a few days away.
     We disc it''s doubtful we can get a ''med need'' started & approved by Tues, but he''s ok w/that & understands.  Since it''s just really a few business days away he may wait to start the ''med need'', but is going to call the billing dept & will call us when he''s ready for help sub the ''med need'' to Zion.     - CA

Andrew called back.  He didn''t get to tt the billing dept, but was able to get a written est for the scan.  However, they cannot show the discount on the estimate.  We decided he''s going to call tomorrow for the invite to set up his memb port (they are already closed today), then we talked about everything he needs to have ready in case the site is still timing out too quickly: Verbal est w/discount (comes to about 8% even though they told him 10%), the estimate, all prov names & cont info, etc.  
     He knows he''s resp for the first 1k & will worst case pay & get reimb for the extra $800+.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-03 10:46:22', '2023-08-03 17:36:17'),
