  ('zcrm_1579374000122899043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059725045', 'Michelle Skellion', NULL, '8-2-23 Michelle called bc her provider told her that Beck is no longer covered but I looked at her account in Zoho and Admin123 and I see both kids included as of 3/1/21. Her account is current and paid. I don''t see any problems on our end.  I gave her the MPB Concierge # to call and have them check with each entity to make sure they are showing active with them as well, ie. Planstin.  If I don''t hear from her again, then she''s all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-02 16:39:06', '2023-08-02 16:39:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122895033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109083002', 'Karin McGrath', NULL, '08.02.2023 Patrick called to learn how to search for a Urologist. I led him to the HCBB link via email on CRM, and briefly perused the site, and practice searched for a urologist and one procedure to learn the site better. Patrick seems well versed in his plan, and receptive. He knows he needs to present as a cash pay patient. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-02 15:45:56', '2023-08-02 15:47:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122895028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121048002', 'Irene Tammaro-Tallia', NULL, '08.02.2023 Karen Torsoe called to verify if her member, Irene understood or was confused from her welcome call, re: having a network for a preventative appointment. She asked if anything has changed in the last 3 days, and I said no. All I know is that since June 1st, members have the option to search for a provider under the PHCS (which is easiest), and if their doctor/finding a doctor is not on there, then they can go the RBP route.
Karen realized where her client misunderstood, and was no longer confused for her member. I explained it and gave her examples. Karen proceeded to ask me if I could call Irene up and rephrase the process for preventative appointments, I accepted. She also mentioned that Irene is going through a rough time with her dad, and if I could guide her towards our MAP program with M&S. I also accepted :). NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-02 15:32:29', '2023-08-02 15:49:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122909024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022839147', 'Ashleigh Bechtel', NULL, '8/2/23 - Ashleigh called in and asked to be transferred to RCI because she had a billing question. I direct transferred her. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-08-02 14:51:01', '2023-08-02 14:51:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122918048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022839060', 'Peyton Bell', NULL, 'Member will be aging into Medicare eff 9/1/23.  She submitted Cognito form in June/23 so no email were ever sent.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-02 14:39:14', '2023-08-02 14:39:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122892041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094942002', 'Tim Ottmann', NULL, '8-2-2023:  Tim & Angela called.  Lots of questions:
     - Tim needs an MRI on his knee.  He had the most recent surgery on this knee about 15-yrs ago & hasn''t had issues since then.  We disc that IF they determined this as a pre-x (which I do not expect, but want them to know worst case scenario), curr 2nd yr of memb = 25k, etc.  However, w/15 yrs, prob: 5k IUA for this issue.  Start ''med need'' w/in 6mos deadline to protect early expenses.  Went over 12mos close if no activity & then IUA resets.  
     - Angela had her ER visit in June.  She hasn''t started her ''med need'' yet, but knows the deadline & will get it done before the deadline even if she doesn''t have anything/everything yet to protect the expenses she''ll incur.  
     - Colonoscopy for Angela = follow-up from her ER visit.  I explained if this is the SAME issue as her ER visit, it should be on the same ''med need''.  We went over how it''s ''issue specific'' and all items towards that ''issue'' sb on the same IUA.  We did disc how it for some reason, the ER visit brought to light another issue, then it could be 2 IUAs.
     - Accident Policy to help cover the 5k IUA?  Tim thinks Analisa Cleland did sell them something, but isn''t sure what it covers.  They appreciated my transferring them to her # at the end of the call so they can find out if either of these instances would have help.  They have the super high 5k IUA.  I didn''t say anything, but they easily would have saved money this year with the 1k IUA, over paying the additional amounts they will on the 2 known issues had they had the lower IUA.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-02 14:32:54', '2023-08-03 15:54:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122918038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109361008', 'Laura Roessler', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation  eff 9/1 due to the fact that her spouse got a job w/benefits.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-02 14:29:59', '2023-08-02 14:29:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122918028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122342002', 'Chantal Carnes', NULL, 'Member will be cancelling eff 9/1 due to the fact that she cannot use this at her school.  I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-02 14:19:46', '2023-08-02 14:19:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122892033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100495002', 'Paul Eckenrode', NULL, '8-2-2023:  Paul & Leah called.  They are 6-wks pregnant & wanted guidance (easily past the waiting period):
     - HCBB:  We walked thru using HCBB together & Paul is quite adept at this.  We looked up everything from midwifes - gyno - obgyn - hosp (in case of emerg), etc.  We talked about the color coding, healthgrades.com, etc.
     - I sent them a freshly downloaded copy (=link) of the Aug 2023 Zion Maternity Guidelines for their reference.  They were wondering about home births, so we looked that up together.  I sugg interviewing midwifes as they may have a good sugg of a doc that is easy to work with, hosp for emerg, etc.  
     - IUAs:  They asked how it works.  I went over 1k is their initual resp, but if the baby should need something there could be a 2nd IUA of 1k (either if there is an issue, or if an issue at birth).
     -      - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-02 14:17:51', '2023-08-07 11:26:34'),
