  ('zcrm_1579374000122895012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091136002', 'Thelma Dillon', 'NB: Thelma WILL NEED DETAILED step by step EXPLANATIONS', '08.02.2023 Thelma called to better understand how to use her preventative - YET AGAIN. 
She went in with how the Planstin site said that lab work it is not covered, but it is covered with a doctor''s recommendations but under Zion guidelines. Thelma is confused between the both Planstin and Zion. So I went in with separating both first to set a better understanding moving forward.
It turns out Thelma is frustrated about a number of items:
-Getting a large Lab bill, ''cause her doctor ordered them and she did not know they were not covered under her preventative. I offered her to pull up the codes on either JasonHealth.com or Ultalabs.com, have it on screen while she calls the lab she had them done at and ask them if they accept this pricing even though it is after the fact.
-She has a in-grown toe nail (from what I understood), and wants to see a podiatrist ( THE PLAN AT THE BEGINNING OF THE CALL WAS TO WALK HER THROUGH SEARCHING FOR ONE ON HCBB, HOWEVER THE CALL TOOK AN HOUR, AND SHE WAS READY TO SPEAK TO Planstin via our notes below).
-She wants to start seeing a NaturoPath Medically licensed doctor for preventative, so I guided her to have that conversation with Planstin to gain approval.
-She also wanted to learn how & when to send bills to Zion, and we went over that extensively: INITIAL SERVICE PAPERS are to be sent with the INITIAL Medical Need Opening within 6 mos of the service, and the rest of the bills trickling in will be sent within the 6 mos of each of THOSE services) Thelma paraphrased the above with understanding.
.... this was a super long, difficult conv.  There was more, but I cannot recall all of it after-the-fact. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-02 12:44:48', '2023-08-02 17:58:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122892022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088570001', 'Nicholas Baciu', 'Mia''s e-mail (=Maria): mia.f.sullivan@gmail.com', '8-2-2023:  Mia (Maria) called.  She had a lot of questions:
     - ''Prev Care'':  She has her gyno w/pap coming.  Chose a PHCS doc from our list (she thinks, but the doc''s off said they could not find her ins, so she''s going to make sure they will at least bill it for her).  Making sure the ''initial visit'' will be billed w/''prev care'' med coding too.  
     - Planstin:  She called them & they were not helpful or very nice.  They basically told her they could not help her w/the doc she was seeing or what was covered.  I sent Jennifer a Teams chat so she''s aware.  Planstin has not been giving accurate info lately anyway.
        Went over how to present w/Planstin, only time "ins" = Y, only time you present an ID Card, doc must bill, all must have ''prev'' medical coding, etc.
     - Healthshare:  quick reminder how to present for an emerg/illness/accident:  No "ins", no ID card, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, resp for $2500 IUA & ask them to bill you for bal.  [Did not go over how IUAs work.  Did this quick info section in case they have an emerg.]
     - Concierge Line:  Encouraged her to use us as their first point of contact.  We can help them know how to proceed, even if it''s just to make sure we get them to the corr component.
     - ''Welcome Call'': Sent her & Nicholas the invite again & encouraged her to do the call as a 3-way call so they can help each other.  She seemed up for that.
     - CRM Correction:  Maria''s DOB is not listed here in the CRM.  Sent an e-mail to Dayra to please correct.  Confirmed w/Mia it is corr in Admin123 = 5/9/1988.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-02 12:26:36', '2023-08-02 13:10:34'),
