  ('zcrm_1579374000122875065', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000072020002', 'Jacob Bonnema', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Jacob called.  He got a new job that is providing healthcare for the family beginning 9/1/2023.  He hasn''t spoken to his advisor, Leslie Jablonski yet, but did send her an e-mail this morning so she would know why he cancelled.  Since he did that & he now has employer prov ins, I showed him the cancellation form online & let him know we''d need it no later than the 19th of this month, Aug.  He said he''s enjoyed his memb & how nice everyone is.  It sounds like this is a promotion & permanent, so I wasn''t worried about him coming back soon, after a temp position.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 16:50:05', '2023-08-01 16:50:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122864018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121804012', 'Emiley Stout', 'Completed Welcome Call', 'Completed 8/1/23 by JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-08-01 14:53:04', '2023-08-01 14:53:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063775002', 'Daniel Gutierrez', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Martha called back.  Zion was in a meeting &amp; she needed their ph # to call them back.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 14:50:23', '2023-08-02 11:50:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084172001', 'Jacqueline Wolfe', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Jacquie (= on the caller ID) called.  She wanted help getting into CirrusMD.  She''s looking for antibiotics for strep-throat, so I warned her they have a limited scope & generally, will not write antibiotics for strep as they want the pt to see a dr & get a culture.  She''s traveling in CA, so I told her to make sure she tells them that.  Maybe being away from home they''ll help her out.  Sent her the invite & she was texting w/the dr when we got off the phone.  She''ll call if she needs an RX Quote, or futher assistance.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 14:43:51', '2023-08-01 14:44:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122865033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, 'Member submitted PU form.  I will update in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-01 14:41:23', '2023-08-01 14:41:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122865023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109179002', 'Corey Vincent', NULL, 'Member submitted PU form I will update in A123.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-01 14:00:08', '2023-08-01 14:00:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000090966002', 'Angela Bryan', NULL, 'CPAP from 10 years ago
needs one for travel - light weight.
RESENT Summary of Care w/ zion and planstin email for resources.
I read to him what I found on the guidelines, AO 08.01.2023:
15. Durable Medical Equipment (DME) Durable medical equipment (DME) is shareable if it is prescribed by a licensed medical provider and if it is related to an approved sharing request. Durable medical equipment can generally be rented, is reusable by other patients, is prescribed for a specific illness or injury, and can be used in the home. Some examples of DME are oxygen tanks, wheelchairs, walkers, crutches, canes, and hospital beds. Zion HealthShare encourages members to rent equipment when possible if the rental costs for the duration of the treatment are less than the purchase price. Sharing in the cost of purchasing DME requires prior written approval from Zion HealthShare. Sharing is limited to 120 days per medical need. Sleep apnea equipment is not shareable.
However, he proceeded to want to learn to see a specialist, since it has been a while.
I''m not sure if he got confused and thought I said it is covered OR he just wants to get a referral to start over, since it has been a while. Might call back to clarify, after consulting with Cari. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 13:46:49', '2023-08-01 15:26:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077322076', 'Colin McCarthy', NULL, '08.01.2023 Received a request via email on Outlook for Colin.
Good afternoon Colin,

It is with pleasure to be able to share the following information to help you move forward with your coverage.
Regarding the subject of submitting an application for a medical need - we are experiencing a common "speed bump" with Zion. There has been an obstacle in that process, since the beginning of June, unfortunately. However, please know that the ''powers to be'' are working diligently to resolve this matter and recreate the convenient experience for our valued members. 
Presently, the process in submitting a medical need has changed, and we do believe is it is a temporary work around, until it''s back up and running independently. With that said, I will include a few simple steps below to follow to get you to completing and submitting a medical need.
Primarily, please remember that Zion members have a 6-month deadline to submit any bill towards a medical need to be shared, and each member is required to fulfill their IUA (Initial Un-shareable Amount) prior to any sharing to commence. In your case, your IUA is $1000.
 
Temporary Steps to Opening a Medical Need with Zion:
Because the website is not recognizing the members, we need to call Zion: 888-920-9466 ________ Choose #6 for Customer Service
After Speaking to a Zion representative, they will send you an invitation to start your medical need process (I suggest staying on the phone with them for this)
The 2nd main glitch is not allowing you to upload your documents/recognizing you again as a member, SO Zion will send you an email to correspond with them (work around).
Don''t hesitate to call them back, if you did not stay on the phone and you need additional assistance: __________ this time choose #5 medical need.
Their hours are Mon – Fri: 7am – 5pm Mountain Time. 
I''m glad you reached out to us, please do give us a call if you would like us to go over this again and transfer you to Zion.     NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 13:44:58', '2023-08-01 13:44:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107048002', 'Peter Coddington', 'COUPONS SENT 08.01.2023', '08.01.2023 An email was sent out via Outlook with coupons for the above RX requests. Here is what I sent in the body:
I was able to price your Rx requests for:
​Zoloft (Generic) • QTY 270 • 100 MG • Tablet • 
Nexium (Generic)  • QTY 180 • 40 MG • CAPSULE DR • 
I am glad I was able to find these deals for you, and I hope they are to your liking, and convenient for you, based on the zip code provided, 20777. Notice the amount for the Zoloft is 270, to fulfill 180 days of 1.5 tablets. You then can have a total of 180 whole tablets, & 180 half tablets to combine 150MG per day/dosage. 
Below are the prices as of ​08.01.2023. 
The average price for ​Zoloft (Generic) in your area is ~$37.00
​Zoloft (Sertraline-Generic) • 100 MG • 270 Tablet, 180 Day supply: Walgreens $30.02
The average price for ​Nexium (Esomeprazole Magnesium-Generic) Tablet in your area is ~$311.00.
​Nexium (Generic) • 40 MG • 180 CAPSULE DR • 180 Day supply: ​Walgreens $15.85
The total for all prescriptions at ​Walgreens = $45.87.
Please let me know your thoughts or if you need anything adjusted.      NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 13:34:38', '2023-08-01 13:34:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108424017', 'Jennifer Eisenberg', NULL, '08.01.2023 Jennifer called to make sure the process of adding her newborn Sage is complete. I confirmed it is, as I see his/her name in the CRM and Admin123 profile. 
Jennifer shared that they received a lab bill for Sage and was wondering if it goes towards her ZIon maternity medial need, and I said it should. The best thing to do is to contact Zion/submit the bill towards the need. If all else fails, they will tell you it is not a fit.
Jennifer wanted to know what the charges would be, now that she added Sage. I shared with her, as long as there was another child added prior to the new child it would not cost anything for the new child. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 13:29:46', '2023-08-01 13:29:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102931013', 'Jonathon Anderson', NULL, '08.01.2023 Kelli called in to better learn how to maneuver a preventative appointment for her husband Jonathon.
We went over the two options: PHCS or the RBP price model approach, how to maintain the appointment as preventative, and how to search for doctors in needed.
I reminded her of the Summary of Care email that has the resources that she can refer to for researching for a doctor and/or learning about them via HCBB and MultiPlan link.
Kelli will call us back if she has anymore questions. nT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 13:14:39', '2023-08-01 13:14:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113668002', 'Steven Valdez', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Kris called.  Steven lost his job & she can''t figure out why she''s paying $615 w/us, and Zion says she can have them directly for just $350 (?- I think that''s what she said) for the same thing.  She says they even give her telehealth, so again, she wants to cancel ''cuz she''s not getting anything more for all that money.  I let her know she is getting quite a bit more: ''prev care'', telehealth, counseling, etc., but this would be a better conv to have w/her advisor.  She apologized ''cuz she got quite snippy w/me.  
     She hadn''t spoken to her advisor Jane Kassel yet, so I let her know that is the place to start.  That I''m not the sales person, but Jane sb able to compare & contrast for her.  She seemed super hesitant to tt Jane, but finally said, okay, Jane''s lovely, I will call her.  I offered to transfer her and she declined.
     At the end, she said she also pays for ''Blueberry Pediatrics'' (something like that), where the doc actually comes to them and they are paying out of pocket for that and how they already got rid of a second PA policy...  Sounds like they''ve had a lot.
     Because we have the ''prev care'', I mentioned that the well-baby, prev care, items could potentially be billed by ''Blueberry Pediatrics'' to Planstin & pd for?  She''d have to see if they offer that service.
     With her looking at going direct to Zion, she''ll at least have the catastrophic if that''s what she decides.  She is calling Jane Kassel, so she''ll have help w/the cancellation if that''s her final decision.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 12:52:42', '2023-08-01 12:57:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122878023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014679198', 'Kari Rosckowff', NULL, '8-1-23 Kari called someone, likely Zion who told her wellness isn''t included. However, she has the MEC. It is included. But, she wants to go to dermatologist for skin check which isn''t included. I left her a vm and gave her the MPB Concierge Team # to call and explained a bit in the vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-01 12:49:49', '2023-08-01 12:49:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108617010', 'Lyubov Guhl', 'RECEIVED MPB Perm. to Discuss Plan w/ Steven Guhl 08.01.2023', '08.01.2023 Steven and Lyubov called to help Lyobov better understand her plan and how to find doctors. I resent the permission to discuss the mpb plan to Lyobov, and asked them to sign it, while we are on the phone. Lyubov is originally from Russia, her English is not very strong, so Steven helps her with a lot of community activity maneuvering.
I emailed them via CRM, the HCBB and Multiplan Link, as well as the Welcome Call Schedule link to set up her welcome call and learn more about her plan.
We opened the HCBB link and had her register/sign in. We perused it a bit together with a brief orientation on how to use and interpret the icons and color coded bar.
We opened the Multplan link and did a simple search for a family doctor, and guided her on how to present and maintain a preventative appointment. I guided her on how to confirm the doctors are in still in the PHCS network, and if they are not, how to work around that (RBP price model).
I explained the only card she will need is the Planstin card, which they have, and that we don''t use terminology like Deductible and Co-Pay.
I explained that there a lot of moving pieces in the plan, to please give us a call anytime, for doctor appointment coaching, or more. 
Steven was going to help Lyubov schedule her welcome call. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 12:20:59', '2023-08-01 12:20:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046605028', 'Donald Spiegel', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Donald called.  Had a full body scan & they found 2 lumps/bumps, so they are going to do 2 more focused scans.  These tests will be ~ $650, but we talked about they are 2 sep parts of the body & could be 2 ''med needs'' = 1k ea.  Once he has the tests and knows what''s next, he will call & we can help him decide how/if he should start a ''med need''(s).
     IF they find something, he may look at deciphering the expense for the orig full body scan to see if it could go towards his IUA.  He & his bros did them together, so he''ll have to look into that.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 12:09:44', '2023-08-01 12:18:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122878008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108399107', 'James Leo Durocher', NULL, '8-1-23  Leo is still waiting to find out what networks Dr. Hugate at Panorama Ortho that he will accept. He accepts different networks compared to the rest of the practice. His back is doing well right now. He only needs to see him every few years now. However, if something goes wrong, Dr. Hugate is the only one who can treat him at this point due to what''s been done thus far and the level of complexity.  He will call me when he gets his answers.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-01 11:30:14', '2023-08-01 11:30:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122865018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000057051028', 'Donald Fain', NULL, 'I reached out to member and explained to him that Sleep Apnea equipment would not be shareable per Zion guidelines. Not sure what Sally told him.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-01 11:14:52', '2023-08-01 11:14:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120108002', 'Penny Fallon', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Penny called.  She has a ''Prev Care'' appt w/pap & wanted to conf how to try to get it paid.  Doc is not in ntwk (she called Planstin & that''s what they told her.  They did not mention she can go outside ntwk.)  I let her know IF the doc will bill Planstin directly w/''prev med codes'', then she can still have it pd for.  This doc has become more of a cash doc, but she may pay out-of-pocket because her rates are very reasonable.  She will see if the papsmear, which will be tested by a separate comp, could poss be billed by the testing group to save a bit.  She was very nice & seems to understand.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 11:10:33', '2023-08-01 11:14:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122879003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447407', 'Elizabeth Friedlander', NULL, '08.01.2023 Liz called back with her estimate for a surgery in October on her hand. Opening a med need with her (a.k.a guiding her on what to expect when speaking to Zion to open the medical need).
Liz was concerned about not having the anesthesiologist pricing/cost on the estimate and I told her, it''s common for that not to be there, b/c they don''t know how much they are going to use perhaps or how long the surgery will take. Also told her not to worry about it, as the member has a 6 month deadline from receiving the bill to submit to Zion for reimbursements.
Liz was also wondering what to do about paying everything upfront, and told her not worry about that either, b/c once the medical need is open and approved, Zion will be in touch with the hospital for all finances for the surgery.
Liz confirmed that she is responsible for the $1000 IUA prior to sharing kicks in, but how to pay the $1000. I told her that she can actually ask them if they will take her $1000 IUA today to fulfill that part of the process. Then I direct transferred her to Zion, after I gave her their number and what extensions she should choose (#6 for cutomer service & #5 for medical need) .   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-01 11:06:03', '2023-08-01 11:16:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122869048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121443002', 'Sajindra Gunawardane', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-08-01 11:03:42', '2023-08-01 11:03:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120972012', 'ELA RAMCHANDANI', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Deepak called.  He''s needing a bunch of lab tests.  We walked thru putting items into his cart on JasonHealth.com.  But, we got to some that were diff to find.  He''s calling the doc''s off & asking if they can provide the ''ntc'' #s so we can be sure he''s selecting the corr tests.  He will call us back.     - CA

Deepak called back.  He''s struggling to get ahold of the doctor''s office, they are not answering (he''s rather impatient).  I instructed him on exactly what VM to leave.  He will do that.  If he hasn''t heard from them by tomorrow, he will call us back.     - CA

Deepak called back again.  He finally got ahold of the doc''s off & they told him they had no idea what the test #s would be.  They told him just to go to Quest & pay the self pay prices.  He checked & as best he can tell, that would be around $900.  The disc price is $216.  We decided he''s going to go ahead and pay thru JasonHealth.com.  Then take in both the pre-pd receipt & his lab order.  IF he''s missed something, he can consider paying the Quest self pay price on that item(s).  But, at least he got a huge savings on what he was able to find.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 11:02:31', '2023-08-01 12:07:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122878003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626120', 'Russell Finsterwald', NULL, '8-1-23 Called to understand his benefits better. Wanted to know about wellness but he didn''t choose to include it. He''ll hold off for now and might add it later. He asked about dermatology visit. I recommended he use the virtual healthcare app to start. He doesn''t have it set up yet. I gave him the Concierge toll free # to get it going and to start there. He was pleased to have that benefit that he will use.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-01 11:00:46', '2023-08-01 11:00:46');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000122875003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000057051028', 'Donald Fain', NULL, '8-1-2023:  Donald called back.  He hadn''t heard back from anyone.  
     - Sleep Apnea:  His machine''s motor life is expired.  His advisor, Sally Thomsen, told him specifically, it was covered after the first year, but w/a max of 5k.  When I asked if that was 25k, as in the pre-x phase-in period, he said no, he knew it was 5k.  I read the Zion Memb Guidelines re: sleep apnea, equip, testing, etc = None of which is covered/shareable.  Maybe Sally sold him a separate product?  He has a call into Sally and will talk w/her since she specifically told him this would be covered.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-01 10:49:10', '2023-08-01 11:17:19'),
