  ('zcrm_1579374000122781043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041906167', 'Pamela Tuck', NULL, '7-31-23 Pam and Court are moving now bc their property taxes just sky rocketed from the changes in the CO property tax laws that just got voted in and indicated it would not increase property taxes. So, they are needing to cut out a big expense which is DIRECT at $580. They are also paying Nextera too. Court had a knee replacement in Nov. 2022 which was in his 1st year of this membership, so they wound up paying the entire bill or $21K-$22K!!!!  They never called MPB but they did call Zion. Zion did not clearly explain that if he waited until Jan. 2023 it would be shared up to $25K!  I knew nothing about this. Also, they paid the entire bill and we might have been able to use the new Debt Eraser program but their income is slightly above the $69-$72K, so that might not have worked. She thinks they were also denied a colonoscopy but that would only have been in the 1st 6 months of membership. I wish they had called me or MPB. They were NOT guided well by whoever they called, which must have been Zion. There are no notes, hence they didn''t call MPB. After explaining each of these items to her again, she was very nice and said maybe when they are financially sound, they will come back. I let her know options change and we might have better options for them at any time.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-31 15:29:16', '2023-07-31 15:29:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120906098', 'Janice Hinds', NULL, '07.31.2023 Janice called to confirm her appointment with  Jen''s WC, I confirmed with Jen it is 8/8/2023 @3EST. Bookings was not pulling up for me.
Janice also wanted to know how to proceed with a non-preventative doctor''s appointment, and I told her to present as a cash pay patient and to save all receipts. If continued services continue for the same situation, to call us back so we can open a medical need. 
I requested that she might want to request the super bill for ZIon''s information, but she said that might be a problem to ask them, b/c they don''t get that detailed on their bills. I said well as long as ZIon can see how much, the date and who they are paying and for what, that is all they need. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 15:18:17', '2023-07-31 15:19:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122818016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079055002', 'Dale Leder', NULL, '07.31.23:  Cindy emailed me today. They are currently being charged $535 for Secure and $90 for Planstin HSA MEC (totalling $625).  She is asking if they can drop the $90 Planstin MEC and keep Secure.  I called Cindy and discussed her needs and options of new MECs as well as DIRECT plan. Gave her my website to check out and told her to think about what her needs are currently.  I explained the RBP approach w/the new MECs.  She said they haven''t been contributing to their HSA in a while and will think about both MECS and DIRECT and get back with me.  I told her to call w/any questions.
Note:  the website shows Secure for MS in highest age group to be $650 but she is being charged $625.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-07-31 15:18:02', '2023-07-31 15:18:02'),
