  ('zcrm_1579374000122813033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063775002', 'Daniel Gutierrez', NULL, '07.31.2023 Martha called to get help to find an orthopedic to look at her wrist injury. She was in a lot of pain, and was typing with one hand.
We briefly perused the Healthcare bluebook, b/c it was slow and not responding promptly like it usually does, but was able to finally find a list of doctors at the same group (search was limited due to lack of site responsiveness this time around. She could not pull up the list, she hit a roadblock with her computer, so she was not able to search the doctors or learn more about them or their practice via the hyperlinks that HCBB offers. Therefore, I took a snapshot of the limited amount of results we were able to conjure up, and sent them to her via outlook email.
*************************************************************************************
Martha called back to refresh her memory on how to search for a doctor via HCBB. We did but we did not see any stars/reviews for the doctor she had in mind. I guided her to other doctors on that list that had almost 5 stars and many reviews. I also guided her to go straight to Healthgrades.com to look the doctors up there, if the reviews do not show up on HCBB to click on and read. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 10:23:08', '2023-07-31 12:41:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122819018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122368002', 'Trine Bradshaw', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-07-31 10:21:52', '2023-07-31 10:21:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122816029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763142', 'Leanne Wagner', NULL, 'Member called in and made us aware that her DOB was incorrect was 1996, should be 1966.  I advised member that this info would go over to Planstin in the file nightly.  So should be update by morning.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-31 10:06:29', '2023-07-31 10:06:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063666179', 'Monique Jensen', NULL, '07.31.2023 Monique ha arthritis in hands swollen, and wants to seek medical help. I told her it is considered a pre-x cond. and she passed her 1st year waiting period, and I think is in her second. I explained what she might want to do: See a specialist (an orthopedic specializing in all musculoskeletal system), present herself as a cash-pay patient and collect all her receipts. We can then open a medical need, where Zion can share $25k towards the first year of sharing on a pre-x condition. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 09:44:44', '2023-07-31 13:38:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122816011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121185002', 'Allison Carman', NULL, 'Member requested Change of start date due to the fact that she will be having surgery for a Pre-Ex condition.  Angela to get a definite date', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-31 09:44:10', '2023-07-31 09:44:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122819003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120896002', 'Nicola Cook', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-07-31 09:43:12', '2023-07-31 09:43:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117650002', 'Paul Copeland', NULL, '07.31.2023 Susan called in an RX request for her son Davis. Jennifer caught it and found the coupon. I emailed it to Susan, as soon as the phone slowed down. I emailed the following: We are glad to find this deal for you, and I hope they are to your liking, and convenient for you, based on the zip code provided, 70820.
Below are the prices as of ​07.31.2023. 
Propranolol - 10MG - 180 Tablets supply: ​CVS $13.54     NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 09:23:55', '2023-07-31 13:51:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106720002', 'Jessica Chariton', NULL, '07.31.2023 Jessica called to get guidance on how to get covered for her son''s 2nd hpv vaccine. I explained that this is usually done prior to the appointment, however there is a work around for her, since she is already at the doctor''s office. I explained in the future, we will submit a medical need to Zion first, a preventative one, and they then will send you a prepaid CC for the vaccine, since she is already a member with a DPC.  FOr today''s visit, to go ahead and present as a cash pay patient, collect all receipts and call us back to open a medical need with Zion to get reimbursed. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 09:23:42', '2023-07-31 13:41:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122818003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079563002', 'James Lee', NULL, '07.31.23:  Was informed Jim called the office to get a quote for a plan for his daughter and asked me to call him.  Called and spoke w/Jim.  His daughter, Michaela, is age 27 and healthy, looking mainly for a catastrophic care plan.  Researched insurance plans and found they''re too expensive - asked her father to check MPB plans out.  Michaela is taking a light Rx for her OCD. In order to get the Rx, she must see her psychiatrist for 15 min. several times a year.  He asked if we have any way to help her w/her Rx. I asked how expensive it is and he said he thinks it''s $10/mo.  I told him about our MAP mental health counseling w/o Rx ability, however, we do have behavior health professionals w/CirrusMD but I wasn''t sure if they would be able to order an Rx for her.  It would be something she''d have to pay out-of-pocket for.  Jim said he''d talk to her about the Care + & Direct plans and get back with me.  
Also, Jim said he and his wife were away on vacation, then Jim''s mother passed away, so he didn''t have a chance to do the video but he will do it.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-07-31 09:05:17', '2023-07-31 09:21:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078817002', 'Matthew Amelino', NULL, '07.31.2023 Matthew called to learn the best way to maneuver his doctor''s appointments, after injuring his left ankle. He plans to see urgent care first, then hopefully an Orthopedic.
I guided Matthew to present himself as a cash pay patient, perhaps even requesting the discount for that and to collect his receipts, should this situation extend into further services for healing. I also explained, should that happen, Matthew is to call us back here at the CC line, to guide him towards the next steps of opening a medical need. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-31 08:25:00', '2023-07-31 08:25:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122816003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122803002', 'Peter Fenwick', NULL, 'Member &amp; Fam 2500 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-31 07:51:25', '2023-07-31 07:51:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122813008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121443010', 'Brandon Allen', NULL, '7/31/23 - Emily called in requesting a Welcome Call scheduler. I sent her one via email to the address on file to which she confirmed was correct. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-07-31 07:16:21', '2023-07-31 07:16:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098254002', 'Angela McGuire', NULL, '07.28.2023 Angela called to attain a list of Mammography places in her area via PHCS. I explained the option to also be able to use the RBP approach. While we were perusing the MultiPlan link together, it was not working for her. I told her I will download the list and forward it to her with the link to try again later.

She emailed back saying the the providers on the list of 32 that I sent her are not a match for her/not accessible to her, and was wondering if I gathered anymore information on why the link was not working for her. 
I sent her another email with additional options:
- Check what browser you are using: Chrome seems to work best.  Mac products may be super popular, however, links from our database platforms struggle on their systems.
- I attached another list with a widened range from your zip code = 84 results
- Searching from a different site - Healthcare BlueBook (Below are the instructions)
This one will not search for the PHCS network or any network. It is more a search on fair pricing and high-quality service of all the doctors/facilities/hospitals in your area regarding the specialty you searched for. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-28 15:41:30', '2023-07-28 15:41:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080613002', 'Michael Van Horn', NULL, '07.28.2023 Michael called to refresh his memory on how to submit bills to Zion. He has a number of bills regarding cardiology treatments and more.
I let him know that the process has temporarily changed, and that we will walk him through what he should expect from this process, and how to proceed. I went over the glitches of the system, what number to dial and extension, his IUA fulfillment and 6 month deadline. I told him to call us is he hits "speed bump". I transferred Michael to Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-28 15:04:22', '2023-07-28 15:04:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799116', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521119', 'Kallie Carpenter', NULL, '07.28.2023 Kallie called concerned about an anesthesiologist''s bill that Planstin did not cover, saying that it needs to be in network. HOWEVER we went through the entire process of shifting members'' accounts from the regular binding PHCS accounts to the new work around RBP price model. Members called concerned about their accounts being cancelled, since that is how the accounts showed up to them. It was even explained that the reason for that is due to the necessity of splitting the insurance from the rest of the billing. 
All that happened 5/31 & 6/1, making the RPB effective June 1st. This should have been covered  at least through through the RBP price model.
I told Kallie that we would need to get in touch with Jen, our supervisor, on Monday and get more guidance on this and call her back. Kallie was kind and patient.
I messaged myself via teams as a reminder. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-28 14:55:03', '2023-07-28 16:43:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799105', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082153001', 'Raluca Socander', NULL, '7-28-2023:  Raluca called.  Her PT is coming and she wants to sub a med need.  NOT A NICE PERSON!!!
     - First she couldn''t hear me, so she hung up then called back.
     - Second time, she could hear me but said barely, so I tried to speak loudly to help.  She didn''t want to hear the instructions I had when I asked if she has a piece of paper for notes.  She told me no, I''m on the computer, just tell me.  I told her they just chg''d their process & doing it directly on the website hasn''t been working, so I wanted to give her instructions on who to call, etc.  It made her angry there were other people she would have to call & then she accused me of having a bad day & yelling at her & hung up on me again.
     - I called her back to let her know I''d love to help her.  She again accused me of horrible customer service, being in a hurry because it''s Friday & I''m about to go home (although, I have hours left so don''t know where this came from).  She will call back when Jennifer is available on Monday.  Again, she was NOT NICE.  I''ve had a great day & tons of thank yous from other memb for helping them today.  This just felt so completely off.  I do not know where the conversation went wrong.  She hung up on me a third time.     - CA

Raluca called back asking to speak to someone else.  I let her know, at this time it''s just me:  Jennifer is out sick, Nahla''s at lunch, and there are just the three of us.  She seemed to hear me re: her assumptions and maybe realized she was accusing me inaccurately?  So:
     - This time she allowed me to walk her thru the curr process for sub a ''med need'' w/Zion & actually took the instructions.  At the end of the call I trans her to Zion and she seemed to be in a much better place.
     Hopefully, she''s better.  I am having trouble w/my throat today & maybe that''s what she heard as speaking is difficult off and on.  Maybe she was projection her bad space, blaming me, & really it was how she''s feeling.  I don''t know.  I''ll notify Jennifer too.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-28 14:19:55', '2023-07-28 14:35:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122774067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110261002', 'Lance Casey', NULL, 'On 7/20 I received a phone call from this member who had talked to Planstin around scheduling a colonoscopy and was told by them that the preventative portion of the plan was added 5/23 and that he would not be eligible until 11/23.  Member has had and been paying for the Direct membership since his 1/1/23 enrollment.  Planstin to fix.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-28 13:14:37', '2023-07-28 13:14:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122802003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610440', 'Kreston Rohrig', NULL, '7-28-23 Kreston called to understand why his wellness visit is getting rejected. He will go back and check where it got submitted or who he talked to. I let him know that goes through Planstin and it must be coded as wellness not diagnostic. They might need to re-code and resubmit it. I also gave him the MPB Concierge Team #. He will work on it. He''s also super tired of the western medicine and insurance non-sense that we all have to deal with. He was very nice and appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-28 12:40:15', '2023-07-28 12:40:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108294010', 'Christopher Kelly', NULL, '07.28.2023 Chris called to better understand how to maneuver a physical preventative appointment with Planstin. I coached him on 4 items:
1-It''s easiest if the provider is in the PHCS Network, so ask or we can search for them
2-IF NOT, the work around is connecting the doctor''s office with Planstin with the infor from the back of the card so they can collaborate billing and pricing.
3-Maintain the appointment as preventative
4-IF rx requests are imperative or any bloodwork outside of the std lipid panel, then ask them to separate those from the rest of the appointment, and request the cash pay discount on the lab work, or call us for further guidance on discounted lab tests. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-28 12:05:02', '2023-07-28 12:05:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026447189', 'David Naber', NULL, '7-28-2023:  Rebecca called again.                 [Henrietta will be going in the 3rd grade.]
     - Dyslexia:  Med Diag finally came thru.  This often leads to secondary issues:
     - ADHD:  Often linked to the dyslexia.
     - Play therapist: 2022 - 2023  They hadn''t had the full diagnosis yet.  Started here due to her daughter orig being in 2nd gr.  Often, people w/dyslexia have issues due to the issues that come w/this disorder (diff focusing, being anxious, not knowing how to work/play/interact w/others, etc.  They started here and got her a psychiatrist.
     - Psychiatrist: This is helping, her husb thought ''Life Care'' would help pay for this.  She''s going to nominate thier doc, but knows it is a longshot.  [See ''MAP'' info below.]
     - Anxiety: Often linked to the dyslexia.  Started seeing pshychiatrist in part due to this?
     - OT - Occupational Therapy:  After play therapy was not have enough impact, they went to OT and are seeing great results.  Orig, her husb thought ''Life Care'' would help with this.  I told here I thought this was outside that scope, but made sure she knows how to ck w/Mazz & Sull.
     - MAP: Her husb did not understand that the ''Life Care'' doesn''t just pay/reimb for any health/mental care.  So, we went to the MAP site together & went over everything.  This way she can try to nominate their counselor (Psychiatrist).  I let her know they will call & invite the doctor, but not to plan on successs as I''d only seen it work a time or two.  Yet, she will have at least exhausted this option.  Either way, she liked they info they have re: ADHD, etc. & was thrilled to know this is available.  Reminded her they are back east, so to us here in CO their hours feel early.  She''ll make sure to call during their normal opp hours.
     - Zion: We decided, due to Henrietta being a minor, to see if Zion can offer an help.  We discussed the 6mos deadline, but she hasn''t really known what all this was until recently when the full report came thru.  She''ll attach a timeline as they''ve learned the extent and finally gotten a "MEDICAL Diagnosis".  Yet, understands there may be no help, and with the time passed, they may not be willing to look at things past 6 mos ago.  But, at least she will have tried.
     - Spec school part time to learn how to handle the dyslexia.  (I think she said 21k/yr)
     - Trad "Ins" option: Her timing is good.  She may need to look at "trad ins" for Henrietta.  I encouraged her to call her advisor Wendy Scipione if Zion & MAP do not have much help.  I let her know Wendy is experienced w/"trad ins" as well & might be able to guide her.  In the past I''ve see families break-off a member from their MPB.Health membership for more trad help.  But, leave everyone else on our prog = less expensive.  We discussed that ''Open Enrollment'' is coming, so they can get answers, then look at this route w/Wendy if necessary.
[We talked about the possibility of seeing if somehow Henrietta would qualify for the state Medicaid program, due to the utter expenses.  She''ll keep that in mind for down the road as well.  She went over some of the expenses & I think it was >40k in the last year!!!]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-28 11:58:46', '2023-07-28 13:16:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122774062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122777002', 'Paul Vinciguerra', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-28 11:19:49', '2023-07-28 11:19:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122769048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012051083', 'Nancy Gentry', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Put in request to Kelly to resend out QR Life code cards to the 2 children Zack and Amelie. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-07-28 11:12:16', '2023-07-28 11:12:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065297505', 'Daniel Birkhead', 'Perm to Discuss Rec''d 7/28/23: Mary Grace (Gardner) = David''s mother', '7-28-2023:  Mary Grace and I spoke.  Since she has not dealt w/healthsharing or MPB.Health in the past, we started w/education, diff vocabulary & why that''s important, how the 1k IUA works, how he needs to present himself, etc.  [NOTE:  Care+ member]
     - ''Perm to Disc'' signed form now on file - I asked her to remind us they sub the form as we are trying to bring in more help & the notice will not be as easy to see soon (esp for new people).
     - Daniel was born w/cleft lip & pallet:  Top jaw has not grown to match bottom jaw.  With this/these issues, he curr went back to the surg  he''s known before.  He''s had a long stretch with no issues & she thinks it''s far before the 24-mos lookback period for pre-x.  This surgeon has them starting w/an orthodontist to prepare his teeth for surgery to make the jaws match.  We talked about med vs dental, but she thinks this will all fall under medical (it has, with effort, in the past).
          She''s aware of the challenges, but we both agree she should at least try.  To show this is part of the medically necessary jaw reconstruction, she''s going to do a cov letter when she starts the Zion ''med need'' w/an explanation of plan, etc.  This may help if they know the orthodontic is necessary for the surgery & at least she will have tried.
     - Pre-x:  Doesn''t sound like it.  He hasn''t had any issues w/this for years and it''s just now coming back into his life.  But, in case, we disc the phase-in period.  (ie: curr yr three = 50k sharing w/approved ''med need'', yr four starts 4/1/2024)  At least he''s already into yr three & w/surgery out 8 mos, may be able to wait until yr 4 for the 125k if necessary.
     - Surgion: sent them to work w/orthodontist to get the teeth into position for the surgery they expect in about 8 months.
     - Zion:  Part of the educ we went over is how MPB.Health is a pkg of prods w/diff comp providing diff portions of the healthcare.  She understand that although we got her set up w/perm to disc Daniel''s records here, Zion (being a diff comp) will need them to repeat the process - she totally understands.
        We walked thru the new Zion Med Needs submission process.  She knows who to call, what to ask for, and what to expect.  She seems very experienced at dealing w/things like this, so I think working w/her should go well.

Mary Grace called back.  It sounds like the glitches are being worked out on the Zion Memb Portal & you can at least access the ''sub a med need'' page now - except it keeps timins out on her every few minutes.  We decided she''s going to prepare everything before trying touse the site:  cover letter, all pdf receipts, inv, etc, then will try to finish it before it times out on her.  She''ll call if she continues to have issues.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-28 11:07:46', '2023-07-28 14:11:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122799011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065297505', 'Daniel Birkhead', NULL, '7-28-2023:  Cut & paste from Kelly F regarding call during morning hours while she was covering:
[10:04 AM] Kelly Frederickson
Hey there guys! I have a question about a member who will also need to be called back once the form is submitted and approved. Well the mother of the member will be called back. I have her name and number. so the situation is, member Daniel Birkhead called with his mother there as well. Asking what he needs to do to get his mother confirmed to be the one to ask questions and talk to us for him. My mom Patti, said there is a Cognito Form for them to fill out called  Permission to Discuss the MPB.Health Membership Plan. I emailed it to them and they wanted to stay on the phone while they filled it out right there and then be able to talk. I unfortunately said no because I have no idea what the process is, who approves the form if at all, etc. I have never had to do this or ever heard or be asked this stuff before. I told them to just fill it our, submit it, and the mother Mary Grace gave me her phone number and I said someone will call her back after they submit the form. Her number is 615-506-4419. 

[10:32 AM] Kelly Frederickson
So if someone could call Mary Grace back at the number of 615-506-4419 that would be great! It is the mother for member Daniel Birkhead, they submitted the permission to discuss mpb plan membership form so she can speak instead of him. He wants her to be the one. Thank you! It''s ok Cari I totally get it. It was back to back calls for me too', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-28 11:07:16', '2023-07-28 11:07:16'),
