  ('zcrm_1579374000122649032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108616009', 'Kevin Kakos', NULL, '7-26-2023:  Analisa called to find out 
     1) how does Kevin add his wife to his memb (she''s losing her employer prov "ins".  -- told Analisa to have the memb call me today & I''d walk him/her thru the form.  Time sensitive due to:
     2) Can we get an exception for an 8/1/23 eff date. -- let Analisa know in Monday''s Advisor meeting, the specifically said to req an exception: e-mail JK & Patti w/the req AND sub a tckt.  That they would try, but the later in the month the harder.  So Patti or JK would have the final word on this.

Kevin & his wife called in almost immed after I finished w/Analisa:
     - I got them to the form & made sure they knew how to fill it out properly so that there are no issues IF an exception to the eff date is made.  Did let them know Analisa is trying, but we are past the deadline, so the corp off will have final dec.
     - We did discuss pre-x = his wife asked about a mole she had rem''d.  We talked about maint derm not cov''d.  IF it was cancerous & that particular mole came back it would be subject to the pre-x 1 yr waiting period, then phase-in proc & I gave them 2nd yr: 25k, 3rd yr: 50k, 4th & bey: 125k, but that''s only on this pre-x item.  Told them anything in her records in the 24 mos prior to memb could be subject to this rule (gave knee & Ibuprofen example).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-26 18:15:12', '2023-07-26 18:15:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122649027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109743011', 'Jared Fisher', NULL, '7-26-2023:  Jen called.  She was having issues w/how to sub a ''med need'' because the instructions were from before Zion''s new process.  We went over a lot:
     - IUA:  Jen did not understand IUAs.  In fact, she thought they were just like a ''ded'', so we went over in depth how the 1k IUA is issue specific, 3 per rolling 12 mos period, 4th & beyond in the 12 mos rolling period >$500 IUA waived, etc.
     - Her daughter''s finger & the Urg Care Clinic visit was $163.  She thinks this issue is complete, so we disc option of doing nothing, 6mos deadline just in case, etc.  Her daughter is a gymnast, but it''s not for money (she''s not professional).  She will think it over & call us if she has further questions.  We went over the curr process w/Zion''s new website, but maybe if she decides in a few months to sub this ''med need'', they will have fixed things?
     - ''Prev Care'':  We talked about total opposite ways of presenting dep on the component.  Did a quick Planstin ''prev care'':  only time you say Y to "ins"; only time you present an ID Card (Planstin card); in ntwk/out of ntwk = both fine as long as doc will bill Planstin directly for you because there''s NO reimb on ''prev care''.
     - Healthshare = illness/accidents/', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-26 17:14:51', '2023-07-27 10:19:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122614069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000024844131', 'Adam Nolan', NULL, '7-26-23 Patti and John granted Adam an Aug. 1st start date and I just notified him. They will refund him the $100 once the payment goes through. Yay!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-26 17:10:18', '2023-07-26 17:10:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122647086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079147335', 'Stacia Montenegro', NULL, '07.26.2023 Stacia and Angel have not had their Welcome Call to better understand how their plan works. 
