  ('zcrm_1579374000122614049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123819010', 'Peter Mueller', NULL, '7-26-23 Cindy Suplizio found me through Deb or Sarah Bergstrom!  Cindy is in Carbondale now and last time I saw her was while on slopes shooting a race. :-) Cindy''s husband Peter needs benefits starting ASAP but can do Cobra for the month of Aug. Taggart needs benefits for the year while he''s teaching at the World Academy for Kayaking! He''s paid as a 1099 but will be fine with CARE+ since he''s young and wellness visit should be less than cost difference for his screening. Peter did all of his screenings already since he knew his benefits were ending. Neither have any pre-x, no tobacco and super healthy, athletic, etc. CARE+ is $215/$1000 for Taggart and $265/$1000 for Peter.  Cindy will share this with them and they will reach out to me directly to enroll for Sept. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-26 14:58:37', '2023-07-26 14:58:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122647046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011659075', 'Snatam Khalsa', NULL, '07.26.2023 Snatam called to get reimbursed for having her daughter see natural path out of NH for a  physical exam. I explained to her that is usually done through Zion, given it is an alternative doctor, and Zion would need to have the need in prior to the visit for approval. However, I told her to let me double check with my co-worker to see if there are other options.
I consulted with Cari via teams, and Cari had already seen that I was on GoTo with Snatam, and understands some of the struggles poor Snatam goes through understanding the plan she has. 
Cari shared that Charlie, her advisor, put in a ticket for her, wanting to get reimbursed for items that are not reimbursable. 
I explained that getting reimbursed after the fact by Planstin, let along for a natural path doctor is not a successful journey at this point. 
She then proceeded to want to understand how to present herself at her another doctor''s office, who is located in reputable hospital. I coached her through the steps of presenting her Planstin card, and reiterating the importance of making sure it stays preventative. I told her she has two options to go about getting covered: 1- Make sure the facility/provider is in the PHCS network, 2-IF NOT, have them to contact Planstin directly from the back of the card to collaborate pricing and  billing. She proceeded to say that she does not want them to know she has insurance, b/c she wants to apply as a cash pay patient to receive the 25% discount. I told her she does not have to worry about the discount, as it is covered 100% with Planstin whether she goes about it the PHCS network or the RBP route.
Snatam continued to add to the story saying she does not want them to know she has insurance at all b/c then she would not be approved for the 25% off discount. At that point (after going through the process a few times before getting to the above), I recommended that she speak directly to Planstin to discuss exceptions to the rules of ONLY CORRESPONDING WITH PROVIDERS and perhaps correspond with her instead to not have the hospital have direct connections with Planstin.
She kept asking how do others go about this matter, it seems very cumbersome, and I told her they don''t do what you are doing, they usually JUST use their planstin card.
The call ended 39 minutes later, and with me giving her Planstin''s number, b/c she could not locate off the back of the card. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-26 14:28:19', '2023-07-26 16:17:23'),
