Thank you,
Karen Peirson


7-24-23 Hi Karen,

OK, I just submitted this to their Escalations Team, my direct contact and through their Extra Help online tool. I assume you submitted the bill through the Redirect App already, right?  If not, that''s a must. If so, hold tight and we''ll see if I get a response. If all of these methods fail, I''ll send it to the very top. But, I have to try these avenues first.

Thanks,

Wendy Scipione', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-24 11:54:09', '2023-07-24 11:54:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122513026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109502001', 'David Hartman', NULL, '07.24.2023 Elizabeth called asking how if it is common for doctor''s offices to deny cash-pay patients, and I told her that has not come up for me to be a common experience, but that I spoke to another member around 1.5 months ago saying the same thing. 
They are moving to a more rural area, and want to make sure they can lock down the physicians needed in their new area. I guided her to HCBB, she finally was able to log in properly, she searched for providers/specialists and procedures and was glad to be able to peruse the site solely for a while. She did as about prescriptions would be covered, and I got to consult Jen and Cari via teams. Both shared that sharing the arthritis meds could be in a grey area with Zion, due layers of approvals. I explained that to Elizabeth and read straight from Zion''s guidelines AS OF 07.24.2023 from their site, and named a few meds that MIGHT be shareable. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-24 11:52:59', '2023-07-24 11:52:59'),
