  ('zcrm_1579374000122474006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064767140', 'John Parks', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3177 Question : It said I had a missed chat, but I was on the chat the entire time and no one responded. Can you please advise?', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-07-23 05:46:57', '2023-07-23 05:46:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122467004', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064767140', 'John Parks', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3176 Question : I am looking for a referral to a physician for shoulder pain and possibly a strained or torn muscle. I had a consultation with the telehealth medicine doctor, and he recommended that I go in for tests to see what the issue is.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-07-23 05:37:56', '2023-07-23 05:37:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122434036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120816002', 'Michael Lam', NULL, '07.21.2023 Samantha called to inquire about a diabetes rx iand if they need a specialist or pcp to get a refill. I recommended they start at CirrusMD as the first 1st step. Samantha already has HSA and wants to link it to MPB. I advised her to speak to her HSA accountant/financial institution. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-21 14:53:46', '2023-07-21 14:53:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122434031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106693002', 'William Spiccia', NULL, '07.21.2023 William Spiccia called to address the following:
1- Unfinished charges/billing (like Laura Hunt) - Will be addressed by JK early next week
2- Referral program - Will be addressed by Julia on Monday
3- Lead (Sean &amp;Sally Conroy family wanting to sign up) - Will be addressed by Julia on Monday. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-21 14:45:42', '2023-07-21 15:08:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122455018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022809040', 'Pamela Finch', NULL, '7-21-2023:  Pam called.  She''s trying to fix the issue she was working w/Jennifer last week.  From what she describes, it''s a billing dept issue.  They pulled her Planstin ''prev care'' only ins months after she pd cash, chg''d the billing codes, and now want to backbill her the extra $.  We looked at who you can report medical billing issues to in MN & talked about creating a bullet point timeline.  She''s waiting for the ''Team Leader'' of the billing dept to call her.  She may call for more advice if they still refuse to hear her.  She has an amazing background for this, so she seems to know what she''s doing.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-21 14:20:00', '2023-07-21 17:55:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122448038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122615027', 'Sean Conroy', NULL, '7-21-23 I spoke with Sally 49 and her husband Sean is 50. They have two kids 20 and 22. Their current insurance runs out Aug. 27th which is just a short-term plan.  They are both self employed. If they paid for traditional ins it will cost them $30K a year! They haven''t used their ins in years and they just do self-pay. They have a $5K ded and never reach it. They chose SECURE $2500/$765 $125/$25 but the $25 is not showing.  Sean also did his colonoscopy this year but Sally hasn''t done hers. Since they have a family they chose to include wellness and HSA compliance. 

They also joined HMA 10000. I was on phone while he completed both. They are all set except he didn''t include SS for each family member.

Update - I called Sean back to get the SS #''s for each family member. Patti got them.  Also they were referred by Joseph Spiccia and that is Leo''s client and Leo''s no longer with MPB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-21 14:00:34', '2023-07-21 17:40:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122455013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108424017', 'Jennifer Eisenberg', NULL, '7-21-2023:  Jennifer called - their son arrived yesterday: 7/20/2023  Sage.  Jennifer was snippy with me at first because she''s dealing w/a new baby and toddler & why can''t I just do it over the phone.  She wasn''t really working w/me, so I let her know it requires she sign a legal document, but it''s super easy and fast.  Then we started working together, got her the instructions, and we even had me saying hello to the toddler.  She knows there is a 30-day deadline.
     - Baby ''Wellness Visit" is tomorrow.  She knows to present her Planstin card & to make sure they will bill for her (in or out of ntwk).  Jennifer & I tried to determine if this is a ''prev care'' item & I found the following in the gvmt link: 
     - How often do I need to take my baby for well-baby visits?
       Babies need to see the doctor or nurse 6 times before their first birthday. Your baby is growing and changing quickly, so regular visits are important.
       The first well-baby visit is 2 to 3 days after coming home from the hospital, when the baby is about 3 to 5 days old.  [=Looks like this sb part of the prov prev care?]
       After that first visit, babies need to see the doctor or nurse when they’re:
               1 month old
               2 months old
               4 months old
               6 months old
