  ('zcrm_1579374000122229003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082047009', 'Marianne Leman', NULL, '7-19-2023:  Leslie called quite upset.  He says we told him to go have their annual visits and now we''ve declined to pay it.  Why is he paying 6k a year for something that refuses to pay.  After talking, here is the situation:
     - Orig they started on the Secure plan.  Karen told them they should go ahead & get their annual appts.  BUT, Alison Carey just had them talk to Planstin, rather than going thru all the caution items herself & they had $800+ in lab work that of course was not paid for.  All of this is back in June 2022 (& he''s just getting the Planstin notice of those labs being put twds his 6k ded).  We went over how that ded is something set to qual them for their HSA, but since Planstin is only ''prev care'', they generally only have the 1k IUA.
     - Lab work:  they live in NY, where disc labs are not permitted.  Therefore, I told him IF they need labs again for preventative, we can see if they are within driving distance of another state''s disc lab & gave examples of some recent savings.
     - Care+ = the plan they moved to eff 10/1/2022.  He asked why have it, so we discussed it''s a catastrophic/illness/accident type plan with NO prev care.  I gave examples of how this works & why it truly protects you financially.  
     We decided he is going to tt his advisor Karen Torsoe (who I believe is in Norway right now, but he was okay with connecting w/her when they can) because she''s the one that told them to go & now it''s not paid.
     I read thru some of the notes & Leslie decided he is going to tt Marianne since she''s the one that''s been taking care of all this.  Plus, they will tt Karen Torsoe as well.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-19 11:12:44', '2023-07-19 11:19:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122222013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108053001', 'Chris Pilgrim', 'SENT New Welcome Call Scheduling Link 7.19.2023', '07.19.2023 Chris called to get his member ID number. I thought he was talking about MPB member ID number, so I went into Admin123 and pulled that up. He asked is this all I give the doctor when I''m making a wellness appointment? I said No, you need to provide them with the information from the back of the Planstin card. He did not have that card on hand, so I guided him to access his email on this profile, and search for Planstin, to attain the virtual card that they send to new members.
I was in the middle of providing him guidance on how to present himself and what guidelines to maintain but we got disconnected. I could not hear him anymore. 
