  ('zcrm_1579374000122123018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, '7-18-2023:  Martin called.  They''ve been presenting their Planstin card for visits to the babies doc thinking it was ''prev care''.  After talking, it sounds like it''s probably part of the babies ''med need'' from being in the NICU.
     - Baby ''prev care'':  Took Martin to the heathcare.gov site & showed him what the gvmt lists as ''prev care''.  Let him know, if he sees something here & needs clarification, Planstin can do that for him.
     - vs NICU follow-up visits:  When we talked, it sounds like the weekly visits were more a part of the baby''s ''med need'' following birth.  First NICU, then weekly doc visits for monitoring the baby.  Martin says they have been working w/Rachel at Zion for the baby''s ''med need''.  I made sure they have Zion''s # & trans him there so he can tt Rachel.  I think this will just be continued expenses on the baby''s ''med need''.  If he finds out that''s incorrect, he will call us back.
     - Martin has an extremely strong accent, so this may be even more confusing than normal.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-18 12:34:11', '2023-07-18 12:48:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122115038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109799008', 'Reginald Ashby', NULL, '07.18.2023 Reginald called trying to get Karen his spouse access to CirrusMD. Both seemed on edge and snippy. I allowed them space to sort this CirrusMD ordeal out, in hopes that their demeanor would soften.
I registered Karen, and she received the link no problem and completed her  set up. I asked if Reginald is able to access his account and he said yes no problem. They wanted to link their accounts and I was not sure what they were talking about. I consulted Cari via teams and she said for legality purposes, they cannot link their accounts. I relayed that information to both Karen and Reginald and they understood. They seemed more relaxed at the end of the call, and both agreed that they are all set up and ready to use CirrusMD, when needed. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-18 12:04:08', '2023-07-18 12:04:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122085093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098470001', 'Jen Coggin', 'New Plan eff 8/1/23', 'Member &amp; Fam $5000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-18 11:52:53', '2023-07-18 11:52:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122123013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108734002', 'Amy Winsand', NULL, '7-18-2023:  Amy called w/lots of questions.  NOTE: Direct Memb
     - Immunizations:  Her DPC does not offer them & she wondered if they are covered by her ''prev care''.  I let her know adult immunizations are not part of the Direct plan.
     - Annual Derm Appt:  She asked if the $175 office visit would work for this appt.  We went over how it will only cover the office visit itself, nothing else (ie: no tests, etc).  She seemed fine w/that.  If she decides to use it for this, she will either get an estimate (so she can get the pre-pd cc for this ''prev care'' appt) or will call us afterwards so we can show her how to sub it as a ''prev care visit'' reimb.
     - Mamm:  Amy and I discussed getting her mamm on this Direct plan.  She will again either get an estimate so she can get the money together (and pre-req a ''prev care mamm med need'') or pre-pay & call us to sub afterwards.
     - We went to Zion''s curr Memb Guidelines & read the details on the above items so it''s in their words.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-18 11:51:33', '2023-07-18 13:36:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122085088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098470001', 'Jen Coggin', NULL, 'Member had submitted Chage form to add spouse &amp; children and it was overlooked.  I will process for 8/1.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-18 11:50:46', '2023-07-18 11:50:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122126028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122131012', 'Qiuyi Lin Wright', NULL, '7-18-23 Qiuyi has Anthem BC/BS AZ with her husbands employer through the University, I think she said. Their coverage looks really good actually. The ded is $1500 per indiv/$3000 per family and mop is $3500 Indiv/$7K per family. His employer is paying a portion and she didn''t know what they are paying. She was thinking of using MCS as secondary but it''s probably not worth the money since they have low ded and mop. I recommended leaving it alone. She doesn''t want or need dental. She does want to expore life ins which we began the process.  I quoted her for $250K which is $40 for standard non-tobacco and $500K at $75 and Hope Ins will pay up to $25 stipend. She wants a 30 Yr Term. Her income is $75K and household income is $180K. They are going to pay off their car loan of $6K this week and $10K student loan they''ll pay of very soon. That leaves a $110K mortgage. They should really have a $750K-$1M policy but we''ll start where they are comfortable to fund moving forward.  I sent her two policies to review and she''s in training right now and doens''t know her schedule. She''ll let me know when she''s ready.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-18 11:46:13', '2023-07-18 11:46:13'),
