  ('zcrm_1579374000122085013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110260002', 'William Burg Jr', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to remove spouse &amp; children from membership as they have separated.  I clarified with member that he wanted to stay with the Secure membership.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-18 07:23:09', '2023-07-18 07:23:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122085003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121976011', 'Robin Kruel', NULL, 'Member submitted Payment information after picking "List Bill" option when enrolling.  I will charge the Enrollment &amp; set up for Monthly billing.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-18 07:01:58', '2023-07-18 07:01:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104655002', 'Melissa Hernandez', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Diane Border & Melissa Hernandez called in together.  Melissa has a ''prev care'' appt for her daughter tomorrow.  She gave them her Planstin card & Planstin told the doc''s office the member is inactive.
     - Sent Patti a concierge Teams chat (so everyone knows the answer in case Melissa calls in before I''m on shift), asking her to please straighten out Planstin.  The Admin123 file shows everything is pd up & all is fine.  We''ve had a multitide of issues w/both Zion & Planstin claiming our members are inactive lately.
        Melissa asked that we notify her when things are corrected: 520-342-9952.  Diane Border is fine with notifying Melissa if that helps out as well.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 18:12:27', '2023-07-17 18:13:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122214002', 'Tara Skredynski', NULL, '7-17-23 Tara is 46 and her son is on her x''s plan. She was on Friday Health and then got onto Medicaid as of Jan. 2023. But, she will be kicked off Medicaid for Aug. 1st. She lives  a super healthy lifestyle. She does have a pre-x since she was 16. She takes a med to maintain healthy levels prolactin levels. She had a growth on her pituitary gland at age 16 and now simply takes the med to avoid too much prolactin. She does her annual wellness visit. She also gets some additional blood tests done to test her prolactin levels. I explained to her that this will not be included in the wellness visit labs, ie. she will need to pay for these on her own. I recommended she calls the MPB Concierge Team when she needs to do these for the best price. She understood.  She used to see an endocrinologist but no longer needs to do so either.  She''s earning about $75K in 2023. I discussed SECURE $1000/$300 and $125/$25.  She wants an Aug. 1st start date. I''m sending her the video and written overview now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 17:38:48', '2023-07-17 17:38:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122049024', 'Brent Kruel', NULL, '7-17-23 Brent has updated the payment form and should be all set. He wants to add employees down the road and part-time employees. PT will pay for themselves.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 17:28:05', '2023-07-17 17:28:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, '7/17/2023:  Bryan e-mailed later on Friday.  I ret''d his call Mon:
     - Sue has another new extremely expensive drug she wants to try for her alopecia:  Dupixent.
        Reid can source, but it''s still outrageous:  
               - Dupixent 300mg "pre-filled pen", 300 mg.  Once every two weeks.  Would probably get 3 doses to start to see how it is tolerated."  
                  Reid''s resp:  "can source this, but it is over $3000 for a 1 month supply."
               - Online coupons =

ILM letting Bryan know I was calling per his req; the quote I rec''d from our international shopper; & to please call me on my office line.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 17:01:30', '2023-07-17 18:15:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122133002', 'Paul Szotek', NULL, '7-17-23 Dr. Paul is 47 and wife is 45, kids 15 and 17. He wants SECURE to be able to fund an HSA. His goal is to pay for his current DPC Little Village Pediatrics for his kids out of the HSA. I need to look into that.  He also has a very small practice with only 3 employees, 1 of which is his wife. So, they won''t have a group of 3+. I let him know it''s fine and only difference is in how he''s billed. The only health issue is one son has ADHD as controlled substance which is about $300. But, his son hasn''t used it all summer and is probably fine without using it ever again. So, he''s not terribly concerned about it. But, he can at least pay for it from the HSA if need be. He and His wife do plan to get their colonoscopies some time down the road, not any time soon. Wife gets mammo and typical wellness. I will send him video to review again and written email. We will reconnect on Tuesday to enroll assuming his procedures don''t go extra long. He''ll call or text if he runs into any problems.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 16:44:03', '2023-07-17 16:44:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010870127', 'Heather Braeutigam', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Heather called.  She wanted to conf how to handle ''prev care'' colonoscopy.  We disc everything.  How to present for ''prev care'' only = "ins" = Y; only time you will ever present your Planstin ID card;  all prov must bill Planstin directly = no reimb on ''prev care''.  Make sure to keep any ''prev care'' appts w/in ''prev care'' for proper billing.
     She has her ID card &amp; will make sure they''ll bill.

Note:  her Admin123 files are on the old side of records (green).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 16:32:10', '2023-07-17 16:45:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122049024', 'Brent Kruel', NULL, '7-17-23 Left vm for Brent to complete payment form that I sent via email to they don''t miss the deadline.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 16:18:59', '2023-07-17 16:18:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108522002', 'Michael Hulstrom', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Karen called:
     - ''prev care'', ntwk still?:  as of 7/1/2023 no ntwk req''d, but can still use PHCS if desired.  No diff on included ''prev care''.  Just make sure to conf doc will bill for you.  No reimb on ''prev care''.  Went over how to present.  ''Prev Care'' only:  "ins" = Y; only time you will ever present an ID card = Planstin card.  Keep all ''prev care'' to keep med billing ''prev'' & pd for.
         colonoscopy & mamm:  Doc mentioned these.  We went over making sure all prov included (facility, doc, & anesthesiologist; imaging prov & reading prov) will bill for you.  Went over what happens on colonoscopy IF polyps pulled.  IF = diagnostic & now 1k IUA, must start ''med need'', so she can call us for guidance should that happen.
     - billing:  She thought her billing was off.  I checked Admin123 & it looks fine.  Took her into her MPB.Health Memb Port to see the pymts & she agreed, looks good for now.  She know next draw date is 20th & will show sometime after that.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 16:18:51', '2023-07-17 16:52:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109364009', 'Nina Martinek', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Fell skiing in Feb 2023 - It''s due to an accident, not a pre-x condition.  
     - Yr waiting period?  She was super worried that she had no help on this for 1 year.  But, after talking w/her, I do not see any reason she wouldn''t.  I''m not sure where the 1yr waiting period came into her conversation, but it sounds like she should be fine since she''s never had issues w/this issue before.
     - Zion is having even more issues w/their new ''med need'' sub process.  It will not allow her to set up her Zion Memb Portal at all.  Zion then gave her an e-mail address w/instructions on how to sub the need & get everything going.  We discussed the entire process.
     - I encouraged her to submit all expenses she''s had on this issue since everything is < 6mos old.  However, she knows they may not include the chiropractic expenses twds her IUA since alt medicine req''s prior approval (but, worth a try.  Would help twds her 2500 IUA...).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 15:25:50', '2023-07-17 15:47:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108056002', 'George League', NULL, '7-17-2023:  George called in.  Said when he purchased the plan, his advisor (Tupac) told him we could tell him where to go to get cheap colonoscopy.  He wasn''t at a computer, so I sent him a list of the only 3 gastroenterology practices that are hightest quality and fair price on a colonoscopy.  There are 4 docs listed, but when I ck''d their rating on colonoscopies, the first doc was worst quality care for that particular procedure.  Therefore, I did not send that name to him.  I also gave him avg price for his area (& the range to expect).  Did not go into negotiation w/this info as he seemed overwhelmed already & was just sitting in his vehicle.
     - 5k IUA - we did not go over what happens if they pull a polyp & this becomes diagnostic.  It could go over the 5k if they are pulling polyps, but he''s super early in the process.  He plans to call & ask if we can see how the facility his doc recommends is rated for colonoscopies.  We found one hospital listed as worst quality in the Huntsville, AL area, so hopefully, they will recommend somewhere else.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 15:16:48', '2023-07-17 15:20:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122040038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109364009', 'Nina Martinek', NULL, '07.17.2023 Nina called to learn how to get coverage for a torn ACL. I explained that this would go through medical cost sharing part of her plan. Due to the glitch with Zion''s medical need application, I went through what she would expect as a turn around from Zion, until they fix the glitch. Nina understood the process by repeating it, and was happy to move forward to speaking to Zion. I direct transferred her to them. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-17 15:15:39', '2023-07-17 15:15:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121975002', 'Lynn O''Malley', NULL, '7-14-23 Lynn is joining MCS solo and dental with her husband. She hasn''t done her wellness visit in a while but plans to. She''s no meds, no tobacco, no health issues. She actually might add her husband once she realized how much more affordable it will be. We enrolled her for now and may add her husband before the 20th. he has rosacea and slighly high blood pressure. She is 52 and enrolled in SECURE with the Hope Institute for Aug. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 14:51:24', '2023-07-17 14:52:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104633018', 'Robin Lacrimosa', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Robin called.  Tons of questions.  She''s feeling like this is too difficult & she may go to the mkt pl during open enrollment.  I let her know her advisor Diane Border, is quite good & should be able to help her make an educated decision as to what that looks like.*
     - ''Prev care'':  went over everything.  How to present, "ins"= only time you will say Y & only time you will pres an ID card = Planstin card.
     - Maint: has appt every 6 mos for medication mgmt.  She knows this is not a cov item.  IF becomes an issue, and will be > than her 1k IUA, then it would move into diagnostic/treatment for a ''med need'' & could be shared.  But maintaining a situation is not a qual ''med need''.
     - Lab: Doc ordered $300+ lab tests.  She will call ahead next time so we can go over the disc lab test procedure & hopefully bring that expense down.  This is for the maint meds.*
     - Mamm:  Dense breasts, so thinks they will want something more than the std 2D mamm.  She knows when it steps outside that norm 2D mamm, the ACA MEC does not consider paying for that.*
     - Colonoscopy:  Went over how just need to make sure all prov will bill for you (facility, doc, anesthesiologist) & what happens IF they pull a polyp.  She knows to call us for help in sub a ''med need'' & she''s will then be resp for her 1k IUA.*
     * Went over options for paying for these unincluded items:  HSA, HMA.  She does something & sees how often Medicare does not cover exp, so the HSA could help her 15 years from now, but, I''m not sure either of these spoke to her.  If she has quesitons, she knows her advisor Diane Border can help her w/looking into the HMA.  We talked about = absolutely diff options.  NOT the same.  Warned her:  HMA = a policy.  You quit paying, you lose everything you''ve put in & matched, so much be maintained until ready to quit, then strategically used & cancelled.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 14:25:13', '2023-07-17 18:26:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122050018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000119626010', 'Alicia Koscinski', 'Welcome Call Completed on 7/17/23 by JAT', 'I completed Alicia''s Welcome call but she was not happy about her experience and honesty from her advisor. She stated she was never told she had to meet 3 IUA''s in her year or that her plan does not cover ALL wellness visits. She said that Zach told her all of her and her children''s preventative care would be covered, why would she purchase this if it wasn''t? I apologized and empathized with Alicia; we finished our welcome and I asked Alicia if she''d like me to transfer her to Zach to speak with him. Alicia declined the transfer and stated that she will contact Zach directly. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-07-17 14:18:41', '2023-07-17 14:18:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Andrew called.  He orig was looking for doc''s in his 
     - Post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail = resent to him so he had access.  We walked thru how to understand healthcare.gov & if quest about extra items, call Planstin for conf.
     - Immun: we can verify qualified pharmacies if he goes thru the pharmacy for these.
     - They live in Steamboat Springs, CO during the summer mos & that''s where their PCP has been for years.  He wondered if we''d opened up to non-ntwk doc on ''prev care'' yet.  Let him know it became eff 7/1/23 & how to pursue other docs = must be willing to bill for him; only time "ins" = Y & only time you will curr prov an ID card = Planstin; doc''s off can call Planstin for billing details & instructions.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 13:38:33', '2023-07-17 20:45:32'),
