  ('zcrm_1579374000122053003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061768243', 'Haley Collins', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to increase her IUA.  Plan changed in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-07-17 12:15:12', '2023-07-17 12:15:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107048002', 'Peter Coddington', NULL, '7-17-2023:  Lisa called.  She had questions re: prev care annual appt, mamm, etc.  We walked thru how to present: "ins" = Y, only time you will ever pres an ID card is for your ''prev care'', in PHCS ntwk & outside ntwk both fine as long as prov will bill for you as no reimb to memb.  [Did not go into an illness appt later & telling them your "ins" is not effective at that point so it is not billed.]
     - Encouraged her to always feel free to call concierge line as guide twds anything she''s considering doing so we can make sure she know guidelines, etc.
     - They have 2 daughters (twins) who turn 18 and will no longer have healthcare (maybe a divorce decree?).  We talked about how to add them to their membership & how that impacts the pricing.  One daughter will be entering the military in a few mos & she''ll probably pull her off at that time.  The other is off to college & will be needing the coverage long term.     I took her to the update form & she''s going to get it filled out.  I cannot see it submitted, but she knows it must be rec''d by the 19th for the twins to be added for an 8/1/2023 eff date.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 12:06:03', '2023-07-18 13:11:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122051003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109285002', 'Michael Danze', NULL, '7-17-2023:  I answered Michael''s call after he was so difficult/not nice to Jennifer.  I think she took the brunt of it because he was in a much nicer place for me.  Maybe the shock of thinking all his ''prev care'' was included & not so limited had passed.
     - Direct Plan = Lmt ''prev care''.  We discussed the very few items covered, waiting periods, etc.  I explained this plan is designed to dovetail w/a DPC doc.*
     - Zion ''Prev Care Med Need'':  His daughter already went for her ''prev care'' annual visit, but not too long ago & he has one soon.  We disc the curr $175 office visit (& pap) max.  How it covers nothing but the office visit itself, so other expenses will be out-of-pkt.  Also discussed available 1x every 12mos/pers.  Also, they are past any waiting period for mamm, colonoscopies.  
        He''s goint to submit both as a ''prev care visit med need''.  He hasn''t made any pymt twds either appt, so he''s going to get those sub right away.  I made sure he has Zion''s ph # & gave him full instructions on their needed Zion Memb Portal & how I just heard from another member that invitation/system is not working, so just make sure they give him the info for submitting via e-mail.  He will find out too, whether the portal is per membership or per person (esp since his daughter is of age).
     * Plan designed to dovetail w/DPC doc/memb is & how they often help w/many of the ''prev care'' items as part of your memb.  Hence why this plan doesn''t have duplciate cov.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-17 11:50:06', '2023-07-18 14:00:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122050003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109285002', 'Michael Danze', NULL, '7/17/23 - Michael called in because him and his daughter had their wellness visits and they received bills. Michael thought that preventative care/wellness visits were included with his plan. When I tried to explain to Michael that wellness visits are not included with his plan, but he and his daughter each have $175.00 to go towards the wellness visits, Michael didn''t like my answer, told me I was wrong, and that he wanted to speak to someone who would give him the right answer. I asked Cari to speak with Michael. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-07-17 11:34:57', '2023-07-17 11:34:57'),
