  ('zcrm_1579374000121715028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116383002', 'Liza Bakken', NULL, '7-11-23 Liza called to inquire about how best to approach her wellness visit in case she needed pre-approval. I told her she should call the MPB Concierge Team to make sure she has the newest card that is for RBP and removal of network. Her card is still showing the PHCS network. So, she definitely needs the new digital card for her appointment on July 18th for wellness. She will call the Team tomorrow morning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-11 18:55:36', '2023-07-11 18:55:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121715023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447234', 'Thomas McCarthy', NULL, '7-11-23 Tom called bc he''s having a GREAT experience with Zion Health and he''s having fun with obtaining the lowest discounts possible. He has some major bills/expenses he tending to. He had a $20K+ bill that he was able to get down to $1500 bc of his knowledge of the industry. He was wondering if there are any benefits to him to get more benefits by doing such a great job in negotiating. I let him know the only option is possibly asking them to lower the IUA or removing it all together. But he''s actually not concerned with the $1000. He was curious if there were any other benefits he could get from doing so.  I told him no. But, I will share this with JT. Pretty incredibly. He''s pumped!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-11 18:32:43', '2023-07-11 18:32:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121742049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116121002', 'Brayden Luna', NULL, '7-11-2023:  ILM for Brayden, that we are trying to contact him to help figure out how to get the ''medical needs'' submitted properly.  Left the conc line hours &amp; #.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-11 17:02:36', '2023-07-11 17:02:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111395009', 'Eric Hove', NULL, '07.11.2023 Aimee called because it sounds like her son might need his tonsils taken out. They have been to a few doctors appointments, which brings them close to fulfilling their $1000 IUA.
Aimee was in the care driving, and she was cutting in and out. So hearing her was a little challenging.
I explained to make sure to present as cash-pay NOT self-pay, as I learned earlier in working here, self-pay means the patient DOES NOT have any coverage, cash-pay does.
Aimee understands the process of how to proceed with a medical need. I made sure she knew about the deadline within 6 months, and she shared that the first appointment was 4 months ago. I encouraged her to start the medical need NOW, since she is close to the deadline, and to fulfilling her IUA. 
Aimee was receptive and appreciative, and will call us back to start the medical need process, when she''s not cutting out. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 16:38:51', '2023-07-11 16:38:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727105', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005676445', 'Maureen Pisani', NULL, '07.11.2023 Maureen called to learn how to submit a medical need to Zion. 
I explained to her that Zion is going through some major changes trying to make it easier on members with this part of the medical cost sharing, however, there are many glitches that are surfacing, so I will share what to expect from this situation and then I''ll have to transfer her to Zion, when we are finished talking. Maureen was super understanding and receptive.
I shared the elements that would come up during this glitchy chapter with Zion:
- Went over the IUA and deadline
- Website not allowing members to work independently yet
- Must call Zion, 888-920-9466, #6 for customer service to get help in opening a medical need
- Zion will send a invitation link to start that application.
- The glitch is that members are not able to upload documents and/or the system is not recognizing their member ID.
- Then the member will Zion again and this time choose #5 for medical need assistance. Zion will share an email for correspondence until they fix this glitch.
Maureen was happy with the instructions, but she wanted to scan her documents into pdf files before I transferred her to start the process. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 15:44:00', '2023-07-11 15:52:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727097', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000085362001', 'Laura Plummer', NULL, '07.11.2023 Laura called wanting to use CirrusMD for a tick she pulled off her son. CirrusMD is not recognizing her information/account, so I told her I would put in a ticket for her. She then also mentioned that she used to have a different account in the past and maybe the previous information is still in there causing this glitch.
I noted the above in the support ticket email to CirrusMD, with hopes that they can resolve this today for her. I told Laura, they usually are pretty quick in resolving matters, so if they contact me back today, I will call her back. If she does not hear back from me, it is because I have not heard back yet, and they will do so tomorrow. NT
******************************************************************************************
I thankfully heard back from CirrusMD saying that she already has an account with them UNDER THE NEW email address, which makes her next step much easier. And they offered a link to reset her account, and another link to reset her password.
I called Laura back, as promised and left her a VM, then I forwarded her the CirrusMD email (deleting their email address) so she can have access to the links they shared for her to reset it all. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 15:20:29', '2023-07-11 16:00:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727087', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120398001', 'Cole Rhodes', NULL, '07.11.2023 Cole called to see about mental wellness services that we might have. I shared about our MAP program, walked him through accessing the site, and the site itself.
He asked about being seen by a Natural Path Doctor and how that would be covered. I said it depends between Preventative or Medical cost sharing. I do believe both times, you''ll need approval to be seen and get covered. Cole wanted to know how to search for a physical therapist, and I was happy to answer it. However he caught us at a really busy time and we were short handed. Therefore, I suggested to schedule a welcome call, with our welcome call specialist. I sent them the link to schedule via CRM. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 14:54:42', '2023-07-11 15:47:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121742026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120398001', 'Cole Rhodes', NULL, '7-11-2023:  Cole called because he needs to pickup an RX.  He was a bit challenging because he''s asking for help, yet has a diff time following instructions, taking time to look at things, & thinks he knows how to do everything (even though he then inaccurately tells you how to do it). Sent him the following RX quote coupon:
     - Doxycycline Hyclate 100mg, #14 caps = $8.04 at Costco on Sngl Care (no sign-up req''d)  [This ended up being less than is girlfriend''s $10 copay.]
     - Cole wants to chg his IUA.  We went over the various price differences, but that there will also be a 60-day waiting period from the eff date of the chg.  It sounds like he decided he''ll go with the $2500 vs the curr 5k IUA.
        He''s a bit challenging saying he knows what "button" to hit to fix it.  I asked him to give us a call & we would direct him to the correct form to fill out on our website because it''s not just a button. He didn''t want to do it right now.  He knows for it to process for Aug 1st eff (the waiting period from there), we must rec the req by 7/19/23.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-11 14:53:32', '2023-07-11 19:32:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084812002', 'Hermilo Cavazos', NULL, '07.11.2023 Hermilo called, now that they have had their initial Doctor''s visit, for their pregnancy. He shared that they had a deadline, but do not have the breakdown of the pregnancy process and billing yet. I said, it will not hurt to go ahead and start the medical need, and note that part in the notes section provided.
I explained to him that Zion is going through some major changes trying to make it easier on members with this part of the medical cost sharing, however, there are many glitches that are surfacing, so I will share what to expect from this situation and then I''ll have to transfer him to Zion, when we are finished talking. Hermilo was super understanding and receptive.
I shared the elements that would come up during this glitchy chapter with Zion:
- Went over the IUA and deadline
