  ('zcrm_1579374000121715018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111954002', 'Daniel Soto', NULL, '7-11-23 Daniel got a new job with benefits that started July 1st. He''s cancelling for July 31st since already paid for July. His new job might be short lived and he expects to come back to MPB in a year or so possibly. He''s happy with our services and was very appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-11 14:06:31', '2023-07-11 14:06:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121742003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110468002', 'Emma Mallon', NULL, '7-11-2023:  Emma called upset that she hasn''t rec''d a call back she was expecting.  She says it is unacceptable that sleep apnea & sleep studies, CPAP machines are not covered.  She feels she''s  being scammed.  I asked if her advisor had not suggested she read Zion''s Memb Guidelines prior to becoming a member & really never got a response.  She keeps using my "ins"...
     - I sent Emma a copy of the curr Zion Memb Guidelines I downloaded today, to make sure they are the most recent, to her e-mail (& cc''d Michele Rebal so she can see they were sent out too).
     I tried to trans her to Michele since yesterday I can see in the tckt Michele had Nahla start that Nahla''s notes/tckt say:
     "... OR speak to one of our admin/supervisor.  Emma was glad to speak to one of our team members. I messaged Michele via teams, and she requested a ticket for tracking." & had to LM for Michele.  I''m not sure she''s in today, so I told Emma she may be out & we''ll ask her to call Emma back.  
     Because Emma did not receive the call she expected today, she was short & we agreed, if she doesn''t hear from her tomorrow, she will call the concierge again for another option.
----------------------------------------------------------------
     Michele sent a Teams chat asking for the name & # of the memb & saying she did not realize she was supposed to call the member.  Here is my response:

[2:50 PM] Cari A.
     Nahla started a ticket yesterday?  She was at lunch.  Christine Corsini''s member Emma Mallon at: (608) 490-3856  is extremely upset that sleep apnea, sleep studies, & equipment are not part of her "insurance".  
     She kept saying she''s being scammed.  I asked if she had not had the chance prior to becoming a member, to read the guidelines because those items have been excluded as long as I can remember.  I just sent her the curr Zion Memb Guidelines & cc''d you on the e-mail.
     She got snippy about how would I know I need this before I need it & what do I do.  I quickly let her know that sometimes we don''t know what will need.  If it''s something like this, some people will move during open enrollment back to traditional insurance trying to get help that way.
     Christine Corsini may or may not have gone over this w/her, but since Nahla started a ticket, you might check w/her on Emma''s expecting a call.  Nahla was at lunch, so I was doing the best I could to help.
     Let me know if you have further questions.  Also, Nahla may be an even better source.

[3:06 PM] Michele Rebal
Unfortuanly I can not call her now.  I didn''t know that was my directive.   I will do what I can when I can.  Thanks!

[3:07 PM] Cari A.
She knows it will probably be tomorrow either way.
----------------------------------------------------------------
Nahla & I talked.  We are both going to try to put "This member is expecting a call back from admin/supervisor/etc., at the top of the tckt to help make that easier for the ticket holder to see.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-07-11 14:05:19', '2023-07-11 16:53:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010870127', 'Heather Braeutigam', NULL, '07.11.2023 Heather called to get help in opening a medical need.
I explained to her that Zion is going through some major changes trying to make it easier on members with this part of the medical cost sharing, however, there are many glitches that are surfacing, so I will share what to expect from this situation and then I''ll have to transfer her to Zion, when we are finished talking. Heather was super understanding and receptive.
I shared the elements that would come up during this glitchy chapter with Zion:
- Went over the IUA and deadline
- Website not allowing members to work independently yet
- Must call Zion, 888-920-9466, #6 for customer service to get help in opening a medical need
- Zion will send a invitation link to start that application.
- The glitch is that members are not able to upload documents and/or the system is not recognizing their member ID.
- Then the member will Zion again and this time choose #5 for medical need assistance. Zion will share an email for correspondence until they fix this glitch.
Heather was happy with the instructions, so I transferred her to start the process. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 13:58:02', '2023-07-11 15:52:50'),
