  ('zcrm_1579374000121716018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073820032', 'Ottis Fausett', NULL, 'Suzanne called and asked 2 billing questions, one of which I was easily able to answer and give her what she needed. First, she needed the Member Payment Update/Chage cogntio form that I emailed over to her, as she needed to change the account that the monthly premium was being withdrawn from. Secondly, I needed to have Patti give Suzanne a call back to help assist her with her 2nd inquiry. Suzanne asked to have sent to her what she called a "Legend" dating back from January 1st, 2023, until this month''s billing cycle for some booking, she needed to do. I told her that every month she & all members are emailed over a receipt after payment has been deducted from the accounts. I let her know thought that Patti who deals with billing with questions like that would be the one I will need to have call her back about her question. Patti did so but no answer and Patti left a voicemail for Suzanne. Patti told me the members can see everything with receipts and previous billing cycles on their MPB.Health Member Portal as well at any time they need. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-07-11 12:27:40', '2023-07-11 12:27:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120690002', 'Feyisara Adaramola', NULL, '07.11.2023 Feyisara''s 9 month old baby has a rash, got a cold, the rash is still there (two weeks now), wants to be able to do a telehealth  session if she could avoid taking her baby out.
I walked her through setting up an account with CirrusMD by sending her an invitation to register. She registered just fine. Then I took her to the updates and portal page, had her bookmark it and let her know that now she has two options to use for a telehealth appointment. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 11:50:27', '2023-07-11 11:54:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000092126001', 'Sandy Giacobbe', NULL, '07.11.2023 Sandy and Maria called to learn how to proceed if they go to an orthopedic doctor. It was a little difficult to hear and understand them. Phone lines were very staticky.
However I did understand that he has an arthritic hip issue, and that his orthopedic will be a cash pay visit, and I shared that with him. He asked about coverage, and I confirmed what he knew that his preX condition, in his second year as a member with Zion will be covered up to 25K. I explained that Zion''s advocacy team will contact the team players in a surgery, should he have one, to negotiate costs and quality.
Sandy and Maria were concerned b/c the ortho.''s office was not wanting to proceed with the appointment without proof of "insurance". Sandy said he did tell them he''s a cash pay patient with a medical cost sharing company. They wanted more. Sandy gave them our MPB card information, but I suggested they speak directly with Zion and I gave them their number, and told him that we would be happy to speak to them to confirm your membership. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 11:23:18', '2023-07-11 11:23:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121727022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109491019', 'Jamie Kosten', NULL, '07.11.2023 Jamie called not knowing how to get her annual visit bill covered. $300.
We did send her the link to submit her bills to Zion and briefly went through what steps to take, however, when Jamie attempted to speak to someone from Zion to complete her medical need process, she believes she received a doctor to speak to who ended up requesting that she speak to us instead. Jamie feels like she''s getting the run around and is not receiving the appropriate support.
I called Zion while she was still on the phone with me and I was able to connect her with them to have a conversation. After Chalice offered a little common information for the situation, I was able to let them have the floor, so I exited the call.  I had offered Jamie''s phone number just in case they got disconnected when I hung up. Chalice promised to call Jamie back if that happened. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-07-11 11:07:32', '2023-07-11 11:26:35'),
