  ('zcrm_1579374000121167060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088688002', 'Perry Thomas', NULL, '6-28-2023:  Lynn called.  She had a bunch of questions:
     She''s having a hard time understanding the different components.  We did the 3 sheets of paper to go over the primary components & basic info on each.
     - ''P''lanstin = ''P''rev Care only & only time you will ever present an ID Card.  She has her post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail, so I was able to go to healthcare.gov w/her to show her the list of what the gvmt says is on the ''prev care'' component.
     - Does this plan have dental and/or vision.  Went over discount program, however she may have purch sep dental and/or vision policy from ind advisor.  Also discussed dental vs medical, vision vs medical.  Gave cataract surgery as the example (& how w/cataract sur = 2 eyes, 2 IUAs).
     - Nuclear Stress Test:  Pd out-of-pkt.  $1200, but they didn''t know they have a $2500.  They''ve seen the doc, had lab tests, etc.  She''s going to quickly get everything scanned because they are at/near/past the 6mos deadline since this started in Jan 2023.  She''s now aware of the deadline, so will hurry to get the scanning done, then call us back for further guidance.
     - She wanted to know if they could lower their mo cont amt.  We talked about 5k IUA & what that looks like w/resp of 3 IUAs per 12 mos period, 4th & beyond, etc.  As we discussed there''s more to look at than your mo contibution (ie: when the healthsharing company kicks in = one example), it seemed like she may be open to calculating what it would cost for the lower 1k IUA (using this newest ''med need'' for Perry as an example = w/1 med need, pricing higher/mo cont, but kicks in sooner).
     - Tomorrow am she has a meeting w/her advisor Whitney Kline & will go over the diff in pricing for the IUAs.  She said she planned orig to ask Whitney most of these questions, but wasn''t sure if she still needed to tt her.  There are some things I cannot answer for her & she will ask Whitney:
               a) price diff for diff IUAs & how that looks w/1, 2, 3 issues in the year.
               b) did they purch sep dental or vision from Whitney?
               c) did they purch a policy from Whitney that covers the IUA (accident type policy)?  If so, what all does it cover.     - CA

Lynn called back & we went over how to sub a ''med need''.  I made sure she has Zion''s ph # & what to expect, then trans to them so she can get the invite for setting up her Zion Memb Portal.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-06-28 13:12:48', '2023-06-28 18:02:55'),
