  ('zcrm_1579374000121167040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121177002', 'Lynn Schauwecker', NULL, '6-28-23 Lynn is turning 60 this year. She''s a W2 employee and 1099 for a small non-profit biz she created. She watched the video. She lives in NY State and it shows MCS count for exemption from penalty - https://nystateofhealth.ny.gov/exemptions.html. She doesn''t do her annual wellness visits and doesn''t plan to fund an HSA. She hasn''t been to the dr. in 10 years since super healthy, no issues at all. No pre-x. She''s paying $287 now for NY exchange plan that costs $465. She will earn more this year and may wind up paying some $ back in taxes. She showed about $68K AGI last year and isn''t sure what it will be this year. Since she doesn''t want the ACA compliant wellness and wants the lowest monthly price, she chose CARE+ and $1000/$265. She also plans to cancel her current ins for possibly July and Aug. and will start with CARE+ on Sept. 1st. She''s saving up money to help pay the $125 fee to get going. Prior to our conversation and her sister Nancy Gentry referring her to me, she was going to simply cancel her ins. altogether.  She''s all set to go and thankful for my time.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-28 11:54:50', '2023-06-28 11:54:50'),
