  ('zcrm_1579374000121126003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091136002', 'Thelma Dillon', NULL, '06.27.2023 Thelma called with a medical wellness check up billing concern. She went to see a PCP, as a new patient on 5/3. She did not get checked out like she expected, the doctor''s office treated the appointment as a new patient consultation in-take appointment for $353.25. They gave her an invoice that broke down other costs, including $445 for THE ACTUAL ANNUAL CHECK-UP.
Thelma, as it seems now, has to wait till next year to get her annual check up. So I consulted with Cari, but she was engaged with another member, so we will call Thelma back.
She still needs a check up but is unsure about the cost now, due to the invoice they gave her
***Prev. supposed to be free, 1st visit for this Dr $353.25 *** The actual annual check up is $445
I needed to consult with Cari on this one, given that it is out of our hands.
*****************************************************************************************
After consulting with Cari, I learned that doctors and their billing office can recode the visit to be preventative to proceed with appropriate billing. In Thelma''s case, that would be fine, except she did not even receive the annual check up during the visit on 5/3m and it''s presently an outstanding bill, as I understood they billed Planstin $445.
I called Thelma and suggested that she speak with the doctor''s office again and ask them to recode the visit, as well as recognize that she did not know the visit on 5/3 was NOT AN ANNUAL check up, and ONLY a consultation visit. Should she have known that detail she would have gone to a different PCP office that operated in a more concise manner with new patients.
Thelma is calling the office to have this conversation. I am looking forward to hearing back from her to take the next appropriate steps. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-27 10:07:41', '2023-06-27 15:23:46'),
