  ('zcrm_1579374000120969306', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086948001', 'Bradford Winship', NULL, '6/22/23 - Renee (Janet) called in today because she was not sure how to use her plan. Renee and I spoke extensively about Planstin, Zion, MPB, how to present herself at specific appointments, and bloodwork. Renee will call back with any questions or concerns she may have. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-06-22 08:18:31', '2023-06-22 08:18:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120980069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120977002', 'Thomas Roule Sr', 'Decline of 7/23 Share Amount', '1st notice sent to member &amp; advisor via EM &amp; VM - 6/21  Member emailed me directing me to rerun pmt w/exsisting CC info.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-06-22 07:04:40', '2023-06-22 07:04:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120982066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109372147', 'Aimee Day', NULL, '6-21-23 I am requesting proof of membership from Sedera for son who''s going to Villanova in PA and needs proof that costs will be shared up to 70% for a hospital stay or ER visit. Waiting for Julie Silverman to respond to send off to Aimee. Aimee was a little nervous about sharing for accidents/injuries since son is an athlete. So, she was pondering accepting the school''s ins for $200. But, son loves Dr. Tusek and wants to keep that membership with Cloud. Also, they are already paying for another child with MCS, so the membership contribution is the same with or without Spencer. Once she understood that she''s responsible for $5K per incident and costs are shared 100% above that and no savings on cancelling, she''s psyched to keep him a member, assuming Sedera will provide the proper letter.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-21 22:52:32', '2023-06-21 22:52:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120987112', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610497', 'Adam Burstein', NULL, '06.21.2023 Adam called to follow up on receiving or haven sent yet the new RBP card. I did not have an answer for him yet, so I guided through the PHCS network approach and to definitely offer the information from the back of his card. He understands to keep everything preventative, and that the new card does not hinder his coverage under Planstin. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-21 17:38:49', '2023-06-21 17:38:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121010043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165427', 'April Porterfield', NULL, '6-21-2023:  April called w/multiple questions:
     - Wanted direction on her ''prev care'' - We went to her post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail & the healthcare.gov site together to review what is & is not considered a benefit.
          - Had questions about a colonoscopy:  We disc cologuard & how using your benefit for that test can leave you resp for the more expensive colonoscopy screening should it come back with a (false) positive.  Wendy sent me info just today on https://coloncancerscreeningkit.com.  April liked that it''s just $35, less invasive, and maybe a better starting point.  She will tt her doc first & I just cut & pasted Wendy''s info that tells her to tt the doc first as well.  Disc what happens if they pull a polyp & how it shifts to healthsharing at that point w/her $2500 IUA, etc.
          - Mamm - we disc the current guidelines on healthcare.gov
          - Went over extremely limited cov labs (in general, just the std lipid panel), but that we can get her to one of our disc lab sites to prepare at a discounted rate.
          - I got her over to Planstin to req a new ID card.  She knows it may or may not have the PHCS logo on it still.  However, I filled her in on our new ''no ntwk req''d'' option.  She will get w/both providers for her up & coming ''prev care'' appts to make sure before she goes that they will bill for her.
          - PHCS Ntwk:  We went ahead & looked for her doc in the PHCS Search Tool: Hansen, Christine C, M.D.	     Obstetrics and Gynecology,Gynecology     4745 Arapahoe Ave, Ste 110 
    Boulder, CO 80303     303-444-5110.  Although, Dr Hansen is listed there is a yellow yeild sign & that means although she is listed, it''s conditional, so I told her to present her Planstin pdf card to them ahead of time & ask the office to call to verify they can in fact bill for her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-06-21 16:46:59', '2023-06-21 17:27:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120982061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165427', 'April Porterfield', NULL, '6-21-23 April called bc she was told by Zion that she doesn''t have preventative. She has the MEC included but she wasn''t familiar with Planstin and couldn''t find her card. I gave her the lowdown on the changes to the ACA for mammograms every other year, pap screenings every 3 and limitations on blood work. I suggested she asks her doctor to do whatever is within the ACA guidelines and code as preventative/wellness screening. She found the MPB.Health card and will call the MPB Concierge Team to request a new digital and hard copy of her Planstin card.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-21 16:14:35', '2023-06-21 16:14:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120987096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011509065', 'Joy Kelley', NULL, '06.21.2023 Analisa, Joy''s advisor, called to confirm Joy''s husband, William was added to the plan, and wanted to know what the difference in cost it was.
I needed to refer to Cari via teams to learn these bullets, b/c I do not have access to the older plans platform on Admin123 (green side).
Cari shared the attached snapshot to reveal the pricing and the difference from adding spouse William to the plan. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-21 15:42:32', '2023-06-21 15:55:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120987085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117844002', 'Lilian Pontillo', NULL, '06.21.2023 Lilian called due to missing her WC for the 3rd time with Jen. She was frustrated but was calmer at the end of the call. Her frustration seemed to stem from a language barrier/misunderstanding. I did give a few details about her plan to soothe her anxiety about getting coverage for her doctor''s visit, which sounded like more than $300.
I shared with her for her wellness check up in the direct plan she would receive a prepaid CC for what we, MPB THINK (due to discrepancies in the guidelines) is $175, this is a bit in a grey area due to it being new, so I asked her to let me check with my supervisor and learn more about this. nd next time her and I talk I''ll have new or same information and she will have the receipts/invoices to possibly start a medical need with Zion prev"
I checked with Jen via teams and she confirmed that Lilian can open a preventative care need in order to get reimbursed, and that''s what we will do when she calls back with the appropriate docs - NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-21 14:34:27', '2023-06-21 14:43:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120987074', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109649024', 'Suzanne Duval', NULL, '06.21.2023 Suzanne called about RBP mischarge, and getting connected with CirrusMD. I guided her to registering with telehealth from our member portal and updates page. She filled out the request and waited on line with me for the confirmation, I ended up needing to send it to her myself and she received it. She completed her set up.
