  ('zcrm_1579374000120516093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118826002', 'Cathy Baker', NULL, '6-8-23 I called Cathy per encouragement from Jennifer. Cathy needed a refresher to our conversation back in April. She actually just had her mammogram done on March 8th, so she''s set on that front. She was planning to do her colonoscopy before her insurance ended but an expected trip came up that she had to go on. None of the dates available for a colonoscopy were possible. So, she now remembers our conversation about why she chose CARE+ and not DIRECT. She''s not self-employed so SECURE is not an option. After some back and fourth she realizes she''s not worried about rushing to get a colonoscopy. She''s happy to wait a year and then another 6 months waiting period for DIRECT, if she wants to switch next June. She''s also interested in the stool tests such as Cologuard or other one I learned about reccently which is coloncancerscreeningkit.com shared with the team from Jane.  I told her of course I''m not a dr. but just learned of this from a colleague in case she wants to do a test right away. She doesn''t have any family history or any of that. She was very nice and remembered all we had talked about and why she chose CARE+. She will revisit with me in a year and decide if she wants to change to DIRECT for an additional $30 per month.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-08 14:13:51', '2023-06-08 14:13:51'),
