  ('zcrm_1579374000120352175', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109660015', 'Erin Kinne', NULL, '06.06.2023 Cari and I spoke, after she found a drug list with a hierarchy chart on it that rendered Erin''s RX request for Etonogestrel-EE to be actually be covered under her preventative. I called Erin back, per Cari''s suggestion,  informed her of the information about OptumRX, where to find their website,  how to search for her pharmacy, and how to present it to the pharmacy. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-06 18:01:13', '2023-06-06 18:01:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120352167', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080613002', 'Michael Van Horn', NULL, '06.06.2023 Michael called concerned about charges that exceed the usual $325. Supposedly, as explained in Planstin''s email, it should show a separation of charges NOT additional charges, which in this case is $50.
I added Michael to the list of members that need to be reimbursed, and shared with Jennifer, my supervisor. I checked his Admin123 profile and it shows that he received a reimbursement today. I told him to give it a few days for it to show up in his bank account. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-06 17:34:16', '2023-06-06 17:41:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120420041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003158023', 'Lorene Cecilia', NULL, '6-6-23 Lorene is choosing to change from PDHC to SECURE now that her accident injuries are doing well which was primarily whiplash. She sees an acupuncturist, osteopath and massage therapist each about 1x per month. She will pay for those cash and set up the HSA to pay that way. She knows they won''t be reimbursed since pre-x and preventative in nature.  She''s a licensed psychotherapist and has own biz. She also owns a rental property which she might sell soon bc there are problems with it. She''s thrilled to get the tax benes from HSA. She did a colonoscopy at age 50 less than 3 years ago and might want to go back at 5-7 years following the first one since they removed polyps. She doens''t have a PCP and asked me for recommendation. I suggested Dr. Gloria Oberbeck in Erie. She was thrilled for the suggestion. She enrolled in SECURE $1000/$325 and cancelled PDHC at $498/$500. She was reimbursed by Sedera for her outstanding bills with car accident that the auto ins didn''t cover. She was thrilled and it took a huge burden off of her. I removed the $100 fee since she''s already a member with MPB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-06 16:59:12', '2023-06-06 17:14:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120379176', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108211002', 'Karen Sachs', NULL, '6-6-2023: Karen called.  She called Fidelity to open her HSA & they told her the MCS didn''t qualify & the "ded" had to be between 1500 & 7lk.  We did some education reg components & how it''s the ASA MEC plan thru Planstin that qualifies her for the HSA (to see her ID Card which will show that high ded - so she can see it in writing).  She wanted to know exactly what she could use the HSA for, labs? etc?  I told her I hadn''t seen a list recently, but it is designed to take care of healthcare exp, so I''d ask Fidelity if they can provide a list.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-06-06 16:58:46', '2023-06-06 16:58:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120420036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003158023', 'Lorene Cecilia', NULL, '6-5-23 Lorene - "Hi Wendy, thank you for encouraging me to submit the bills that I had for my car accident with Sedera
They did end up reimbursing a significant amount and it was really worth doing that :)
Now that it’s done, I would like to discuss with you other options than Sedera. It costs me nearly $500 a month and I remember you saying you had other suggestions

 let me know if a phone call for us to talk about that would make sense. I am mostly free this afternoon if you have time After 1:30 PM 
Otherwise, I have time tomorrow morning before 10 AM and after 330 pm.

Thanks !
Lorène Cecilia "', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-06 16:58:33', '2023-06-06 16:58:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120352145', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086715002', 'Nancy Krampetz', NULL, '06.06.2023 Nancy called to learn how to get reimbursed for her two preventative appointments that she paid for; a wellness check-up and an inconclusive mammogram.
I consulted with Cari to confirm that Planstin does not reimburse, and I shared that with Nancy.
What Car did suggest is to call the doctor and reverse the payment and offer them her Planstin information from the back of her card. 
Nancy and I got cut off. In the meantime, while I was get started back up again (cause I have not received a laptop from the company yet, Nancy contacted her PCP and had the reimbursement conversation and offered her Planstin information.
As for the mammogram, she needed to have a conversation with Planstin to ask if they would go ahead and pay for the 2nd imaging that the imaging facility is requesting, due to the 1st one beign inconclusive. I went ahead and transferred her to Planstin. I emailed her via CRM the Healthcare.gov preventative guidelines link. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-06 16:29:32', '2023-06-06 17:03:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120352134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062132050', 'Elizabeth Longbotham', 'RCV''d Perm. Discuss MPB Plan w/ Steven Longbotham on 9.19.2022', 'Spouse, Steve completed the permission to discuss the MPB plan his wife and daughter are on.
His initial request for the call was to see if the split cost for his daughter''s portion to pay is straight down the middle = $312.50. I said it should be, and I will double check that with the billing department. If I am wrong, I will call you back and clarify the information.
Elizabeth is wanting to get a colonoscopy, but went in for a consultation first, and they charged them $300. I consulted with Cari to see how that works, and if they could''ve declined the consultation, and if members are required to have one..........', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-06 15:24:17', '2023-06-06 17:31:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120352129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109660015', 'Erin Kinne', NULL, '06.06.2023 Erin placed an RX Request for Etonogestrel-ee vaginal ring (Generic), 0.015 MG, 1 for 28 days
I generated and sent the below email via outlook:
Thank you for reaching out to us. I was able to find a few coupon options for:
Etonogestrel-ee vaginal ring (Generic), 0.015 MG, 1 for 28 days
In the zip code you provided, 45011 (Hamilton, OH), you requested Kroger as your preferred pharmacy, so I included that here. However, it was less expensive at Rite Aid, so I included that as well. In addition, GoodRX site stated that presently the Nuvaring BRAND is less expensive than the generic (at Kroger). Therefore, in caser you''re interested, I included that here as well.
I took the liberty and checked with our international shopper, to see what deals he might have on this drug. I included his pricing below. If you''re interested, although it will take longer due to shipping, please contact me with the quote below to place your order.
Below are the prices as of Tuesday.2023:
Etonogestrel-ee vaginal ring (Generic), 0.015 MG, 1 for 28 days: Rite Aid = $45.65
Etonogestrel-ee vaginal ring (Generic), 0.015 MG, 1 for 28 days: Kroger = $96.37
Nuvaring vaginal ring (Brand), 0.015 MG, 1 for 28 days: Kroger = $48.00
From our international shopper:
Nuvaring 0.12/0.015mg x 3 rings. $133.15 + $9.95 shipping

