  ('zcrm_1579374000120252078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106211002', 'Colin Stroumpis', NULL, '06.01.2023 Colin called regarding her son''s blood work results that rendered him to be submitted to the hospital due to very low platelets. Colin was concerned about being able to be covered and moving in the right direction to adhere to any guidelines and verbiage. I guided Colin to present herself as a cash-pay patient, and request the cash-pay discount, fulfill or get close to fulfilling the $2500 IUA. After she''s able to go through all the intro process, she will have paperwork to share, more information as to what is going on with her son, and movement towards fulfilling the IUA to show in the need request. Colin understood and will give us a call back once things settle with the hospital and she has more to work with. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-06-01 15:49:38', '2023-06-01 15:49:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120244093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005956089', 'C. Michaele Hogan', NULL, '6-1-2023:  Michaele called.  She had questions on how something worked, mentioning she hadn''t been able to have her ''Welcome Call''  because our team member became sick.  We had a ton of calls at the same time.  I  believe this was the scenario:
     - Both Michaele & her daugher have been battling RSV.  Michaele''s coughing, they think has actually broken on of her ribs.  She was with a friend when she could barely breathe & they have medical training, so they were able to get her well enough for her to drive to the ER.  She was in the parking lot when she called.  She called to find out if that would be covered.  I let her know she first & foremost needs to take care of herself.  She then mentioned in ~6 minutes her reg doc would be in & she thought she could wait to talk to them, because she trusts what they tell her.  Plus, if they could see her, they are only about a block away.  I mentioned another option might be an Urg Care Cntr, because unlike most doc off''s they often have x-ray machines & could verify if the rib is broken [she seemed worried about the 1k IUA & this might be 1/4 to 1/3 the price.]  She will consider the Urg Care, but she said that drive is pretty far & she''s concerned about being able to get herself there.
        I let her know, take care of yourself.  Once you get the chance to tt your reg doc, you can decide.  In the meantime, we spent a few minutes going over how to present: no ''ins'' or card to present, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, save pymt receipts & ask for detailed inv, offer to pay up to the 1k IUA & ask them to bill her for the bal so she can get the cash together.  Then, in the next few days, when you are not in this emerg situation, call us again & we will show you how to sub a ''med need''.  I think she''s good to go.
     - It sounded like she''d still like to have a ''Welcome Call'' (Jennifer got sick & had to go home when she was orig sched), so I sent her the scheduling link again too.
     - NOTE:  She was so focused on this emerg situation (rightfully so), so I did not go into the fact that the RSV situation for both her & her daughter may be something she should submit to the healthsharing company.  When we tt her again, I thought we could discuss it then.     - CA

6-1-2023:  Michaele did go to the ER.  Nothing broken, not her lungs, they ck''d her heart to rule that out, but that was fine too.  They decided she''s just exhausted so they are giving her medication, which she may or may not fill because her daughter has some left (& she''ll ck w/the fam doc to see how to take).  She will let us know if she needs an RX quote should all that change.
     - She so exhausted.  They are billing her in full for today''s visit & she''s pd nothing so far.  She''s going to call us after the weekend and get help sub her ''med need''.     
     - When she calls, she''ll remind us that she needs to update her name as well (sounds like she''s now divorced).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-06-01 15:32:38', '2023-06-01 17:04:00'),
