  ('zcrm_1579374000120208023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030826196', 'Christopher Howe', NULL, '5-31-2023:  Tina called.  She needed to find out how she gets a colonoscopy screening & a diagnostic endoscopy done.  The center will NOT split the billing (she asked) if they do both procedures at the same time.  She wondered, does she have to be put under twice?  Planstin is supposed to send out the new RBP ID cards on Fri, 6/2/2023.  She''s going to wait for that e-mail & if she doesn''t have it by the following Mon, 6/5/2023, she will call us.
     My suggestions:
     - if they pull a polyp, the colonoscopy will become a diagnostic procedure anyway & then both items will go through Zion (although, 2 parts of the body prob means 2 IUAs).  I suggested, once she gets her new RBP card, call Planstin:  I think she can have the ''prev care'' colonoscopy billed w/prev med coding, & the diagnostic endoscopy billed together to Planstin.  The endoscopy will just come back as member''s resp.  
     - in the meantime, we can make sure we start a ''med need'' for either just the endoscopy, or both if they pull polyps - but we must do this before the 6mos deadline.  Once she has the procedure, she''ll call us back for help in sub the ''med need''.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-31 14:17:21', '2023-06-01 17:36:32'),
