  ('zcrm_1579374000120116013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120770001', 'Adele Haynes', NULL, '5-29-23 Deli Haynes is 56 and getting a divorce. Her children have their own ins and 1 will remain on dad''s ins. She''s had UHC ins. Never had to look for ins for 30 years. She prefers naturopathic, intergrative medicine, chiro, acu, etc. Just got a mammogram but prefers thermogram. She might go get her colonoscopy now with UHC and already got her mammo and pap screening. No health issues except Hashimotos which is pretty much asymptomatic other than she takes a super mild dose of compounded thyroid medicine. She is considering trying bioidentical hormone replacement per her naturopath for the "health benefits." She hasn''t had cycle for 3 years and no symptoms of anything at all.  She also might need a crown within 6 months. Interested in Delta Dental Clear Plan for $55.50 with PPO Premier Plus. Doesn''t need glasses, so no need for VSP. She''s interested in the HMA and not sure what level. Zip code is 80304 and DOB 3/5/1967. She plans to be self-employed but doesn''t know what that looks like yet. Didn''t know what an EIN was and isn''t sure how she plans to move forward. So, I recognized that CARE+ will be a  better fit for now until she starts her biz. I explained this removes the ACA wellness and HSA but all else remains the same as Secure. She understands. She also understands pre-x for her Hashimotos and understands it''s best to ask Concierge for help accessing labs. Wants a July 1st start date and will be away tomorrow to June 10th. We will talk next on June 13th at 12:00 EST / 10:00 MST to enroll in CARE+ and possibly dental and HMA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-30 16:30:58', '2023-05-30 16:30:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120115013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032809035', 'Michele Manna', NULL, '5-30-2023:  Michele called.  She had several things to say:
     - She wanted help finding a gen prac so she could get a referral to a derm for something she thinks is cancerous, on her ''ins''.  We did some educ, not ''ins'', & diff rules.  We don''t req a referral.  Can ck w/a derm, but unusual they req one either.  She will keep receipts & contact us w/in 4-mos to start ''med need'' w/Sedera unless she''s already at the $1500 IUA in which she''ll reach out sooner.  Went over how IUA works, issue spec, etc.  She''ll call if she needs us to send the video of how to start the ''need''.
     - RCI:  she just got off the phone from talking w/Charlie Frohman (the upper guy, above her advisor, Leah Garcia?) who told her ''she no longer needs to worry about ntwk'' on her ''prev care''.  I let her know he must not have realized she''s still on an older plan & I would address 
