  ('zcrm_1579374000120097013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099559002', 'Phonesavanh Phongsavan', NULL, '5-30-2023:  Phonesavanh called w/her sister to make sure she understands (whose English comprehension & speach is much better).  Her husband Prasith went to visit his family in W VA & got sick.  They took him to the ER & it sounds like he''s now in the hospital.  They presented as ''cash-pay''.  I encouraged her to ask for a ''cash-pay'' discount, pay their 1k IUA to get a pymt receipt (& work towards getting  detailed inv).  Then later today or tomorrow, Phonesavanh (& her sister) w/the receipt to upload will call us here on the concierge line to get help submitting the med need.  Due to the language barrier, we all agreed our walking them thru the form will be best.  Phonesavanh let me know, we''ll need to override the e-mail to her sister''s e-mail add so she has help filling out the form.  I let her know we can do that manually when we talk again.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-30 12:52:31', '2023-05-30 13:07:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120090053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080945002', 'Macay Hunter', NULL, '05.30.2023 Macay called a little frustrated and worried and confused as to why Zion is claiming the medical need request for his wife is a pre-X condition that was present prior to signing up with MPB/Zion.
Macay and his family signed up on January 2022. His wife''s back ailment started on October 2022. I consulted with Car and Jen via teams, and unfortunately I had to share with Macay that there isn''t much that we can do to influence Zion''s decision on this. However, he can appeal their decision, and I encouraged it. 
I did encourage that he speak to the PT that Zion did approve to attend to, and he ask them to share what date they shared on the form they submitted to Zion. IF they shared the wrong date, to please go ahead and change it and communicate that with Zion. Macay was not comfortable with contacting the PT yet again, and was wanting to speak to Zion directly first. Macay shared that they submitted the medical need, and Zion came back and said "now we need a treatment plan", they uploaded the treatment plan and invoices (from what I understood), and Zion came back and said "we actually need an itemized receipt", and now they are not considering it a regular shareable need request.
