  ('zcrm_1579374000120048084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104296', 'Roland Jefferson Jr', '6/23 Decline', 'Member had called ahead and advised me that he would have funds available on 5/26.  I reran on 5/30 and pmt declined.  I left VM for member.  After trying on both 5/30 &amp;6/7 Member advised me that funds would be available on 6/9.  However I never heard from him.  After speaking with Karina we agreed that member needed to be cancelled.  I will cancel eff 6/1/23', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-30 12:28:00', '2023-06-12 10:18:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120097008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108211002', 'Karen Sachs', NULL, '5-30-2023:  Karen called.  She''s a bit challenging because she wants to get ahead of you & tell you how it''s going to be, but eventaully she seemed to see the benefit in our being at the same place.
     - Labs:  She wants to have comprehensive labs done.  I asked if she thought she''d want more than a basic lipid panel and she reiterated ''comprehensive''.  So I showed her how to utilize our discount site & it sounds like she''ll just pay the discounted prices, rather than worry about any ''prev care'' lipid test.  [At the start of the conv re: labs, Karen was upset that I wouldn''t just send her an e-mail, "other concierge just e-mail me".  Her comp was right there & I told her, "I can show you in just a few minutes, where e-mailing this would take a good 1/2-hour, hour, for me to type up.  At the end of me showing her the site, she acknowledged, "I see what you mean, that was much easier to do together."]
     -  She was recently laid-off and will for a short while qualify for free ''ins''.  She wondered if she could put this on hold, or what her options are.  We talked about no ''hold'' available, but she could cancel, then reapply, but then there is a new set-up fee & if anything happened in the interim, then there could be a pre-x issue.  
        In the past, she''s had shortterm jobs/benefits (she a consultant), & was prev told she could keep this as a secondary during the short stints.  But, she wondered if having this will preclude her from having the free ''ins''.  I told her, esp since she lives in CA, I wasn''t sure of the rules/reg there.  That maybe her advisor, Kirk Bennett, could ans that for her?
     - HCBB:  she wants to see a derm for a rash & wondered if I could tell her how much that will cost; wants to know how she can find a derm; etc.  It was tough for a while to show her how to look things up, but eventaully, she saw the benefit of staying with me & I was able to show her how to see the range of prices for procedures, how to find a doc, etc.
     - Derm:  We went over maint skin cks not cov.  IF issue found, 1k IUA, so keep all recipts.  If issue >1k, then could have help w/sharing.
     - Upset she doesn''t understand all the vaious names, like Zion.  Went over bried component/pkg education.     
     - HSA:  she asked where she had to go to set-up her HSA.  Went over any financial inst, but to watch fees.  If they req proof of high ded ''ins'' plan, show them your Planstin card.
     - Planstin: She''ll be on the lookout for the new Planstin e-mail w/the new ID card w/out the PHCS logo.  Knows we are moving away from the req''d ntwk.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-30 12:09:30', '2023-05-30 13:46:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120090037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014679123', 'John McBride', NULL, '05.30.2023 John called concerned about charges that exceed the usual $325. Supposedly, as explained in Planstin''s email, it should show a separation of charges NOT additional charges, which in this case is a separation of $275 and an addition of $150.
