  ('zcrm_1579374000119981048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030826048', 'Trent Mullikin', NULL, '5-26-23 I had just sent Trent the email again but I reached him on the phone now. He will connect with me on Tuesday at 10:30 and will have a computer available to walk through the process. He was appreciative of the call. He''s on his way out to meet a tow truck driver bc his car broke down. He has his hands full. Super nice.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 14:14:25', '2023-05-26 14:14:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919192', 'Tanya Bell', NULL, '5-26-23 Left another vm with Tanya letting her know only 2 more days to complete. I also left a vm on her work phone just in case her home # is old. Forwarding her email now as well too.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 14:06:15', '2023-05-26 14:06:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537076', 'Maria (Chris) Comfort', NULL, '5-26-23 Chris called me back to get a full understanding of her membership. During a routine visit they discovered something of concern that''s brand new. They want her to see a pulmonologist. She gave someone that Planstin card and they panicked her by saying she only has preventative care. She was very nice and calm and I explained how it works and why she was told that by providing the Planstin card. She''s relieved. She can afford $1000 but not many thousands. She will call the MPB Concierge Team on Tuesday for their help with pulmonologist and next steps. She does have someone her dr. referred her to and will ask them if he gets good reviews and outcomes.  She has used Zion already bc she had a detached retina during covid. The dr. originally told her she''d have a 2 week stay in the hospital! Instead she found a dr. who could do these surgeries in out patient in 4 hours! She did that and it all went really well and she paid her IUA and all was well. 
She wants to come to our event in June and I told her of the additional times and now she will commit and RSVP.  Yay! She was super nice.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 14:03:24', '2023-05-26 14:03:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037657058', 'Douglas Evans', NULL, '5-26-23 Calling them back since I haven''t heard from them and leaving a vm. Let him know we only have 2 more days to get this done next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 13:45:50', '2023-05-26 13:45:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537076', 'Maria (Chris) Comfort', NULL, '5-26-23 Chis called bc someone told her she only has preventative care with her membership. I left her a long vm explaining she has preventative with Planstin and MCS for accident, injuries, illnesses, etc. I gave her the Concierge # and my # in case she wants a better refresher.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 13:43:28', '2023-05-26 13:43:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044406061', 'Mark Ovind', NULL, '5-26-27 Mark completed his re-activation process just now. It said thank you for your enrollment. YAY!  He went through the entire process in about 22 min from his phone it sounded like.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 13:23:56', '2023-05-26 13:23:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120678002', 'Michael Hand', NULL, '5-26-23 Michael is 33 and getting divorced. Lives in Vail and is self-employed. He watched the video and totally understands. He''s healthy, no meds, no tobacco, yes for annual wellness and yes for HSA. He''s still on his wife''s plan and has to figure out when to move off of it. He''s thinking of a July 1st start date. He''s considering SECURE $1000/$300 or $2500/$245. He''ll call me in a week or two once he''s sorted out the details of ending his current ins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-26 11:21:46', '2023-05-26 11:21:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120004008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118196018', 'Amy Schecterson', NULL, '5-24-2023:  RX Quotes - Amy orig req''d CVS but Safeway was about $55 less.  I sent Amy the options & she chose Safeway.  Here''s what I ended up sending:
     - Sertraline HCL (=gen Zoloft) 100mg, #90 tabs = $13.36 at Safeway on RXGo
     - Metoprolol Succinate ER (gen for Toprol XL) 100mg, #90 tabs = $13.84 at Safeway on BuzzRX
     - Folic Acid (=gen Folate) 1mg, #90 = $8.42 at Safeway on RXGo
     - Methotrexate Sod (=gen Rheumatrex) 2.5mg, #90 tabs = $22.55 at Safeway on GoodRX
     - Simvastatin (=gen Zocor) 40mg, #90 tabs = $9.79 at Safeway on RXGo
Note:  Cost+ might be an option, but they were out-of-stock on 3 of these RXs, so I could not compare all of the pricing.    
     The orig e-mail I sent, I could see the attachments, but when I went into look at the e-mail, the attachments disappeared after I sent it.  So, almost immed I sent the 5 attachments again.  The next day she e-mailed she could not see the attachments.  Maybe she opened that first e-mail?  I resent the 5 coupons & hopefully that took care of the issue.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-26 11:03:01', '2023-05-26 11:03:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120004003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058356758', 'Joan Tekula', NULL, '5-26-2023:  RX Quote:
     - NP Thyroid BRAND 90mg, #90 tabs = $53.45 at Walgreens on RXGo
Orig Joan wanted CVS, but they cheapest coup was $77.64 on RXSaver.  She doesn''t get other RXs, so she said Walgreens was fine.  Sent her the coupon.  She knows we are out for the holiday weekend &amp; will call next Tues if she needs anything further (she still has about a 2 week supply, but will be picking this up next week, or once the RX is trans to Walgreens).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-26 10:51:38', '2023-05-26 10:51:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119978017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091198002', 'Robyn Hallet', NULL, '5-25-2023:  Robyn called &amp; Nahla brought me in.  She wanted to talk a bit further re: the pre-x item (she''s very tight lipped about what she''s having done).  It sounds like she thinks they will recomment surgery, so we discussed non-emerg surg &gt;5k:  we may be able to get help from Care Connect with a willingness to work with them on docs, location, day of the week, etc.  This could help with her only having 25k limit for pre-x if that''s what is determined.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-25 15:44:14', '2023-05-26 00:44:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119989018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091198002', 'Robyn Hallet', NULL, '05.25.2023 Robyn called to refresh her memory on how to proceed with a preventative annual check-up for July, and needing to get lab-work done prior this upcoming Tuesday. I shared the limited coverage on lab-work (standard lipid panel), and anything else will need to be separated by the docs office and presented as a cash pay patient and/or use JasonHealth.com to prepay for a discounted set of lab-work at the chosen site (usually LabCorp/Quest Diagnostics).
Robyn also asked about her preX condition that was mentioned before with Cari. I did explain that she is out of the waiting period, and now Zion would share up to 25K THIS YEAR.
I brought Cari in to help refresh her memory on how to proceed, once her and her doctor want to move forward with treating that preX condition. Cari shared:
Pay the doc appt (it''ll go towards the IUA)
She mentioned CareConnect and the $5000 ceiling, if the surgery is not an emergency and is not going to be more than $5000, and how this could be  a POSSIBLE solution.
She urged her to contact us back to open a medical need. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-25 15:37:47', '2023-05-25 16:01:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119978006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100500002', 'Robin Rudy', NULL, '5/25/2023:  Robin LM w/Backoffice Betties:  She is trying to find a doc for her prev care & also wondered how to present herself.
     I called & tt Robin.  Let her know we''ve been notified she will have a new Planstin ID Card because we are moving to RBP & no req''d ntwk on ''prev care'' on 6/1/2023.  She''s going to be on the lookout for the Planstin e-mail w/her new ID card that no longer has the PHCS logo (I let her know we were told today, those e-mails are going out next week, on 6/2/2023.  We talked a bit about how to present.  Although, I let her know it''s my understanding that the e-mail will also give instructions on the best way to present as well.
     If she has further questions, or doesn''t rec her e-mail as anticipated, she will call back.  She was find waiting until then to find a doc & sched her appt(s).', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-25 14:48:05', '2023-05-25 15:03:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119989008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, '05.25.2023 Willa contacted me via Outlook email re: not receiving the PDF versions of Planstin cards yet. I contacted Planstin, spoke with Carmen. Carmen verified your account and forwarded a softcopy while on the phone to both of the emails included on the plan. In the mail, Willa and Martin should receive two hard copies, one for each adult. 
