  ('zcrm_1579374000119836018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075974301', 'Gerardo Garcia', NULL, 'Gerardo called to inquire about why his MPB portal lists that he will be inactive. I explained that we are moving to the RBP model and that the information in the system will be updated once our files transfer on 5/31/23. I did reassure him that his plan is active and he was happy for the explanation. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-24 13:30:09', '2023-05-24 13:30:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119836013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110083002', 'Benjamin Stephan', NULL, 'Benjamin called to check the status of his wife''s need. I warm transferred him to Zion and I am also sending him an email with his MPB portal login info in it. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-24 13:28:59', '2023-05-24 13:28:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119866031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '5-24-2023:  Jillian called.  Re: multiple items.
     - Colonoscopy:  Back in 9/2021 she had her colonoscopy.  In discussing, she''s upset because it was denied for sharing -- they ruled it pre-x due to polyps being pulled & some cramps in her record.  It cost her ~8k & she''s still paying on it!  So, see below for further discussion.  She had been shocked when it moved from prev to diag, then was denied.  We discussed in depth.
     - Jillian called because they still have her old PO Box listed on her invoices.  She''s upset because she sub her new add mult times.  The add we have showing her at 705 Heartstone Dr here in the CRM is accurate.  I told her I thought they updated her physical address & just didn''t know to remove the mailing.  We sub a new chg form w/"Remove PO Box..." & I told her I think that will fix the issue.  Let me know if it''s still her PO Box on the inv next mo as they sb able to fix before then.
     - Last visit was $850 for a diagnostic test.  They are still trying to figure out what her cramping is from (=why the said her 8k colonoscopy above was pre-x).  She said they are struggling to figure out where the issue is coming from.  We disc that maybe they finally discovered it was her ovaries or something, whe could reapproach Zion on the above colonoscopy, but that since it''s almost 3-years ago, it would be diff to get reimb.  She thought, since the cramps are still there even though they pulled the polyps, that was enough to chg their verdict.  I told I thought they would minimally need something more definitive, but that she can always try (which she said she''d already done).  We talked in detail on the 6mos deadline for this new diagnostic testing on her cramping.  She''s now in her 3rd yr of memb, so she''s phased in & might have help at this point (50k this yr).  She''ll think on & let us know around mo 4 from her DOS if she wants to learn how to sub.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-24 13:28:15', '2023-05-25 00:40:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119836008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113141002', 'Scott Readence', NULL, 'Elizabeth called for some clarification regarding Planstin telling her she will no longer have a plan come 5/31/23. I clarified for Elizabeth what was happening and she was thankful that she will still have a plan, but with the new RBP pricing model. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-24 13:21:43', '2023-05-24 13:21:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119865021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084812002', 'Hermilo Cavazos', NULL, '05.24.2023 Hermilo called to better understand where to go from here now that they found out they are pregnant. I emailed him the directions to submitting a prenatal medical need via CRM and suggested they call us back right after the initial visit to upload and submit all the documents. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-24 12:52:45', '2023-05-24 12:52:45'),
