  ('zcrm_1579374000119676111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098248002', 'Marcus Alig', NULL, '5/19/2023:  Marcus called &amp; wanted to discuss his PCP options for his ''prev care''.  He found a doc, who then told him they were not a part of the PHCS ntwk.  We disc that this last Mon, we heard the ntwk may no longer be req''d in the next month-ish (although, that''s not guaranteed).  He''s going to watch for the new Planstin ID card &amp; will call me next mo if he hasn''t seen anything.  But, waiting was just fine...', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-19 17:37:59', '2023-05-19 17:37:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119676106', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105652002', 'Anthony Jogoleff', NULL, '5-19-2023:  3 RX Quotes.  Costco was cheapest, but for the $10.29, Ashley decided it wasn''t worth doing a transfer.  So, I sent her the following.  We went w/Rite Aid because that''s where they purch Anthony''s RXs last time:
     - Metronidazole 250mg, #56 tabs = $9.87 at Rite Aid on RXGo
     - Doxycycline Hyclate 100mg, #28 tabs at Rite Aid on Good RX
             This strength comes in tabs & caps.  Anthony didn''t care which form.  I ck''d the sites & when it mattered, curr the tabs were less exp.  However, on some sites the price was the same.
     - Pantoprazole (Sod) 40mg, #28 tabs = $9.33 on WellRX.  This is loc spec, & Ashley said they useL 10631 Tierrasanta Blvd, so that is the location I selected for the coupon.
            This drug shows ''DR'' on some of the sites on the 40mg.  As best I can tell, that is the only way this comes.  Well RX is one of the sites that showed the Delayed Release form, so I let Ashley know I can adj if necessary.  When I look online I do not see another option, but sometimes it is really difficult to tell.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-19 17:20:07', '2023-05-19 17:20:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119676095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028177143', 'Heidi Piper', NULL, '05.19.2023 Heidi has an aggressive UTI that is not responding to antibiotics the traditional way. She''s going to see her Infectious Disease Dr and her Homeopathic Dr next week.
She asked how to submit bills to Zion. After consulting with Cari via teams, I relayed the following information to Heidi:
We will open one ''reg med need''.  She will be able to put the homeopathic (if they are licensed) towards the IUA, possibly if Zion approves them.  I shared that alternative treatment usually requires prior approval so we will include it in the request, then it is up to Zion to approve it.  I let her know:  that alternative healthcare, 1) generally requires prior approval  2) needs to be a licensed practitioner  3) since we do not see these ''med needs'' we do not know how they will handle that portion.  Zion, the health-sharing comp, will be the only ones that can determine that. She will call us next week to move forward with what she finds out.
Heidi also needed her log in information. I could not find it in CRM, I consulted Cari, and she was able to find it in the Admin123. I went to the Admin123, but my screen looks different, so Cari helped out. I shared the log-in info with Heidi.
Heidi also does not have her member ID card for MPB, so I connected with Kelly via teams and requested another one sent to her. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-19 15:36:11', '2023-05-19 16:03:45'),
