Sub tckt #2686:  Trying to get a Memb Application sub for the June 1st Eff Date - keeps running into error codes!

19 May 2023 12:35 PM
Cari Adams-Waneka

This member has called the Concierge Line three times in the last 28 minutes for items that are truly the sales process.  He''s been trying to work through getting re-applied to re-join MPB since May 9th.

He keeps calling asking for help through the sales process for the new plan, application help, etc.  It feels like this is something his advisor should be helping him with [even though I''m an advisor, I don''t know why he''s running into these issues.]

I''ve had him call Analisa Cleland multiple times for help.  Finally, today Analisa sends him her link saying to hurry to fill out the application because the deadline is 3pm Eastern today (they have just gotten off the phone & he''s calling the Concierge Line for application help at 2:38pm eastern).  I suggest having Analisa walk through the application with him because of the 20-minute deadline, might be good.  To make sure he doesn''t make mistakes in his rushed timeline.  The Concierge line works with members after they are members & not trained to help with the application process, that''s the advisor''s job.

He does call her & when they run into issues (it''s telling him it won''t accept ss #s, she has him call the Concierge Line again).  I told him I didn''t know if he could put in temp ss #s until he has all of them, & update them later, or what the best process was.  He calls me at 3:12pm eastern to let me know Analisa had a 1:00pm mtn appt (=3pm eastern) & could not help him.  But, it continues to tell him they ss #s are not valid. 

I let him know I would send through a ticket so the office is aware that he tried to get his application in for the June 1st deadline.  That I didn''t know how else to be of assistance.
-------------------------------------------------------
JD responded to this tckt thinking it was my pot memb.  I gave him Analisa''s name & Ryan Dunlap -- he & JK are going to work on the issue.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-19 12:43:30', '2023-05-19 17:39:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119637078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018080005', 'Audra Boyd', 'New Membership eff 6/1/23', 'Member &amp; Spouse $1000 IUA Redirect', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-19 12:43:10', '2023-05-19 12:43:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119676047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113835002', 'Terry Draper', NULL, '05.19.2023 Shelly, annual exam, how can she have more than the standard lipid panel as labwork for future RX prescriptions.
Shelly''s questions revolved around better understanding her plan and how to maneuver different scenarios: Annual check ups and keeping it preventative, Mamm 2D/3D, Colon and what if they pulled polyps and should she get the colorgard or plain colonoscopy, lab-work and if they too need to be in network.
I explained all the angles to preventative scenarios, the language to use, and what to do if it turns diagnostic. We spoke about IUA''s and how they apply.
Shelly usually gets the 3D Mamm due to dense breasts, per her doctor''s recommendation. Jen, Cari and I agreed that that is a conversation worth having with Planstin and share those exact details with them. In the past, she''s had the coverage pay for 2D and she cash paid for the rest.
Wondering if that would work here with Planstin (she will call Planstin and have a conversation she said)?
