  ('zcrm_1579374000119552021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '5-17-23 Patti discovered Elizabeth was not billed correctly from FTNI since the beginning of the year. She''s been billed at $378 + cc fee but should have been paying $493.78+cc fee = $508.59. I talked with Elizabeth and this comes at a terrible time after her two surgeries and Sedera stating they will make her pay $25K for the 2nd knee replacement. But, most important is that her membership remains active. She''s asking that she''s billed at the lower amount for May and then wait until the 25th for the higher amount for June. I''m waiting to hear back from Patti. 
She''s also struggling with Redirect who only see her membership began in June of 2022 or something weird when in fact it began Jan. 2020. We need to resend the file to Redirect to get her start date corrected ASAP. This will allow her more chiro visit for 2023 now that she needs them to recover from her surgery. 
She''s also reached her max of PT through Sedera which is capped at $3K. There''s not much I can do about that. Steadman''s will charge her $125 for each visit as their cash price. Apparently they charge 3X that rate normally. Crazy!
I also suggested she reviews my email sent about a month ago as suggestions for how to deal with the $25K she''s expecting to have to pay for since Sedera won''t. Her income is lower than usual but may not still qualify for the debt dismissal. It would work if she only has to submit a W2. But, if she has to submit her tax return then it won''t work. 
She''s in good spirits today, but yesterday was a terrible day in her healing. She''s spent her entire life out of the medical establishment and she sees its woes even more now. the oxycodone was brutal on her body and incredibly addictive. She doing various detoxing now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-17 14:02:40', '2023-05-17 14:02:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119565036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093072002', 'Richard Brodeur', NULL, '05.17.2023 Melissa called to refresh her memory on how to present herself (for her daughter, 21 YO), at the  physical check up. I went over the process of making and maintaining a preventative appointment, and should something arise at the appointment (i.e. rx quote), to have them separate it and ask how would they like to handle that part. Melissa asked about having her tested for TB, and if it is covered with the preventative appointment, and after I checked the healthcare.gov, I was able to confirm with her that is should be covered. I could not find Melissa''s doctor that she and her husband have been to, and who she is taking her daughter to, but Melissa said it should be fine, because it did not raise a problem before. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-17 13:22:32', '2023-05-17 13:22:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119542056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111070002', 'Charles Reynolds', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation  eff 6/1/23 due to the fact that Labs are not covered.  I spoke to Lou and he told me that member was aware of that prior to enrollment.   I will process cancellation', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-17 12:14:54', '2023-05-17 12:15:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119552013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001230091', 'Lester Pardoe', NULL, '5-17-23 "Somehow auto pay got turned off, and they accepted payment and turned my plan back on.

I had an unopened letter from them dated last week with an invoice amount for a few months, but zero communication other than that, and nothing in last weeks letter saying I was terminated.

Thanks a ton for the heads up!!  Greatly appreciate  the A+ customer service

Lester"

Phew, all set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-17 12:13:30', '2023-05-17 12:13:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119565026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108404009', 'Mark Carty', NULL, '05.17.2023 Mark called to understand why the urgent gyno visit for his wife did not accept his Planstin card, saying they are not in network. 
I explained that if it was not a preventative appointment you do not have to abide by the PHCS network. For this appointment, to go ahead an present as a cash pay patient and save the receipts.
I then said I can help you find a doctor in the PHCS network, if you like. He said that that''s where he found that doctor''s office and thought he did good. I was not sure why they showed up, when they are not in the PHCS network, but I did recommend that he call the offices prior to the appointment to confirm they are indeed still in the network where he just found them in. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-17 12:11:30', '2023-05-17 12:11:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119548018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005185119', 'Susan Ronit Carter', NULL, 'Susan called to cancel Health Excellence Select. Form sent', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-05-17 11:44:20', '2023-05-17 11:44:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119570006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106211002', 'Colin Stroumpis', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 3060 Question : What do I put down as our Health Insurance member number?', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-05-17 11:40:15', '2023-05-17 11:40:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119565013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014900054', 'Terry Talley', NULL, '05.17.2023 Terry called back wondering how to proceed to be seen by a doctor for his infection. I guided him to see any doctor of his choosing who is available and to present himself as a cash-pay patient and to save all his receipts from this incident, and should his expenses start reaching or exceed his IUA $1000 to give us a call back and we will open a medical need. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-17 11:32:50', '2023-05-17 11:32:50'),
