  ('zcrm_1579374000119487008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095964011', 'Benjamin Deweese', NULL, '5/17/23 - Ben called to change his payment info. I sent him the payment update form via email. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-17 07:34:18', '2023-05-17 07:34:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119470088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027283234', 'Kristen Le Peau', NULL, '5-16-2023:  RX Quote:  KS is preferred pharmacy.  We went w/Safeway last time, but she''s listed KS again and it''s only a $1.88 more, so I did send the cheapest coupon.
     - Ampnetamine/Dextroamphetamine (= gen Adderall XR) 15mg, #90 caps = $70.40 at KS on Sngl Care (no sign-up req''d).
        I also let her know it shows there is a contract between KS & Sngle Care, but we don''t use that site as often as others, so the next cheapest KS coup = $71.90 on RXGo, Safeway is $68.52 on RXGo [and for our info: Walmart is $69.85 on GoodRX.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-17 00:39:10', '2023-05-17 00:39:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119474044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117873002', 'Marc Marlowe', NULL, '05.16.2023Patricia called to confirm what she understands about the prescription request process. I guided her through the member portals and updates page, had her bookmark it and note the form on there. She had already filled one out, and ok this is what I filled out, just wanted to make sure I did it right. I explained the process to her, included the international shopper option and if there''s an emergency situation.

I fulfilled their RX request and sent them the following coupon information via Outlook:
".....based on your zip code 85215.
Attached you will find 2 coupons, from the least expensive to your preferred pharmacy.
Below are the average prices as of today, 05.16.2023
       -Metoprolol Er Succinate: 100MG, 90 Tablets: Osko $16.82
       -Metoprolol Er Succinate: 100MG, 90 Tablets: CVS $17.27            -    NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-16 16:46:10', '2023-05-16 17:23:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119474039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116236002', 'Lisa D''Onofrio', NULL, '05.16.2023 Lisa called with several questions. She had not had her welcome call yet, but signed up for one in two days, while we were on the phone. 
Some of the questions Lisa had, and I answered multiple times in different ways are:
-She started off by saying that she was told she could attend any doctor of her choosing, upon signage with MPB. I told her that the company, Planstin, has not solidified that plan with us and are still finalizing loose ends. I consulted with Cari via teams regarding this and we discussed the matter after my call. I offered to call Lisa back to update her on it.
-How and when to submit bills to get covered? We went over the process, and how the IUA works, and what it stands for and how it IS NOT the same as the deductible.
-What are all the parts of her plan? I went over the three major parts in the Secure plan (Essentials, Prev., Zion)
-How to proceed with a preventative appointment? I went over the process from the start (PHCS Network, present as Planstin card holder, offer their information, request that they maintain the appointment as preventative, what to do if diagnostic surfaces during that appointment)
-Searched 3 entities to confirm they are in network, and I encouraged her to contact who she found directly and ask if they are still in the network. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-16 16:42:46', '2023-05-16 17:03:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423116', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130802017', 'Bruce Maleski', NULL, '5-16-23 Came to me via Justin Acker.  Sara is 47 and husband is 62 with 2 boys and the oldest is 22.  They have 3 different policies now. Sara gets one through her employer. Husband is self-employed and gets a plan through ACA with one son. They eldest son is on Medicaid but will likely be kicked off now without the emergency covid Medicaid coverage.  Sara had melanoma 7 years ago. Her last treatment was in Nov. 10th of 2016. For the melanoma she was only treated for 4 months and then it made her too sick, so she stopped. The only ongoing issue is the treatment affected her adrenal glands. She now has adrenal deficiency and takes progesterone every day to keep that managed.   Her husband and the oldest son both have high blood pressure that they manage well with meds. No hospital stays for this. She''s not sure what they are paying now for their insurance. But, they see how terrible the coverage is and they wound up paying a huge amount back in taxes from last year.  So, they''re not pleased with that. Educated her about SECURE $1000/$915. She was hoping for the lower IUA of $500 like Sedera offers. I let her know this is a better option at this time with the more inclusive guidelines, etc.  She will discuss it with her husband and make a decision by Thursday 3:00 MST for next appt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-16 16:27:53', '2023-05-16 16:27:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119470080', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109649002', 'Sean Clouse', NULL, '5-16-2023:  Sean sent an e-mail asking if the IUD was a covered bc.  I let him know I''ve heard they do include that, however, please call Planstin directly (gave him their # & hours of srvc) as they can confirm that for you.
     - He also wanted us to find and negotiate with the doctor.  I replied:  The list of providers I sent over on 4/24/23 is our helping him find a doc.  That elig ''prev care'' is paid in full for him, so there are no negotiations necessary.  Negotiations is not a service the Concierge Team provides.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-16 15:51:10', '2023-05-16 15:51:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119474026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122013002', 'Donald Hubbard', NULL, '05.16.23:   Cindy called me with several questions about the plans.  She said she found several insurance plans he asked her to check out and she had him review them but they''re all more expensive than ours.  He seems to be reluctant with an MPB plan because it''s a new concept and it''s foreign to him. She likes the DIRECT plan for him.  He''s also interested in Dental.  I told her about Denali.  She said she watched the video and thought it was very helpful and well done.  He needs a start date of July 1.  She''ll discuss it further with him and let me know.  I told her I want to help him enroll if he decides to do so. And he must do our Welcome Call to learn more about the plan.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-05-16 14:56:40', '2023-05-16 14:56:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119474018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122013002', 'Donald Hubbard', NULL, '05.12.23:  Called and spoke to Cindy.  Donnie needs a July 1 start date.  He has no pre-x, no meds. I explained difference of the 3 plans and recommended the DIRECT plan for him.  I also gae her pricing for each plan for his age group:  Care+ - $265; Secure - $325; Direct - $295. Cindy asked for the website to review info.  I sent her my website link. Cindy said they''d make a decision this week.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-05-16 14:41:24', '2023-05-16 14:44:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119474013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122013002', 'Donald Hubbard', NULL, '05.11.23:  Cindy Hubbard, Donnie''s wife and Emily''s (my member)  mother, texted me. She is a biologist for the state of VA and she''s retiring.  Her husband, who is on her health insurance plan, will have to pay $880/mo. just for himself, if he stays on it.  Cindy is seeking a less expensive health plan for him to use until he is age 65 and gets Medicare.  He''s 62 now.  We scheduled a call for 5/12.  
Cindy''s phone:  804-221-1025
Cindy''s email:  hokie780@aol.com', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-05-16 14:40:01', '2023-05-16 14:59:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119470066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096786002', 'Jonathan Lampert-Hiller', NULL, '5-16-2023:  Natalie called.  She moved onto Jonathan''s memb (her fiance''s:  Jonathan Brumbaugh) eff 5/1/2023.  However, the draw for her May mo cont on her own memb was still processed.  I can see in the CRM = her own memb cancelled, but it''s still showing as active in Admin123 &amp; sched to draw again for the June mo cont.  Because we are so close to the deadline for the next draw, I trans her directly to Patti.  But, I''m documenting in both accts for general info.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-16 14:07:57', '2023-05-16 14:13:44'),
