  ('zcrm_1579374000119472013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098327002', 'Cindy Gordon', 'New Plan eff 6/1/2023', 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-16 08:24:01', '2023-05-16 08:24:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119472008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098327002', 'Cindy Gordon', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request to remove dependent &amp; lower her IUA to $1000 eff 6/1/23.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-16 08:22:01', '2023-05-16 08:22:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119472003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006690', 'Miguel Gallardo', NULL, 'Member emailed me and left VM with intention to cancel.  I emailed member the link w/copy to adviser.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-16 07:49:58', '2023-05-16 07:49:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119465013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108524001', 'Megan Land', 'Jennifer Opened a Ticket for Issue', '5/16/23 - Megan called in this AM inquiring about how she gets her preventative care appointments paid for under her Direct Care plan. I explained to Megan that preventative care is only included in this plan if you have a Direct Primary Care provider but she would have $250 per person for office visits only once her 6 months are up. I also advised Megan that the $250 is to go towards the office visit alone and that it does not go towards any preventative care items that are done during the visit. Megan stated that she was under the impression that she could use the $250 towards anything and that she thought that meant for the items that would be done during her prev. care visits. She stated that Zach told her she did not have to have a DPC (which is true) but I reiterated to Megan that her prev care items would then be out of pocket expenses. 

Can someone reach out to Zach to make sure he knows that prev care is not included in the DPC plan without having a DPC provider?', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-16 07:30:50', '2023-05-16 07:30:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423101', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116613002', 'Timothy Foley', NULL, '5-15-2023:  Meryluz called, she is very confused.  Here''s what we went over:
     - CirrusMD:  She orig said she was trying to set up their CirrusMD so she could sub her husb''s emerg receipts from an ER visit.  I did a bit of explaining the diff components.  We tried to send her invites for CirrusMD, but on Timothy, it says he already has an acct & says Meryluz is not recognized.  I got the proper e-mails from Meryluz & sub a supp e-mail to try to fix both of their accts.  They''ve done some changing of e-mails so that could be confusing issues. (See end of Nahla''s note from 4/28/23 to see accurately whose e-mail is whose.
     - Zion: Sent Meryluz the temp for sub a ''med need'' to Zion (she couldn''t find the prev one).  Went thru the process in depth.  At the end, made sure she knows Zion''s # & trans her to get her Zion memb #.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-15 17:39:17', '2023-05-16 00:08:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027220284', 'Michael Kennedy', NULL, '5-15-23 He requested email opt-out which I just selected.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-15 17:33:05', '2023-05-15 17:33:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060583574', 'Carlos Guerrero', NULL, '5-15-2023:  Frances called & is having back pain that is radiating into her legs.  She needs to see a doctor to get the MRI referral.  We tried to use HCBB, but is on a MAC & it doesn''t work very well.  We finally were able to look up doc''s by their names (it wouldn''t pull up specialties) so I could show her the info available.  She was excited to see the comments and ratings.
     - We went over how to present as no ins, ''cash-pay'', ask for disc, resp for 1k IUA, save all detailed inv & pymt receipts.  IUA is issue spec, 6mos deadline, alt treatments req prior-approval before 1st visit, etc.  She will call for help in sub ''med need'' once she gets into this.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-15 15:45:30', '2023-05-16 00:12:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069994428', 'Kelly Snider', NULL, '5-15-2023:  Kelly called.  Husb had a stroke recently.  It sounds like she sub a ''med need'', etc, directly w/Zion.  Speach Therapy is req''d for him to swallow, but they were told "we wouldn''t pay for that".  I let her know who we are, and who I thought maybe they''ve been talking with = healthshare comp Zion.  I encouraged her to use us as a guide in the future, which she liked.  I made sure she has Zion''s # &amp; trans her there to tt the ''med need'' dept to see what they need to do.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-15 15:24:35', '2023-05-15 15:30:36');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108409002', 'Alan Monte', NULL, '05.15.2023 Rebekah called to help Alan submit a medical needs request with Zion. I emailed her the instructions via CRM, and we filled it out together.
I noticed her email was not included on the plan, so I recommended that she add it, if she plans on making use of the telehealth at all, as she can only use her email for that and not his. She was happy to do so, so I emailed her the change form link via CRM as well.
They did not have their Zion member ID number, so I direct transferred her to Zion after we were done filling out the form request. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-15 15:11:05', '2023-05-15 15:22:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119465008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118196002', 'Brian Gould', NULL, 'Left detailed vm and sent a new scheduling link. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-15 14:32:40', '2023-05-15 14:32:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571414', 'Donald Henig', NULL, '5-15-2023:  Donald is having an MRI done on an old inner ear tumor that it''s been years since they''ve looked at it.  [I did not go into pre-x w/him.  He''s in the 3rd yr of his memb, so would have some help if needed if it were.]  He knows no ntwk, present as ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' discount, pay 1k IUA &amp; ask if they can bill him for balance.  IF they decide they need to do more or is &gt; his IUA, he will call us for guidance on sub a ''med need''.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-15 14:13:51', '2023-05-15 14:13:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119405093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, 'Member submitted Change from to add newborn to membership.  I will add and change pricing in A123.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-15 13:43:48', '2023-05-15 13:43:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119405088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028419199', 'Jane Rosenberg', NULL, 'I finally spoke to member re: 1095 and the monetary breakdown of her membership.  I told her that the 1095C would not address that, that it only would show when she was on the plan during the year.  I advised her that the MEC portion is $81 per month.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-15 13:24:49', '2023-05-15 13:24:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119427043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000119464002', 'Sandra Chase', NULL, 'Sandra called in on the sales line this morning. She has been with Medishare and had too many price increases. She found us through a Google search. She had several questions, and we spent quite a while on the phone. Nice lady, I gave her my link and she said she will look it over, and will probably enroll today. She did so.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-05-15 13:21:34', '2023-05-15 13:21:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119405078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117968001', 'Amanda Williams', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation eff 6/1/23  due to the fact that she now has employer coverage.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-15 13:04:48', '2023-05-15 13:04:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119405068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115064002', 'Samantha Everhart', NULL, 'Member requested cancellation  eff 6/1 due to the fact that she now has a medical condition.  I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-15 12:56:18', '2023-05-15 12:56:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119405058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006727', 'Charles Korb III', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation  eff 6/1/23 due to going on Medicaid.  Wendy ok''d via teams.  I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-05-15 12:40:23', '2023-05-15 12:40:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119423038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115751002', 'Rocio Borzage', NULL, '5-11-2023:  William sent a bunch of RX Quote info thru his advisor Whitney Kline.  She says he doesn''t need them right now, but is looking at pricing.  There were 12-RX Quotes, but qty of creams/ointments was challenging.  I sent basic info w/best practice for getting coupon(s) instructions [ie: coupons best to be used w/in about a week, so need to be fresh req about 1 week before you need.  IF getting 12-items at once, plez give us extra time. Allow extra time if ordering from our Int shopper for shipping.]  Rite Aid was cheapest for his last RX & we cheapest on most items, so I quoted everything there.  Here are the estimates I sent:
     - Levalbuterol 0.63mg/3ml Nebulizer Solution, #25 vials = $19.50 at Rite Aid  on RXGo.  It''s cheaper to purchase 3x at this price, because #75 vials is $60.75.
     - Betamethasone DP Aug Cream 0.05%, 50gms = $20.14 at Rite Aid on RXSaver.  15 gms is the other available size and it''s currently $10.87.
     - Tretinoin Cream 0.1%, 45gms = $48.01 at Rite Aid on GoodRX.  20gm tubes are also available, but the price seems best for the larger tube.
     - Vuity Eye Drops 1.25%, 2.5ml = $76.58 at Rite Aid  on RXGo.  This drug does not yet have a generic version available & is expensive.  However, Reid cannot source.
     - Fluocinonide Ointment 0.05%, 60gms = $35.48 at Rite Aid on Good RX.  This also comes in 15gm and 30 gm tubes.
     - Atorvastatin Calc 10mg, #45 tabs = $9.05 at Rite Aid on WellRX (location specific, ''As Low As'' price, so must conf location for accurate pricing) .  NOTE: I cannot find a 5mg tablet as requested, therefore, I quoted 10mg tablets, with ½ tablet equaling 5mg and assuming you take that once a day with #45 equaling a 90-day supply.
     - Ezetimbe 10mg, #45 tabs = $18.93 at Rite Aid on GoodRX.  NOTE: I cannot find a 5mg tablet as requested, therefore, I''m quoting 10mg tablets, with ½ tablet equaling 5mg and assuming you take that once a day with #45 equaling a 90-day supply.
     - Bupropion HCL XL 300mg, #90 tabs =$31.55 at Rite Aid on GoodRX
     - Spironolactone 100mg, #90 tabs = $18.59 at Rite Aid on RXGO
     - Tacrolims Ointment 0.1%, 30gms = $60.77 at Rite Aid at RXSaver (& GoodRX if 1-83 day supp).  This comes in 60gm and 100gm sizes as well.  However, due to the price, I started with just 30gms.
     - Flovent Diskus 100mcg:  There''s no generic available in the ''Diskus'' yet.  This is extremely expensive locally = 1 x 60 doses, the cheapest price I found was just under $210.  Reid can source & his price is amazing = 3 x 60 doses = $154.77 w/s&h.  Sent Reid''s quote & contact info.
     - Rite Aid - $379.78 = total for above RXs
          + prev Fluticasone Prop HFA inhaler price:  $67.86
          + Flovent Diskus (see info above)
     - MyFreePharmacy: Only 4 items, in these strengths are available thru them & just as many are not even available thru them, plus some would require the doc chging the strength which seems unreasonable since it''s not equivalent.
     With so many drugs, & Rite Aid consistently being well priced, it seemed more imp to have the interactive software thru purch everything at one location.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-15 12:15:57', '2023-05-15 12:40:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119427038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000119467002', 'Bradley Kirts', NULL, 'Bradley called back, he has a strong accent, hard to understand. Discussed Care Plus, sent email with pricing and enrollment.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-05-15 11:38:51', '2023-05-15 11:38:51'),
