  ('zcrm_1579374000119285023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096555046', 'Anastazia Laubert', NULL, '5-11-23  Anastazia called bc she filed her taxes with Turbo tax and it told her she owed $1700 from the APTC. However, she wound up actually borrowing money to survive while she was self-employed. She didn''t even make what she projected with C4. She did get a job after and the system seems to be accounting for that, not for the months she was unemployed. I recommended she speak with a tax advisor or she will have to change her inputs into Turbo tax to better show her income during those months. She will work on it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-11 17:04:50', '2023-05-11 17:04:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119285018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779108', 'Laura Laffoon', NULL, '5-11-23 Laura called me back to let me know she finally successfully made her payment and set up auto-pay. She had called Cinga twice and tried online tried and it never worked. But, she finally got it set up with her bank account and now she should be all set as far as she knows. She thanked me for the call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-11 16:31:42', '2023-05-11 16:31:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119285013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113410109', 'Jeremy Colbert', NULL, '5-11-23 Hey Wendy,

Thanks for the heads up. I just paid it last week and got notified, I thought it was a delayed response. I tried setting up auto pay last week but couldn''t find it---though just logged in now, paid the updated balance, and found out how to enable auto-pay. All set. Thanks again!

Jeremy', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-11 16:22:15', '2023-05-11 16:22:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119285008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062250051', 'Cody Bennett', NULL, '5-11-23 Left vm and sent email to let him know of his late payment notice. He owes $50.56 and perhaps more now in May.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-11 16:19:53', '2023-05-11 16:19:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119279016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000076937066', 'Margaret Tiscornia', NULL, '05.11.2023 Margaret called to check if she can pay her membership with her HSA account. Between Cari and I, we did not want to be wrong, so we said most likely healthsharing is not eligible, but Margaret must speak to Wendy for more information and understanding, and for the latest list of eligible items, her financial institution would help best.
She added a newborn, not the 1st child though, and her plan went up in price. Cari help check on that, and it turns out it was during the same time in the fall of 2022 when Zion shifted their price toward age-contribution. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-11 16:10:34', '2023-05-11 16:17:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119285003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113410109', 'Jeremy Colbert', NULL, '5-11-23 I sent an email and left a vm to let Jeremy know his payment is late to keep his plan active. He has health issues now and really needs to keep his account. I''ve asked him to let me know when it''s all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-11 15:59:53', '2023-05-11 15:59:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119279011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000090048002', 'Lisa Chlysta', NULL, '05.11.2023 Lisa called to give more information about the open need for her husband. She thought she needed to call us  then talk to Zion, but I told her she is always welcome to call us, but for answers regarding the medical need, Zion is best to call for a more productive call. I transferred her to Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-11 15:15:04', '2023-05-11 15:15:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119245013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094942002', 'Tim Ottmann', NULL, '5-11-2023:  A providers office called asking for Angela''s pharmacy ''ins'' info.  They are trying to get her Xolair & when the gal calls to order it, they reqire that info.  I tried to expain Angela doesn''t have ''ins'' and therefore no pharmacy ''ins'' either.  The gal got snippy, "I know she doesn''t have ''ins'', but I have to give them this information."  
     I sugg, if this is for a ''qual med need'', it''s possible she could get help if it''s >$500 per month, at least for a while, but I do not see anything in the prev notes re: a ''med need''.  The gal gave me some long medical terminology:  idiopathic something...  I let her know I didn''t know what that was so I could not advise whether Angela might have help.
     Also, I see Angela asks about other products in the prev notes, so I let the gal know:  maybe Angela''s Ind Advisor sold her a stand alone pharmacy product, but that wouldn''t go thru us.  I did provide Analisa''s first name & ph # in case that''s the situation.
     After we got off the phone, I looked up the drug: it looks like a single syringe of this (& it requires going through special sources/ordering to get it) is  ~$1300/mo.  Usage is for nasal polyps, and unknow rashes?  Plus, the instructions online say "XOLAIR is given in 1 or more injections under the skin (subcutaneous), 1 time every 2 or 4 weeks."
     - NOTE:  There is a 5k IUA she''s be responsible for, however, they could easily get to that w/this expenisve RX if it''s a qualified need.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-11 13:52:37', '2023-05-11 14:10:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119279003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109496027', 'Stephen Osteen', NULL, '05.11.2023 Stephen had already started filling out the med need request and just wanted to make sure he was filling it out correctly. We walked through it together in sections, until he was ready to upload and submit. I told him to expect two emails from his submission; confirmation that they received his request and assigning a processor a few days afterwards. I recommended that he call us back in a week if he had not heard back from them. Stephen will be going on vacation next week and will call and follow up after he gets back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-11 13:33:09', '2023-05-11 13:39:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119266008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117961002', 'Ryan Banuelos', NULL, 'Welcome call complete! JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-11 13:11:22', '2023-05-11 13:11:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119251018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116391002', 'Catherine Rodriguez', NULL, 'Cathy called into the concierge line while I am covering for their weekly Concierge meeting every Thursday at 2pm, to state that she just enrolled for this plan while traveling, and she just got back so she just needed some help with how everything works. She has a lot going on right now and just wanted in depth detail on how everything with her plan works, etc. Also, she said she got notified that her payment info declined. I let her know that Patti would have called and also sent an email with the link to the Payment Update form to update billing info. She does not see any link so I told her along with the Schedule a Welcome Call link to schedule one for betting insight on how her plan works, I also sent the payment update form with the link to click. I explained to her how to do the payment update form and schedule the welcome call, etc. She was very thankful and is all set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-05-11 12:45:59', '2023-05-11 12:45:59'),
