  ('zcrm_1579374000119200013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005663549', 'Dana Jackiewicz', NULL, '5/11/23 - Dana called to find out what the $50.00 charge is for monthly. I explained and she said she approved this charge so she does not want to cancel it. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-11 08:57:39', '2023-05-11 08:57:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119200008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000090048002', 'Lisa Chlysta', NULL, '5/11/23 - Lisa needed to update some information for her need she has opened with Zion. I warm transferred her to Zion so that she could update that info with them in real time. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-11 08:17:51', '2023-05-11 08:17:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119200003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571414', 'Donald Henig', NULL, '5/11/23 - Don called just to make sure his provider, Laura Munoz, was in the PHCS network for his physical today. I did verify that she is in the network and we went over how to present his Planstin card. Don was also inquiring about his HSA and how to make a contribution to which I had him speak with his advisor since that is who his HSA is with. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-11 08:09:06', '2023-05-11 08:09:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119187003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110424034', 'Todd Schrum', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-05-11 07:36:18', '2023-05-11 07:36:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119118126', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104184', '(Ronald) Shaefer Welch', NULL, '5-10-23 Shaefer decided they are ready to make the change. I helped him complete the Change Form. They are moving from SECURE to CARE+ and changing from $1000 IUA to $2500 IUA for June 1st start date. It will remain Shaefer and his 2 kids on the membership. I sent a note to Patti to make sure the form is clear. She''s away and will see it next week. All set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-10 22:48:28', '2023-05-10 22:48:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119118121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104032', 'Clove Berger', NULL, '5-10-23 Clove needed CirrusMD for her daughter who has pink eye. I sent info via text to help her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-10 22:46:26', '2023-05-10 22:46:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108211002', 'Karen Sachs', NULL, '05.10.2023 Karen called looking for chiro sessions and how to get coverage. I explained the process of a referral from PCP, and a treatment plan from the chiro then uploading them into a medical need. I read a blurb from the Zion guidelines about the limited chiro sessions (25 max) and how all other chiro session requests would go under alternative need.
Karen is thinking about getting Kaiser as insurance and wondered how it would work with medical health sharing. I explained that the medical cost sharing part would always come in as 2nd. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 17:48:46', '2023-05-10 17:48:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119146065', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000087509002', 'Mark Carman', NULL, '5-10-2023:  Mark & Janalee called from Peru.  Their son has surgery on Tues when they are back home, but the surgeon is telling them they "don''t take Zion".  I did a ton of education:  remember the docs are thinking ''ins'', so we have to use diff vocab.  My sugg: call all entites (surgeon, anesthesiologist, etc) and tell them you don''t have ''ins'' & you need ''cash-pay'' estimates, with any ''cash-pay'' discounts, so you can get the money together.
     According to Mark, Zion has approved the surgery, they prev started the need, so I showed him how to use "Additional Doc Sub" in the toggle (he couldn''t get the computer to cooperate, so this was verbal) or if they have an e-mail address they can use that.  Once those items are submitted, it''s ok to bring to Zion''s attention those items were sent in & just remind Zion of the sensitivity of the timing. 
     If they have further questions, they''ll call back.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-10 16:40:24', '2023-05-10 16:49:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050186012', 'Jerry Bateman', NULL, '05.10.2023 Jerry Bateman while we were working with other members. So we missed his call. I called him in hopes that I can be of help. I left him a VM of my name, company and phone to reach us back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 16:33:17', '2023-05-10 16:33:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119146048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104457002', 'Normandie Rainwater', NULL, '5-10-2023:  James called thinking he was calling to confirm his appt for an injury.  I let him know we are not involved in that portion of his healthcare.  We talked about how to present, his 1k IUA, present as ''cash-pay'', ask for a discount, etc.  It''s a reinjury of an old item but he says it''s been 5 years ago w/no treatment/symptoms since (we did NOT disc pre-x phase-in...), we talked about PT, acupuncture req''ing prior auth  because that worked for him 5 years ago, etc.  He seemed to understand & will save receipts & detailed inv.  Knows to call us to learn how to sub his ''med need'' & there is a 6 mos deadline from 1st DOS to include the initial exp.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-10 14:00:18', '2023-05-10 14:16:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006617001', 'William Murdy', NULL, '05.10.2023 William called to understand why his blood thinning medication did not get covered, THIS TIME around. William is with liberty healthshare. I am not familiar at all with that plan, so I consulted with Cari and Jen via teams. Both ladies have not worked with Liberty Healthshare in over 1.5 years, so Jen consulted Wendy Scipione, the advisor. 
Where we are at with this now at 3:30PM ( William called an hour ago), I left William a VM saying to identify what card he presented for this matter/appointment/prescription purchase, and to let him know that it is a matter for RCI to have a conversation with. I left him their phone number as well, and asked him to call us back for further details and clarifications. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 13:34:24', '2023-05-10 14:31:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031359127', 'John Scarrow', NULL, '05.10.2023 VIA OUTLOOK, I emailed John information and options on the expensive medication, Wegovy for  2.4 MG, 4 injectables:
 I was able conjure up some options for this new medication Wegovy, through the discount pharmacy sites, our international shopper, and Sedera''s guidelines and Wegovy''s actual manufacturing website.
        The pharmacy discount sites did not offer any good coupons for Wegovy 2.4MG 4 injectables. However, I did attach the least expensive coupon that was generated and a Costco one, per your preference. 
Wegovy: 2.4 MG, 4 Injectables: Kroger = $1223.31
Wegovy: 2.4 MG, 4 Injectables: Costco = $1429.56
        Our international shopper does not source this medication, yet. We will keep trying him, if you request this medication again. Maybe we will get lucky, and he then will start sourcing it. 
        When I was running your prescription quote, I noticed the Wegovy is used for weight management.  Although I do not know if that''s what you are using it for or if this would be shareable, I found the following in the Sedera Member Guidelines:  "6.B.56. Weight Reduction Shareable only if prescribed by a licensed medical provider and a $3,000 maximum shareable amount per Member."
We can help you learn how to submit your receipts for this specific issue (doctor''s appointments receipt, etc.) to see if Sedera would consider this within that guideline.  Please call the Concierge Line M-F 9:00am-8:00pm Eastern 1-800-519-2969, for a video on how to submit a ''medical need'' to Sedera.  As expensive as this prescription is, reaching your $1500 issue specific IUA (Initial Unshareable Amount) should happen quickly, then if they share in some of the expense you will at least have a little help.
        As for the actual manufacturing website, they do offer expense coverage, but it looks like it''s only available for commercial insurance holders only.
I''ll wait for your response to proceed from there. I hope you''re having a great day. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 12:52:03', '2023-05-10 12:52:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119146035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113835002', 'Terry Draper', NULL, '5-10-2023:  Shelly called w/lots of questions:
     - ''Prev Care'':  annual (Doc curr shows in PHCS search, she will conf), mamm cntr (the name of the clinic shows in the PHCS search, but not spec "mamm".  She will call & find out.)
        Daughter works at PCP office, & they usually require an initial visit, which will not have the ''prev med coding'' on it.  --  Her daughter called her back & it sounds like the office will work with her on this, so it will be considered ''prev care''.
     - HSA: Choose any financial, Planstin card shows high ded.  
     - Maint Meds:  Showed her the form & went over best practices for getting her coupons.
     - ''Welcome Call'':  She found her post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail & I showed her some of the items in it.  It does not have the PHCS link, so I sent her the ''Prev Care'' template.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-10 12:42:54', '2023-05-11 10:03:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117965002', 'Kerri Lee Wemett', NULL, '05.10.2023 Kerri called to better understand about the waiting period for any lab work.
I consulted with Cari via teams, since the direct plan is not on my radar as often. She explained and I shared with Kerri that the Direct plan does not have help for preventative lab work, except for the pap smear.  For that, there is a 6-month waiting period. 
I offered Kerri to possible make use of the discount lab work site, JasonHealth.com, it turns out they are available with 2,300 labs in 47 states (all states except NY, NJ, RI). NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 12:21:07', '2023-05-10 12:21:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119137043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000053149054', 'shawn warner', NULL, 'Been actively trying to reach Shawn, regarding his membership. I''ve left messages and emailed him to return my call. No response.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-05-10 11:52:34', '2023-05-10 11:52:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119137038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028115365', 'Elizabeth Bennett', NULL, 'Been actively trying to reach Elizabeth to find out if she will be moving forward with a new enrollment. Can''t reach her, hasn''t returned a call since we spoke, and hasn''t responded or opened the email I sent.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-05-10 11:50:23', '2023-05-10 11:50:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119173040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006727', 'Charles Korb III', NULL, '5-10-23 Chuck updated his C4 account so we could both access it again prior to our call. He no longer has any income coming in and is sad to say, he needs Medicaid at this time. He really enjoyed working with me and was super complimentary. He offered suggestions over time which helped MPB to improve. I helped him update his income to $0 in Medicaid as of today, 5-10-23. He''s been retired for quite some time now and just needs the financial help with Medicaid. He knows he has to find a doctor who accepts Medicaid and prefers to find those who don''t Only accept Medicaid but accept a range of insurance. He will work on that on his end.  I also helped him to cancel MPB and he was complimentary on his form as well. If his income status changes, he''ll let me know right away and we can discuss a new path. However, do doesn''t anticipate that. He also knows the corruption in our gov and healthcare system now. His 88 year old mom recently tripped over a throw rug and hit her head on a mantel and banged up her face and hand. They went to Kaiser since it was the only option at night. They were there for 3 hrs and she got 5 stitches on her cheek and some on her hand. She''s on Medicare. But, they charged $37K!  He believes MCS and MPB are the way of the future to end this corruption and lack of transparency.  He sees the truth in what''s happening in our country and in the world. Very nice man.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-10 11:37:44', '2023-05-10 11:37:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119175012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114775002', 'Joshua Corvelli', NULL, '5/10/23 - noticed that Joshua has not completed his welcome call. I sent him a scheduler via email requesting that he do so soon. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-05-10 11:28:56', '2023-05-10 11:28:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119172008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080613002', 'Michael Van Horn', NULL, '05.10.2023 Michael was double checking if he has telehealth as part of his plan. I reassured him that he does, through CirrusMD. He already had the app downloaded, I sent him an invitation then he started the process of registering with them. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-05-10 11:19:14', '2023-05-10 11:19:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119146027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118211001', 'Kara Kelly', NULL, '5-10-2023:  Kara called.  When she called Mazz & Sull they told her they couldn''t find her employer.  We went over how the system is set-up to use MPB.Health or MPowering Benefits as the employer - she was totally open to calling them back w/that info.  If they give her the same response, she will ask them to call us so we can confirm she''s our memb & should have the service.
     - She''s looking for counseling for both her and her boyfriend (who is on this membership).
     - We walked in depth thru the MAP site & diff items available there too.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-05-10 11:05:06', '2023-05-10 11:11:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119167104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118196018', 'Amy Schecterson', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-05-10 10:59:01', '2023-05-10 10:59:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119173020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104184', '(Ronald) Shaefer Welch', NULL, '5-10-23 Shaefer, 38 and wife have chosen a local DPC to join and trying to lower their monthly membership fee for June 1st with that in mind.  Wife has other coverage.  I offered DIRECT and CARE+. He wants CARE+ since he''s not old enough to need a colonoscopy and obviously doesn''t need mammogram. He and kids can get their wellness through the DPC instead which he''s happy with. They will be paying $300 to DPC. With CARE+  EC at $1000/$420 or $2500/$320. He''s leaning towards $2500 IUA EC at $320 and realized the $5000 at $295 isn''t worth the small monthly savings. He''ll discuss with his wife and call me back to complete the Member Change Form.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-10 10:48:32', '2023-05-10 13:45:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119167093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116614002', 'Sydney E LaMorte', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-05-10 10:43:34', '2023-05-10 10:49:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119167088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116689001', 'Kathleen Weller', NULL, 'Spoke to member will book online the welcome call. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-05-10 10:36:15', '2023-05-10 10:36:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119173003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000085362001', 'Laura Plummer', NULL, '5-10-23 Laura just got laid off from her tech job. She will go back to self-employment and can show proof with 1099 or EIN. She does better as self-employed than working in corp world. No pre-x for any of them. She''s interested in Essentials for her husband to have virtual healthcare and Life Care.  I''m inquiring with the Admin Team as to how to include Essentials for husband. She wants a June 1st start date. Would prefer even sooner since she lost her benes as of May 1st. But, she can backdate Cobra is anything happens before June 1st. She''s considering SECURE $1000/$525 or $2500/$425. I will waive $100 since she was a client 2 years ago before she got her W2 job.  We will meet next Wed. to enroll after her husband has had time to review it all as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-10 10:31:37', '2023-05-10 10:31:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119167078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116768002', 'Solveig Johnson', NULL, 'Spoke to member will book online the welcome call. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-05-10 10:30:56', '2023-05-10 10:30:56'),
