  ('zcrm_1579374000119038006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000072425023', 'Lior Moshe', NULL, '05.08.23:  Was notified by Jeffrey that Adria called today upset and confused about her plan.  I called and got Lio but she got on the phone and said she was not able to speak now and asked if I could call her at 4:15 p.m. today at 404-429-3566 (I think this is her cell #).  I said I absolutely would.
Called Adria at 4:15 p.m.  We had a great conversation.  She was knowledgeable but frustrated with what she was experiencing w/Planstin and when she called Zion for answers they were not giving her what she needed.  She explained she now has  3-year old and 6-month old daughters, both of whom need frequent doctor visits for ear infections, one has a foot positioning issue that cost her $1200 so far to test and evaluate.  Says that because she uses the Planstin card for wellness visits (which doesn''t pay for most of the labs the doctor orders) even when she goes for a diagnostic visit and says she is self-pay, they insist on billing her through her Planstin insurance card and Planstin only pays for 20% of the need.  So her out-of-pocket seems to be much higher than it should be and she has a lot of administrative paperwork to do.  She''s thinking maybe she''d be better off taking her company''s health care plan (she is an attorney).  The monthly fee is a bit less than SECURE but her deductible is something like $18,000.
The options I suggested are:  
1.  Switch to our DIRECT plan and sign up with a DPC provider in her area, if there are any, to manage the children''s care.  That would probably be cheaper and give more protection.  And, if she doesn''t need an HSA, she still can use her free provider visit for a free wellnes visit and have the expensive screenings shared by Zion.
2.  Calculate the total amount she paid last year for her children''s visits (which will lessen as they get older) to see if it''s worth taking the health insurance instead.
3.  Set up and use her electronic medical vault to store all her family''s medical records and  receipts in one place.
She had to go but asked me to send her pricing to compare for DIRECT and SECURE, which I''m sending her tonight.  (DIRECT = $660; SECURE = $715)  We''ll continue our discussion to resolve her conflicts about the plan.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-05-08 10:54:54', '2023-05-17 10:40:42'),
