  ('zcrm_1579374000118487070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030630114', 'Elgin MacMillan', NULL, '04.29.2023 Elgin called to understand what health-sharing cards and paperwork he can discard throughout his spring cleaning.
I assured him, according to his CRM profile, he is now with Planstin for Preventative and Zion for medical cost sharing, and that he can discard his RCI card.
He wasn''t sure that he had preventative with his plan, so I briefly explained how his plan has three sections: Essentials, Preventative and Medical Cost Sharing.
He mentioned opening a medical need, so I offered to send him instructions on submitting bills to Zion, and he said he already spoke to Jen about a medical need, and that she''ll help him with it. Elgin was a pleasure to speak with. 
****************************************************************************************
Elgin called to let us know that he won''t need to open that medical need anymore, b/c after speaking with Jane Kassel, his advisor, she informed him that that incident is considered pre-existing for another year. He will take on the treatment that will hold him up till he can get the knee replacement. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-28 15:54:37', '2023-04-28 17:55:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118516008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '4-28-23 I called Elizabeth to get her payment updated. She''s recovering from her full knee replacement surgery and is just 2 weeks out. So, she''s behind on emails and everything and had no knowledge of any vm''s. She did find my email when I called her and she just updated her cc because the card expiration date had changed. She wants to keep using the cc since it''s a biz card and doesn''t want to give access to the company checking account.  She''s doing well and had fantastic care and now has 2 good knees for the rest of her life. She felt in excellent hands. Once the dust settles she''ll see what they still charge her.  She has a fantastic attitude and was very appreciative of my call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-28 15:45:40', '2023-04-28 15:45:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118487045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016111417', 'Dimitri Soris', 'SENT: Permission Form To Discuss MPB Plan w/ Christina 04.28.2023', '04.28.2023 Sister called trying to help Dimitri cause he''s been sick everyday. She is not on the plan nor has permission to speak to his plan. VIA OUTLOOK I SENT him the permission form to discuss MPB plan to fill out for Christina to have permission and help him, with the MultiPlan LInk and the list of PCP''s, which turned out to be the second one I''ve sent him. 
She mentioned he needed a new PCP. He has not had his welcome call yet to have the Multiplan link. So I SENT HIM the email via CRM to schedule his welcome call. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-28 14:33:55', '2023-04-28 15:01:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118487040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109390001', 'Jessica Houston', NULL, '04.29.2023 Jessica Houston returned Jen''s call back, since Jen reached out to clear the air re: the conversation via SalesIQ that Jessica had with one of our team members. 
Jen was with another valued member, and asked that she call Jessica back. As I finished sharing that part with Jessica (not knowing till later, it was a medical need she needed help with), she became strongly forward and aggressive by making statements along the line of we actually do not need to call her back,  she already spoke with Zion who has been helpful unlike us, and she has no idea who we even are and why we are even in the middle of all of it and not doing anything, brushing members off to go talk to Zion directly, what is our purpose and why she is even paying us if we are going to brush her off to Zion to open a need. She felt extremely comfortable with dismissing the efforts I was making to clarify our services at MPB, and especially as the Concierge Consulting Team specifically. 

I needed to go to lunch right after that call, so all documentation is being done via memory.

I was a little confused with her come back, her word choices and aggressive tone that kept on escalating. Each time I had a little space to share/clarify or even ask questions, she spoke over me with more escalation. I tried asking her, WHO was it that she spoke to that referred her to speak directly with Zion, but she kept saying she did not know and continued yelling and saying she doesn''t even know why she is paying us, if we are going to brush her off to Zion. I kept on trying to get space in to explain to her that THAT''s the total opposite of what our services are for, and that we would be happy to help her open a medical need, not to have Zion be the people to call, b/c they tend to confuse members with different information.....all in the meantime, she is cutting me off and choosing her emotions and the bad taste she experienced, with no resolution.
I finally asked her to stop yelling at me, and I did have to use a different tone myself to have her put a pause on they way she was speaking. She was not letting up. After a few times sharing that she is not to be yelling and speaking to us in that manner, I let her know that I''ll need to let her go and we can talk another time. All the while she''s still yelling and speaking over me saying that I have not let her get a word in. 
***THIS IS NOT ok. I will not be subject to abuse from anyone I work for, I work with nor members who are affiliated. NT ***', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-28 13:48:28', '2023-04-28 15:49:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118511019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109390001', 'Jessica Houston', NULL, 'Jessica reached out to me via SalesIQ needing assistance with a claim she needed to submit. Her daughter ended up needing to go to the ER from which the Urgent Care they sent her daughter to. Jessica said she had a link to file the claim but needed her member number to do so. I got some further detail on what type of claim this was for, so I would be able to determine the correct department/organization to send her to. Whether that be Zion or Planstin. Zion is who she needed so I let Jessica know I will be sending her the How to submit bills to Zion email with the link to submit the claims, and Zion''s phone #. 

Jessica seemed to be getting confused with who everybody is in terms of departments and providers with her plan. I was telling her exactly what needs to be done for the situation her daughter was dealing with at the ER, and that Zion Health is the people she needs to speak to about all of this. Jessica wasn''t understanding why she needs to speak to Zion Health, then she just demanded me to give her member number, to which I explained Zion is the one that has a member number for all of this and to call them. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-04-28 13:46:27', '2023-04-28 13:46:27'),
