  ('zcrm_1579374000118384077', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118826002', 'Cathy Baker', NULL, '4-27-23 Cathy is 62 and David is 67. David is getting laid off and they will lose their health ins. She says it will cost her $1200 via C4 for just her. He will need to move to Medicare. She is healthy, but may need a cataract surgery in the next few years. I will give her the Sharing Guideline stipulations for that. She also takes hormone replacements such as progesterone and a patch. No tobacco ever. She''s a part-time W2 employee and no other side income. She''s due for her colonoscopy and might try to get it before her plan ends. She did her mammogram in Jan. already.   She sees a NP that is more holistic in her approach and she pays $380 cash on her own. I let her know preventative items will be her responsibility to pay for. She understands and realizes that it probably makes more sense to go with CARE+ than DIRECT as long as she does her colonoscopy before she loses her current plan. She thinks it ends May 31st.  She also sees a dermatologist every 4 months and will pay cash for that as well. Next appt scheduled for next Thurs. Looking at a June 1st start date for CARE+ $1000/ $265.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-27 15:34:08', '2023-04-27 15:49:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118398044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061522143', 'Steve Remmel', NULL, '04.27.2023 Steve called to understand why Planstin is not paying for his wife, Souraya''s (who has been on the plan since November) mammogram. Planstin claimed Souraya is not on his plan, but CRM and Admin123 both show that she is.
 guided Steve to check his email from Planstin during her addition to the plan. That possibly the information from THAT card is what should be shared with the mammogram facility.
Steve, found the email, the PDF version card and was sounding relieved. I recommended he get off the phone with me, call the facility instead or wife, and have the latest card information.
*******************************************************************************************
Steve called back suggesting that we call Planstin. I three-way called us with Planstin, I spoke with Celeste, I shared the above with her, she verified his membership and did see that Souraya should have been added months ago, and she did see there was a removal of a member at that same time. Celeste needed to double check with a team member/platform, and put me on hold. At that time, I brought Steve in (merged calls), so he''s not holding by himself. Upon Celeste''s return, she said it should''ve updated in the system months ago, but they are looking into that right now. Presently, Celeste will update the numbers by back-dating it, so it''ll be up to date and  Souraya can get her mamm covered TODAY. Steve was planning on calling his wife right after that call. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-27 15:15:56', '2023-04-27 17:59:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118398039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086223002', 'Adam Kobler', NULL, '04.27.2023 Adam emailed me today with the following question, "My GP thought it would be a good idea for me to start getting regular skin checks at a dermatologist and wrote me a referral to go to a dermatologist of my choice. Is that some thing that would be completely or partially covered under my plan?"
After consulting and confirming with Zion''s guidelines and Jen via teams, I responded with, "After researching the Zion guidelines on their page, and double checked with my trainer for clarification, it is with discomfort that I share, unfortunately, nothing dermatologically associated is considered shareable, as of 04.27.2023. This is unless it is determined that the dermatological issue is part of an already approved a large need (a.k.a. car catastrophe, cancer ...).Please give us a call at the concierge line with anymore questions about your plan through us at MPB."   -   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-27 15:07:45', '2023-04-27 15:07:45'),
