  ('zcrm_1579374000117959013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117525128', 'Brian Gould', NULL, '4-18-23 Brian let me know his payment just went through with Friday Health today even though I received a denial letter today to reinstate his policy. Yesterday he got his insulin for $3! We have no idea what''s happening. I don''t know anyone who gets insulin for $3. He thinks it was run without insurance since he had been denied. He''s good for 1 more month now. He will review the MCS video to see if that''s an option in case Friday drops him again. He''ll have to find out what month his payment went towards or then he wants a reimbursement if they won''t reinstate him. It''s super bizarre. He''ll let me know what he wants to do moving forward. Brian''s account shows as cancelled for 1/31/23. So, if they accepted a payment, it''s probably only for February, not March or April. So, he''s probably not in the clear yet.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-18 17:23:18', '2023-04-18 17:49:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117971073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115751002', 'Rocio Borzage', NULL, '04.18.2023
Sent RX request form and change form to update the email on profile right now, via CRM.
William''s main concern was, since he is still with a CA Blue Shield High deductible plan, and transitioning out to our plan, what would be considered primary or secondary.
I explained that MCS is always going to be secondary, but then he asked what if I don''t even reach my deductible in my other insurance in order to even make use of the MCS with Zion.
At this point, I consulted with Cari via teams, and we both agreed that Whitney Kline, his advisor, needs to go over his options again, not send him to the Concierge for those kind of answers.
If Cari was not working tonight, this would have been a call I''d need to call the member back for answers, when all along it is something the advisor should be checking off their lists with new members. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-18 17:19:45', '2023-04-18 17:54:18'),
