  ('zcrm_1579374000117798155', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060779263', 'Catherine Collins', NULL, '04.13.2023 Catherine called because she was having a hard time accessing her member portal account. I tried her credentials and I was able to log in just fine. I asked her to make sure that she is clicking "sign in" at the appropriate site, Member Portals from the member portals and updates page. It turns out that she was clicking on the telehealth service instead :). In the end, she was able to access her portal for her payment history. I asked her if she received the Planstin email for her 1095, she hadn''t checked, so I guided her to search for it via her email and the word Planstin, and she found exactly what she needed for her taxes that she didn''t know was in her email.
Catherine is pleasant and receptive and was a delight to speak to.   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-13 17:19:12', '2023-04-13 17:19:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117798141', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117650002', 'Paul Copeland', NULL, '04.13.2023 Paul called to reschedule his call with Vanessa on Monday, cause he realized he needed to have the call after his plan has started. I emailed him a rescheduling link.
I messaged Cari and Vanessa via teams for confirmation and to give Vanessa the heads up. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-13 16:03:59', '2023-04-13 16:03:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117798131', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105234001', 'Brianna Krampetz', NULL, '04.13.2023 Brianna called to attain her 1095. I guided her to her email, to search for Planstin, and it was the first email that came up. She is going to register and follow the email''s instructions.
She then asked about having an RX filled/refilled and how to go about doing that. I guided her to a few options including seeing her PCP, but I recommended to start with telehealth, CirrusMD. I explained that they do have some boundaries to abide by when it comes to controlled substances and antibiotics, depending on the situation and meds. She said she will try that out. I offered to show her where to find the forms on Member Portals and Updates, but she requested to have it sent to her so she has it on hand and accessible. I emailed her both the Member Portals and Updates website, and the RX Request Form. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-13 15:56:35', '2023-04-13 15:56:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117798115', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044061129', 'Emily Kloser', NULL, '4-13-2023:  Emily called to see what kind of help we can give her.  Nahla was at lunch, so I took the call.  It''s the first time I''ve spoken w/her directly.  In our meeting today, we tried to address the Redirect issue, but it was the wrong format.  Jennifer is starting a ticket re: Emily''s Redirect issue.  Here''s what I learned from Emily & Redirect''s Cielo :
     - Emily had forgotten that Jennifer trans her to Redierct clear back on 1/25/23.  Emily had set-up a time for Redirect to call her back on her phone # because her husb doesn''t answer.  She & her husband waited & waited for that call (both there because the claim is on him & he needed to verbally give perm for her to take care of).  
     - Did conference call w/Emily into Redirect.  Cielo (female) answered.  She first said we called & called you, but it just went straight to VM.  When I asked, it turns out they were not calling the # req''d, but her husb''s ph.  Cielo is able to see the claim, but they will not pay until they can have (their new review w/the member type process) the call to confirm the expenses.  This really frustrated Emily because the doc''s office is getting super snippy w/them, they live in a sm community, & it''s making them look bad.
     - I got Cielo to e-mail a ''permission to discuss'' form to Emily''s husb so he can give perm for the file, which Emily agreed to return immed, & Cielo''s sending a separete e-mail to the call back dept telling them this is Urgent.  Emily''s super upset because their next available call time is 4/26/23 & Emily says absolutely not - she has no idea where she''ll be (they live in an area where cell srvc is spotty).  Since Emily cannot sched a time, Cielo can now only send an e-mail to the correct dept asking them to call Emily - we confirmed she has Emily''s corr ph # for the return call!
     - Unpaid bill is for $792
     - I let both Emily & Cielo know our team is creating a ticket, letting the powers that be know this is an issue.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-04-13 15:19:14', '2023-04-13 16:08:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117798110', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037788057', 'Jean Thompson', NULL, '04.13.2023 Jean called to check on specifics for getting a mammogram. She asked if 3D imaging is covered, and I said only 2D is. She asked if MRI is covered, I told her that will fall under the medical cost sharing umbrella. I consulted with Jen and Cari via teams, and they both confirmed the above.
They also shared that it is possible (due to a previous member''s story), to contact Sedera regarding the 3D imaging, to see if a medical need would cover it. With that spear heading the process, discuss the MRI as part of the need as well, due to her doctor''s orders and support in preventing her family''s history to be repeated.
We decided that Jean is best to discuss getting coverage with Sedera, for the MRI and 3D imaging mammogram, through the lens of her family history and the support of her doctor. I direct transferred Jean to Sedera, 855-973-3372. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-13 13:54:19', '2023-04-13 13:54:19'),
