  ('zcrm_1579374000117809019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111874002', 'Karin Lemke', NULL, '4-12-2023:  Karen called.  She was very coy about telling me details, esp in the beginning.  From what I can tell, the end of Feb she started having over active bladder symptoms, so it doesn''t curr sound like pre-x, but I warned her, it will be dependent on her MD''s records.  I sent her the temp for sub a ''med need'' and we walked thru everything together.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-04-12 12:56:36', '2023-04-20 01:18:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117809014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810668', 'Rosalie Chilcoat', NULL, '4-12-2023:  Rosalie contacted us thru SalesIQ.  Unfortunately, she was give inaccurate info regarding her request.  I called & let Rosalie know I wanted to provide some corrected info.  
     - Rosalie is someone who likes nothing, as best I can tell.  She thinks MPB is too difficult, says nothing ever works out, hates instructions via video (ie: sub a need to Sedera), if the chat gives wrong info than why do you have it, I don''t think anything I said was not met with a complaint.
     - I apologized to Rosalie & let her know I thought it was just someone not realizing she was an older member & on Sedera, but that I''ve sent her instructions on sub a ''med need'' to Sedera e-mail w/video instructions.  She knows if she needs help sub that ''need'', Sedera can help her.
     - She says she gets frustrated with our ''prev care'' (she''s w/RCI) because what they paid last year they didn''t this yr.  As she tells it, she had a colonoscopy & the anesthesiology was not paid, but other portions were.  I asked if they were in network & she said yes.  She says they told her because a polyp was pulled, that''s why they didn''t pay that amt.  (I went into the polyp moves this to diagnostic...)  She said they put me under & did the colonoscopy BEFORE they pulled they polyp, so they did finally pay for it, but I had to fight them & they always pay incorrectly.
        Part of the issue here as I see it:  she has that huge 5k IUA, so if it moves to diagnostic, she owes a ton of money.
     - Her intention for her chat, according to her, was to get help finding a high quality ortho surg for knee replacement.  I tried to show her HCBB, but it would not allow her, me, or even Jennifer tried to register her.  I sub the following ticket asking for help:

Tckt #2597:
HCBB Access - Rosalie Chilcoat
12 Apr 2023 02:42 PM

Cari Adams-Waneka:
Rosalie is trying to figure out a good surgeon for knee replacement in her area.  

We (Rosalie, Cari, & even Jennifer) all tried to register her w/HCBB & we cannot get her access. 
