  ('zcrm_1579374000117526176', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099129002', 'Mark Glass', NULL, '04.10.2023 Mark called to get clarification on how to present himself in either type of appointments: Preventative & Medical Cost Sharing. I had sent him a list of PHCS providers in the past for neurologists and PCP''s.
For preventative I explained to Mark:
-Present himself as covered under Planstin and share the information behind the card 
-Providers/Facilities...etc must be in the PHCS network
-Appointment must remain preventative, be sure to share with the doc/office
-Only Lipid Panels are covered
For Medical Cost Sharing I explained to Mark:
-The difference between a deductible and an IUA
-The difference between a claim/case and a Medical Need Request (MNR)
-Pay as close as possible towards the IUA, and call us to see about opening a MNR
-Save all receipts and invoices/bills for the same issue

Mark was pretty knowledgeable of his plan, despite that he is new, but wanted to make sure he understood the functions and processes better when visiting either a PCP or a specialist.
We briefly spoke about our RX program, because he mentioned OptumRX from the back of his card.      NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-10 14:55:54', '2023-04-10 15:11:22'),
