  ('zcrm_1579374000117394009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105652002', 'Anthony Jogoleff', NULL, '4-6-2023:  Ashley called &amp; caught me.  With the weekend coming, I just took the RX Quote info over the phone because they are headed to pick up these items once Anthony is released.  Here''s what I sent:
     - Pantoprazole (=gen Protonix) 40mg, #84 tab = $16.72 at Rite Aid on RXGo  [2d x 6 wks = 42ds]
     - Scuralfare (=gen Carafate) 1gm, #120 tabs = $21.33 at Rite Aid on GoodRX [4d = 30ds]
Prev they''ve been using CVS, but it was $50+ &gt; in price, so they chose Rite Aid.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-04-06 16:49:29', '2023-04-06 16:49:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117395043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '4-6-23  From Glen Becker as possible options to help with her member responsibility. Sedera will only pay for half of her 2nd knee replacement surgery!  They may stick her with $25K+ bill!!! I''m looking for solutions.  Here are some ideas. If these don''t work, we can tap into Redirect''s resources as well as a next step.

For the situation described below (single member household, $80k/year income) – her income as a percentage of the Federal Poverty Level (which is how hospitals determine eligibility) is 548% FPL. There are very few hospitals that offer FA (Financial Assistance) discounts to patients with income over 400/500% FPL outside of major metropolitan areas like NYC, LA, or Chicago.
We did not able to find any information regarding financial assistance on the website for The Steadman Clinic, but did find a Financial Assistance Policy for Steadman Philippon Surgery Center - https://www.steadmanphilipponsurgerycenter.com/patient-resources/financial-assistance.
This policy states that patients are eligible for discounts up to 400% of the Federal Poverty Level, and also states that patients won’t be charged more than 20% of annual income.
I’m not sure if the Surgery Center FA Policy applies to The Steadman Clinic, but it’s likely worth exploring, as it could reduce the bill down to $16k from $25k.
One other item to consider is that the surgery center’s policy requires residency in “Roaring Fork Valley” in order to qualify. I’m not sure if the member lives there or not.
We looked into Vail Health’s FA Program as well and found that they offer 50% discounts to patients up to 550% FPL, but this only applies to patients without insurance.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-06 16:38:52', '2023-04-06 16:38:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117389045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025283259', 'Julie Oldham', NULL, '04.06.2023 Julie called asking what app are we using for telehealth now, and I said we are using CirrusMD. She said cause it used to be Teledoc.
I offered to send her an invitation link, but she already had an account (seemed like), and wanted to change the passcode. She said she will try that and give us a call back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-06 15:49:00', '2023-04-06 15:49:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117389034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116266002', 'Edee Yuen', NULL, '04.06.2023 Edee is seeking a preventative doctor but wants to use the one she''s been seeing.
She visited the Zion website and learned about their preventative services/options, and wanted to see if she can use her preventative through them. I urged her to not view their options, as they are different and separate from the services/elements she has in her plan with MPB.
She proceeded to share that she was told she can use whoever doctor she wanted, since her doctor is not in the PHCS network, by Jeffrey Bursteen. 
I consulted with Jen and Cari via teams on this, and then I messaged Jeffrey via teams to see if he can help Edee.
Jeffrey was able to connect with Edee, and according to his teams messages to me "I took care of Edee, thank you for the heads up". NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-06 13:36:37', '2023-04-06 16:30:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117389029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105652002', 'Anthony Jogoleff', NULL, '04.06.2023 Ashley called to learn how to get coverage for an RX for her husband who is in the hospital.
I shared usually we searched discounted sites and offer a coupon of at least 75%, or check with an international shopper. However if he''s in the hospital it could be added to the medical need.
I told her I wanted to consult with my trainer on this, just in case. She said she''s been working with Jennifer, but has not opened a medical need.
I consulted with Jen and Cari via teams, and Cari shared that in order for the medicine to be covered in medical needs, they would need to be considered one of the treatments IN THE HOSPITAL.
So I shared with Ashley that we can research their medicine and send a coupon, we are OFF TOMORROW (EASTER), so have it in soon so we can get it out by the end of today. Ashley did not have the med info complete with her, so she went to get it and call us back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-06 12:54:52', '2023-04-06 12:54:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117389021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108509002', 'Ariel Rudland', NULL, '04.06.2023 Ariel called back regarding the above concern, again. I needed to consult with my team to learn more up to date information on the RPB concept with Planstin. 
