  ('zcrm_1579374000117322008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991117', 'Ryan Dunlap', NULL, '4-5-2023:  Called Ryan to let him know the refunds req''d were auth today, so he should see them in the near future.  He was thrilled.  He asked for the person he should tt re: our curr products.  See e-mail below sent to confirmed e-mail address w/info.  Do mention to make sure no new pre-x considerations w/advisor.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-04-05 17:15:22', '2023-05-22 10:34:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117296033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081677002', 'William Fox', NULL, '04.05.2023 William called asking for a card replacement. He could not tell me which card he lost. His tone, demeanor and responses were short, not helpful ("uh I dunno!" "uh, I dunno my insurance care", " I dunno I''m not a tech guy, I do stone".....etc), lost card
contacted Planstin
Yvette answered, put me on a brief hold, she came back saying "what''s a good call back number for me?" I answered her, then I said, "you know usually they just ask for the member''s first and last name and their bday" she said "Oh ok, what is the members first and last name"...I gave them, "what is the birthday?" I gave that too. She said "Ok thank you we will get him a card..." I cut her off, gingerly, so she does not hang up so quickly, as she seemed in a hurry to let me go, and asked her "can we confirm his email really quick?" She confirmed the email that WE have on file and the one he confirmed is correct. I said "Thank you and have a good night." NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-05 16:41:53', '2023-04-05 16:47:04'),
