  ('zcrm_1579374000117276034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089146002', 'Pamela Garrett', NULL, '04.05.2023 Pamela called today with unfortunately and delicate news. She learned in the recent past that she is 14 weeks pregnant. Today, she is possibly facing a miscarriage, given her doctor''s observation (unsure if in person or telehealth). Doc said go to ER to confirm. If so they will schedule a DNC. She has not had her first appointment yet, nor has a medical need  open yet.
I emailed her the directions to submitting bills on Zion, and was listening to her wishes to wanting to get the ball rolling on getting coverage. I was uncomfortable for Pamela and did not feel filling out a need NOW was right. I consulted with Cari and Jen via teams, and both urged that Pamela go to the ER right away, and we can always help her after the fact with all the steps with getting coverage.
I coached Pamela on how to present herself towards medical cost sharing with Zion:
1-Present as cash-pay patient and request the cash-pay discount
2-Pay as close as possible to the $1000 IUA
3-Collect all paperwork, preferably in PDF form for her ease later. 

Pamela was emotional but soft spirited, and I am wishing she is well and will call us back with different news.  NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-05 13:23:12', '2023-04-05 15:22:45'),
