He asked if he could call us back, should there be more questions or come across any snags. I said of course, anytime. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-05 11:36:48', '2023-04-05 11:36:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117261043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115820002', 'Adam Schwindt', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule online the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-04-05 11:12:03', '2023-04-05 11:12:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117261033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000085687002', 'Danielle Howley', NULL, '4-5-2023:  Danielle said Martin is on the way to the ER (I think she said his PCP sugg he head there) for what are cardiac symptoms).  They are in the car & I told her how to present: no ''ins'', no card to present, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, offer to pay your $2500 IUA & ask them to bill them for the bal while they get the money together & save inv, receipts, & call us when Martin is settled to sub a ''med need''.  Also, told her how to handle it if they send in the financial asst team.  She was thankful, knowing how to handle the various situations.  
     However, I told her the big thing now is to focus on Martin.  We can take care of the details once he a bit settled.  I let her know we''ll show her how to sub the ''med need'' w/pymt receipts, inv, etc.  & the sooner the better so we can get approval for the pymt over her IUA.
     According to her, Martin has never had cardiac issues before, so it shouldn''t be pre-x.  [Even if it is, at least they are in yr 2 of their memb.]    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-04-05 11:08:41', '2023-04-05 12:09:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000117276008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779071', 'Ruth Glas', NULL, '04.05.2023 Ruth called to learn the best way to maneuver towards and through her preventative care, specifically a mamm screening.
Ruth was ready to pay out of pocket, and presented as self-pay, to the facility that she is comfortable going to for years. 
I explained at first  that should she want to go the out of pocket journey, it would be best to present as ''cash-pay'' vs. ''self-pay'', and request the ''cash-pay discount''. I explained that from 
 what I understand, self-pay is for those without coverage, and we will circle back to this in a second.
Then I proceeded to look up the facility of her choosing; Akron General Medical Center - zip code:44307. We found over 300 under that zip code in that exact address that she confirmed it would b at. She was glad she can use Planstin for the place she''s been using for years.
We circled back to presenting as ''Cash-pay'', and I said to make sure to tell the facility that her appointment needs to stay preventative. In the outcome that the screening finds something, it will automatically evolve into diagnostic, which then will move us in the direction of medical cost sharing, WITH ZION. That would be an appropriate time to plug in the presentation as a ''cash-pay'' patient and request the ''cash-pay'' discount.
Ruth is fairly new, but is receptive, proactive and seems to be a good listener to the directions. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-04-05 10:52:33', '2023-04-05 11:06:53'),
