  ('zcrm_1579374000116889013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504066', 'Deborah Madsen', NULL, '3-30-23 There are other emails associated with her account. But, she just called me in a bit of a panic. However, she admitted she missed the part at the end of the email stating she won''t pay over the $500 IUA. They are still in negotiations with Steadman''s. She hasn''t heard back from Mikey or another woman on her case. I advised her to give them a little time to complete the negotiations process. She doesn''t need to get  a lawyer bc they are saying they will pay the amount above her $500 IUA. She just has to give them time to do part of the process. She said other than this they''ve been incredible up to now. It seems Steadman''s newly has a target on its back with their pricing. However, Steadman''s has been incredible with self-pay huge discounts. So, we need to give this time to get resolved and paid out. She will keep me in the loop in case I need to step in later.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-30 09:46:47', '2023-03-30 09:47:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116889008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504066', 'Deborah Madsen', NULL, '3-30-23 
Dear Mikey,

I have researched the code 64493 and code 64494 and typically the cost is between $3570.00 and $3500.00. This cost may vary between $300-400.00 per injection. The Steadman Clinic gave me a self pay discount of $9243.00 for 4 injections.

My cost was 4977.00 which I paid directly. Each injection was discounted greatly. You are saying that the cost is typically 1600 per injection and this is far less than that.

That being said I had many conversations with Sedera about having this procedure. I asked repeatedly if I should get a second opinion and was told this was not necessary, that I would be covered. I did not want to add to the cost by getting another MRI so I requested we not do another one.

I would not have had this done at all if I know I was going to encounter these issues.

I am currently pain free so having this procedure has worked and was necessary. I am hoping to get this situation resolved as I have these charges on my credit card. Please let me know how to proceed.

Thank you for taking the time with this.

Regards,

Deborah Madsen


Hey Deborah,

I think there may be some confusion here. There are currently 2 separate bills uploaded to your Needs case. One bill is from Basalt Orthopedic Surgery Center for what appear to be facility fees for your injections. This seems to be the bill to which you are referring but is not the bill that is currently in negotiations. 

The original charge for the Basalt Orthopedic Surgery Center bill was $14,220.00 for which you received a $9,243.00 and paid $4,977.00. The balance for this bill/provider is now $0 and as such, is not eligible for negotiations. The $4,977.00 that you paid has been processed to share to you at the end of this week.

Also uploaded is a bill from the Steadman Clinic. This bill is for physician fees for your injections and includes dates of service 03/06/2023 & 3/10/2023. This is the bill in negotiations. The original balance for these two dates of service, for physician''s fees only, was another $4,762.00 and included a self-pay discount of $644.00 leaving you a balance of $4,118.00. You made payment of $2,760.50 and, as far as the statement goes, still have a balance with Steadman Clinic of $1,357.50. 

The $2,760.50 that you paid to Steadman Clinic has also been processed to share to you at the end of the week. All that is being negotiated is the remaining $1,357.50 that has not been paid in an attempt to mitigate the costs if at all possible.

The total cost, for facility and physician fees for your 4 injections, according to the 2 bills that are uploaded is $9,095.00. Point Health determined a fair price of $1,600 for all of the physicians fees (your bill is for $4,118.00). Steadman Clinic also only offered a $644.00 discount. 
 
The total fair price that I determined, for both physician & facility fees per injection, in your area, is $1,395.00 which is about $5,500 in aggregate. 

That said, there is no issue. Negotiations are standard protocol with inflated bills and part of every member''s responsibility to one another. You will only be responsible for your $500.00 IUA for this Needs case. Any amount charged or paid in excess of $500.00 will be eligible to share with the community, regardless of whether or not a settlement offer is accepted.

I hope this information is helpful. You can schedule a call directly on to my calendar using the following link if you would like additional clarification: https://mnunez.youcanbook.me/

Kindly,
Mikey Nunez

Needs Coordinator
