  ('zcrm_1579374000116834033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109179002', 'Corey Vincent', NULL, '03.28.2023 Corey called wanting to know if the heart monitor device that his wife was just prescribed, is covered. At first they put her to monitor her heart rate/rhythm via her smart watch for 30 days. They found some irregularities, then wanted her to use a portable battery powered device that connects to her chest, and the dr. office gave them a cellphone-like device for monitoring. Corey was wondering if that would be covered under Zion.
Sent instruction to open a medical need with Zion
I explained the medical cost sharing process to presenting and getting covered. Then, I explained his $5000 IUA to him. He understood that he needs to reach the $5000 first before the medical cost sharing kicks in. 
I also explained that Zion has a strict deadline of submitting bills in order to get covered, and that is six months from the initial visit.
Then he asked what if we don''t open it now, just to see what the results are, they don''t see anything now, BUT at the end of the year something shows up. Can we add our visit this month to the the open need at the end of the year (more than 6months)?
I spoke with Cari for more clarification on how to guide Corey. She shared that there are some advisors who offer a companion product to help with the 5k IUA.
Cari also explained that already haven had seen a doctor re: his wife''s heart condition monitoring DURING the HIGH IUA, will be the same amount of IUA for THAT SPECIFIC issue, even if he lowers his IUA. (I did not get to share THIS PART with him)
*****************************************************************************************
I called Corey back around 5:30 and explained the above re: how his advisor, Analisa Cleland, most likely can offer a companion product to help with the 5k IUA. He did share that he has a separate companion offer that Analisa told him would compliment his plan with us, but he was unsure as to how it supports him in coverage, and specifically how it interacts with his IUA. 
I suggested that he contact Analisa to confirm that, just so you knows where he stands, SHOULD a catastrophe or a high medical cost sharing takes place. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-29 12:35:21', '2023-03-29 17:47:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116835013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011659413', 'Brad Uhlig', NULL, '3-29-2023:  Brad''s son is at school in OK & had to go to the ER - they aren''t seeing anything so they want to do a catscan.  I looked up fair price in that area & made suggestions.  He has the 5k IUA, so I sugg he ck w/Analisa to see if his companion accident policy might help pay that portion.  He will call us w/in the next 4 mos if it looks like this will be on going to sub the ''med need'', even if they aren''t at the 5k yet.  He did present at the ER as ''cash-pay'', but that visit alone may take them to or over the 5k mark.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-29 12:25:25', '2023-03-29 12:25:25'),
