  ('zcrm_1579374000116835008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108409002', 'Alan Monte', NULL, '3-29-2023:  Rebekah called.  Alan had a bad accident yesterday & emergency surgery today.  She gave them her MPB.Health card, so we went over how to handle instead.  She will go back to hosp & let them know that''s not an ''insurance'' card.  Let them know she does not have ''ins'', is ''cash-pay'', ask for a ''cash-pay'' disc, that they should offer to pay their 1k IUA, get a pymt receipt, etc.  She will call us in the next few days so we can show her how to sub a ''med need''.  She''s headed back to the hospital right now & knows we''ll want to start this asap, but to take care of Alan & herself for now.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-29 11:52:00', '2023-03-30 01:00:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116783016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116830026', 'Rob Roth', NULL, '3-29-23 Rob came to me via ASHI. He''s 51, wife 50 and son 20. He''s getting kicked off of Medicaid at the end of April. He looked into Healthcare.gov and never heard back from them. But, his income is expected to be about $30K annually including wife''s income. So, he will be best served with APTC through Healthcare.gov. With SECURE the price at $1000 is $915 which is not feasible for him. They do their annual wellness visits and used to have an HSA a while back. Super nice and appreciative of my time.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-29 11:40:42', '2023-03-29 11:40:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116834016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041020063', 'Mitchell Bloom', NULL, '03.29.2023 Mitchell called concerned, cause he thought they were cancelled. He said that he could not see payments coming out of his bank account, and that he called Zion, they said that they do not deal with billing and transferred him to Planstin, and Planstin transferred him to us. He does not know if they could see him as a member, when I asked him.
I search for him here, and it says he IS cancelled. I searched for him in ADMIN123, and AMY (spouse) Bloom came up instead. I confirmed with Cari via teams, and she said to go by Admin123 as it is primary, and CRM is secondary.
Mitchell wanted to learn more about using his plan, specifically preventative, and I shared with him that it looks like they are signed up under a DPC and that the preventative care would fall under the services of that provider. He said they were not happy with the services they were getting from the one "Concierge Doctor", so they cancelled.
I consulted with Cari via teams again, since I don''t deal with a lot of DPC members, and she asked the same questions and led to how it would be covered, should the members NOT have a DPC.
I was not able to relay that information from texting in teams, since I we were still talking, and Mitchell decided it was best to maybe change plans, and requested to see the details of his plan. He tried logging into his portal, but he did not have his log in information. I told him what he would find in his portal, and the details are on a main page that I could lead him to, but THEN he decided he needed to speak with his advisor to revisit the type of plan they are on. I gave him Wendy''s name and number, and he wanted to call her himself. 
 Cari & I will connect w/Dayra to correct the CRM numbers to match Admin123. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-29 11:09:15', '2023-03-29 16:45:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116834008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105466010', 'Anna Marie Somera', NULL, '03.28.2023 Anna Marie called to reinforce her knowledge of the process of getting covered for a Preventative Well Woman Visit. I explained:
1-When you call to make the apt, share that you are with Planstin, offer them their information, let them know that this visit needs to remain PREVENTATIVE ONLY.
2-EXAMPLE: The only lab test we are seeing get covered is the lipid panel. Therefore if there are lab-tests that the doctor wants you to complete, ask them to bill you separately. Present as a cash-pay patient for those items, and request the cash-pay discount.
3-EXAMPLE: Same with prescriptions, ask them to separate them. I remembered a KEY POINT and had to call her back, left her a VM, telling her to actually ask the doctor''s office how they would like to handle the RX requests.
Anna Marie understands her plan and how the basics function including IUA''s purpose, and asked if the separated items would go under the medical cost sharing. I affirmed that she''s on the right track, however, given that it is not large enough to be shared, it''ll be out of pocket. She''ll need to save the receipts, just in case the results of the test come back with leading information. I reminded her that when it comes to items like this that are neither preventative nor large enough to be shared, one can use their HSA.
She wanted to know what exactly would be covered in the WWV, and I guided her to her POST WELCOME EMAIL, and to the HealthCare.gov site.
She asked if there were any new updates about the RPB, I simply told her that AO yesterday, the only information was that IT MIGHT be rolling out on the 1st of April, but that''s a Saturday I told her, so maybe let it be just that they''re still working on it.
She was receptive, studious of her plan and seems to be moving in the right direction. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-29 10:54:01', '2023-03-29 10:56:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116835003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108662001', 'Juan Soto', NULL, '3-29-2023:  Azucena called.  She just had her annual phys &amp; the doc wants her to have her mamm &amp; her bone density tests.  She used to be on Redirect, so has never done the scheduling before.  I let her know there is possibility that our ''prev care'' thru Planstin may change re: ntwk in the next few days.  She offered to call us back late next week or the week after to see how she should proceed regarding which providers to see &amp; how to present.  I told her late next week would be perfect.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-29 10:34:27', '2023-03-29 10:34:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116834003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036530449', 'Emily Jaynes', NULL, '03.29.2023 Emily called and asked to speak to Cari. I checked our teams chat to let Cari know, and according to yesterday''s notes taken, we are still waiting on information to clarify this with Emily. So I let her know that we will get back to her. Emily was patient, kind and receptive regarding this matter. 
*****************************************************************************************
I called Emily back per Cari''s coaching, after she found out more information on RCI and the 1095 tax forms. I was not able to reach Emily, so I left her a VM sharing "I have some information for you regarding RCI and the 1095 tax forms. Please give me, or any of us a call back at 800-519-2969."
*****************************************************************************************
Emily called back and I was able to give her the information Cari shared, re: RCI + 1095 Tax Forms:  
1-Our representative, benefits administrator, contacted RCI to discuss the  1095 situation for the requesting members. It turns out that RCI had not prepared the tax forms
2-They requested a tax extension
3-They had offered inaccurate information about us no needing them to prepare the tax forms
4-Still waiting to identify the $/month RCI component.
Emily thought that she should file an extension herself, while she is waiting on RCI and us to provided her with the needed information. I concurred with her on that decision to stay in good standing with the IRS. 
*****************************************************************************************
Emily called back again requesting an email explaining what we discussed, per her husband''s request. I let her know I will speak to my trainer and benefits administrator to help generate that. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-29 10:21:08', '2023-03-29 17:27:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116806036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000101333002', 'Johnathan ONeal', NULL, 'Heather called in and said that she was filling out a form for Maternity Leave and needed her member number to put down. I just wanted to confirm so I didn''t provide her with the wrong info, so I asked Patti here how to go about that. I let her know that would be through Zion Health, as they are the one that will be taking care of everything as far as her Maternity care goes. I gave her Zion''s phone number and transfered her over to them as well. Will be sending emails to her about both Planstin and Zion as she asked a couple questions in regard to and where to send bills, etc. Along with member portal she asked if there is one, to which I let her know that she does have a member portal with us, that also upon logging in, she can see all the other services that are in her plan, that have portals as well. I will be including her member portal login information as well. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-29 10:09:22', '2023-03-29 10:09:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116824003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064068018', 'Robert Coray', 'Ticket #2480 Mar 8, 2023 2:52pm', 'I have a client, Robert Coray, that changed his IUA from $1000 to $2500 a few months ago. His son just found out he has cancer and so they are trying to deal with Zion and are not getting a response from them. First of all, Zion has it showing that he has a $5000 IUA which he does not. My mpb portal shows he is paying for a $2500 IUA. Secondly, Zion is not communicating with him about his medical bills and what he should do. He is very stressed already with the cancer and not getting a response from Zion is very frustrating for him. What can I do or should I tell him? Is there a form MPB needs to send Zion to prove the correct IUA amount? 

Thank you for your help. I do not personally deal with Zion so I have no idea where to start.', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2023-03-29 08:56:33', '2023-03-29 13:27:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116806021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116119008', 'Kasey Klingensmith', NULL, 'Kasey called in and said she has not received her cards yet and she has her Gynecologist appointment today and doesn''t know what to tell them or show them. As I was pulled up her info here, she realized the same thing I did, that her start date isn''t until 4/1, which is only a few days away. So, she said she will cancel the appt. and just wait the few days. I let her know that the hard copy of the Planstin card won''t come in until about the 15th of the month, BUT she should have if not in the next few days, will get a virtual card in her email. I gave her Planstin''s phone number and told her to call them to see if the virtual card has been sent, if not they can send it right away. Also, I told her that her provider has to be in the PHCS Network and to ask Planstin to check for her as that is the only way the appointment for her yearly woman''s well visit will be 100% shared at no cost. She thanked me very much and was so happy to hear she has her Concierge like this to help. I let her know we are always real people as well, never automated, which was also a huge relief for her as everything now a days is automated and never can get through to a real person. She is thrilled and happy for the help anytime she needs. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-29 08:50:30', '2023-03-29 08:50:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116803013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084286002', 'Jacob Cranman', NULL, 'Member submitted PU form I will update in A123.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-29 08:24:12', '2023-03-29 08:24:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116806016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000070912052', 'Anna Edwards', NULL, 'Anna called in and said she needed help with getting set up with her Tele health portion of the plan as she has never needed to use it before. I do see here that it states she is registered with CirrusMD, so, I sent her an email with the link to click that will bring her to the sign in page. She said she doesn''t remember what she set up and I let her know the username will be the email address that we have on file here, her only email address, and if she can''t remember her password, there is a Forgot Password button she can press to reset the password. Once she is all signed in, she just needs to start a chat to get seen by a medical provider by clicking the chat in the bottom right corner of the screen. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-29 08:07:59', '2023-03-29 08:07:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116806011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062929191', 'Jerry Riechert', NULL, 'Jerry called in this morning looking for Nahla due to the fact that she was supposed to send him some pricing info about what he would be paying per month for taking his son off the plan. His plan then would turn into Member and Spouse instead of Member and Family. He will be going from $765/mo to $550/mo. He was happy to hear the drop in price once removing their son from the plan. Jerry is all set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-29 08:05:53', '2023-03-29 08:05:53');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000116803003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096329001', 'Christopher Cappuccitti', NULL, 'Member submitted Change from to update address.  I will update in all areas', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-29 07:56:38', '2023-03-29 07:56:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116783008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110464002', 'Tosca Kulendran', NULL, 'No response. Left detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to reschedule online the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-03-29 07:40:57', '2023-03-29 07:42:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073656124', 'Lesa Russell', NULL, '03.28.2023 Lesa called to learn how to move forward with her findings of a lump behind her neck, while visiting her aesthetician. I briefly explained that would be under the medical cost sharing umbrella and she would need to present herself as a cash-pay patient and request the cash-pay discount.
After asking for clarification, I educated Lesa on the 3 main portions of her plan (Essentials, Preventative & Medical Cost Sharing), while using the names of the companies for familiarity.
We established that her 1st step is to go see her physician, and see if they can care for it there, or biopsy it there. She is aware of her IUA''s responsibility and when MCS kicks in. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 17:32:05', '2023-03-28 18:15:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062929191', 'Jerry Riechert', NULL, '03.28.2023 Jerry called to inquire of a financial difference, should he drop his son off the plan. I confirmed with Cari that there shouldn''t be a difference, but she explained that it depends on the type of plan he''s on and if there are any other children on the plan. I was able to contact Jerry back to offer him the information, but only reached his VM, where I left along the lines of the following message for him:
Hi Jerry, I apologize for taking so long to get back to you, but I have some good news. Given that your son is the only child/offspring on the plan, there will be savings. If you want to discuss this further, please give us a call back on 800-519-2969. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 17:17:22', '2023-03-28 17:17:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086967002', 'Kris DiNucci', NULL, '3-28-2023:  Gamze called.  $333 office visit & injection.  One & done type issue.  Had to do a ton of education  They presented their Planstin card & wondered why it hadn''t been paid.  Disc the ''prev care'' component  vs  catastrophic/illness component.
     - They have 5k IUA, so went over how that works, how to present as no ''ins'', ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, offer to pay first 5k on issue & ask for them to bill you so you can get the money together, call concierge for help sub ''med need'', deadline, etc.
     - They seemed rather irritated that nothing was going to reimb the $333 they spent, but I do think they understood by the end of the conversation - hopefully.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 17:12:57', '2023-03-30 02:14:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116765008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068994027', 'Linda Garcia', NULL, '3-28-23 Linda cancelled MPB successfully but struggling to cancel dental with Spirit/Ameritas. I just gave her 5 different #''s to try from the enrollment email and from my contact list.  She''ll keep trying.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-28 16:36:51', '2023-03-28 16:36:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442360', 'Whitney Hammond', NULL, '3-28-2023:  Whitney called.  He wants to find a doctor &amp; wondered if we have someone we''d sugg.  Re-sent his post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail &amp; walked thru how to use HCBB &amp; Healthgrades.com.  He appreciatedd the tool &amp; lesson.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 15:54:58', '2023-03-28 15:54:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094853002', 'Brian Burke', NULL, '03.28.2023 Brian called to cancel his membership. I offered to forward him to his advisor, Leslie Jablonski, he said he has her number and will call her. 
While he was on the phone with me, he inquired about his tax documentation from Planstin, based on the email they sent him. He tried to log-in and even changing the passcode, and he could not get anywhere with what they sent to attain his papers from them.
I recommended that he contacted Planstin directly, as we do not have access to Planstin''s platform to generate tax docs. 
Brian was willing and fair to contact Leslie and Planstin on his own. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 14:56:07', '2023-03-28 14:56:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116765003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038883009', 'Melissa Bajza', NULL, '3-28-23 From Melissa just now. I called her back immediately and left her a vm to discuss.

Hi Wendy,

I have not had the time or energy to call and check if this is now cleared. I would like to cancel my policy and have that retro-dated as I had no confidence in using this insurance since July 2022. Please confirm that you are able to credit me 8 months of payments which date back to our original communication in regards to this matter. I will look forward to hearing back from you with confirmation.


Thank you.

Sincerely,
Melissa Bajza', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-28 14:35:19', '2023-03-28 14:35:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116388002', 'Sophie Campbell', NULL, '3-28-2023:  Tried to sub ticket to Michele re: 3/27/23 cov w/Sophie. Tckt system tells me duplicate contact.  Trying to get help & will try to sub again.     - CA

Advisor:  Misty Berryman
Member:  Sophie Campbell
Call date: 3/27/2023

Sophie just purchased her memb & it''s not even effective until 5/1/2023.  However, she called the Concierge Line because she "just purchased" her membership & didn''t understand how IUAs work ("is it accumulative?"), that there are 3 per year, that they are issue specific, etc...  She also asked, "the preventative care has a 2 mo waiting period, right?", because she wants to make her preventative appointments for after their effective date.

I got her to sched her ''Welcome Call'' for after 5/1/2023, but really feel like the e-mails Misty sent her did not answer enough questions for her to understand what she''s purchased.  Maybe Misty''s e-mail needs to have the prospect call her for details, instead of the new members calling the Concierge Line after they purchase to get the sales information?  Hopefully, she''s been vetted for pre-x conditions, etc.  Somewhere in the sales process, the ball is being dropped?

Sophie is very nice.  I hope she works out and there are no bad surprises for her.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 14:15:31', '2023-03-28 16:29:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114324012', 'Brindra Lekhraj', NULL, '3-28-2023:  Brindra called.  He''s an Uber driver & they req proof he has healthcare.  I let him know Planstin (& Zion) sb able to provide letters showing participation.  He''s driving, so he knows to find Planstin''s ph # on his ''prev care'' Planstin card (he''ll only ever present this card for ''prev care'' - a little education while we are talking...).  I let him know they are a sister-comp to Zion & will either be able to provide both, or can trans him to Zion if needed to get that info.
     - He also wanted proof of what he''s paying.  I reminded him he''s not actually effective until 4/1/2023, but his receipt for his April mo cont will be on the MPB.Health Memb Portal.   He asked about the diff portals & I went over briefly, but added: with so many diff comp to your healthcare, it''s best to call us to find out where/which portal will have the info.  He seemed fine with that.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 13:24:15', '2023-03-28 14:21:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063775002', 'Daniel Gutierrez', NULL, '3-28-2023:  Martha called.  Kept saying we didn''t pay the labs from her husb prev care'' appt.  I tried to do education on who MPB is, who the TPA = Planstin is, our different responsibilities, etc.  She got frustrated because "we told her before we''d take care of this", but I''m not seeing anything regardin her husb''s labs from his ''prev care'' appt in the notes, so maybe she talked to Planstin before?
     - Let her know, the ''prev care'' that is included is decided by the gvmt and the ACA MEC plan generally only covers one lab = basic lipid panel.  She got kind of upset, saying "all my husband can do it tell them he''s there for his preventative care appt" and she felt like all that should be covered.  I again said the gvmt sets the guidelines & most doc''s know what is & is not paid for.  If they move outside that, then it is out-of-pocket.  She looked at the long list of labs not paid for & said "did you even pay for any of this"?  At this point I let her know I cannot see her bills and since we do not have any connection with this, I''d like to get her to Planstin..  They should be able to help her since they take care of this component.  She already had their ph #, so I trans her directly to them.     -CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 12:50:07', '2023-03-28 13:00:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111992001', 'Lars Ensign', NULL, '03.28.2023 Lars is looking to have his depression RX refilled.  I explained how our pharmacy program works, and who can be involved: his physician, pharm, CirrusMD, ....etc and us researching the best RX price. 
He at first was mixing, Zion, "Telemedicine", and getting prescriptions all in one area. So I took him back, split up the topics and went over each one and what they are used for. 
He then decided he wanted to start with CirrusMD as his first step. I sent over a CirrusMd invitation link. By the time we hung up, he had not received the invitation yet, so prior to hanging up, I showed him how to resend himself an invitation link, JUST IN CASE. I also shared, if my invitation link makes it to him, that link is short-lived 24 hrs.
Lars will call us back with more questions about getting his RX request discounted. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 12:42:43', '2023-03-28 12:54:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011899022', 'Lisa Nicholls', NULL, 'Spouse Russell inquired about changing Pmt Method to CC.  I advised of the 3% fee. and also deadline.  Sent link', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 12:16:48', '2023-03-28 12:16:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991117', 'Ryan Dunlap', NULL, '03.28.2023 Ryan called re: a phone call from Jackie, saying they don''t have coverage.
Referred back to the above note on 01.31.2023 re: his conversion attempt, and the obstacle of Sedera''s lack of availability and inclement weather. 
I reminded him about the instructions given, to email THAT NIGHT with shedding light on him attempting to complete his conversion, and having a hard time accessing his account AND reaching anyone at Sedera.
With the guidance from Cari via teams, I coached Ryan to contact Sedera back and share the following information to share proof of evidence towards a good faith effort in trying to complete his conversion with Sedera prior to the required date.
I asked Ryan to contact us back to keep us informed on the results. AON, they are getting charged by MPB, with possible no coverage from Sedera''s end, AND Ryan most likely will want to talk about refunding him the last few months. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 11:24:08', '2023-03-28 12:14:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116760033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115246001', 'Kristi Anderson', NULL, 'Spoke to member will reschedule welcome call after start date of April 1, 2023. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-03-28 11:05:06', '2023-03-28 11:05:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107280002', 'Bibi Frederick', NULL, '3-27-2023:  Bibi called.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 10:48:49', '2023-03-28 10:48:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116757003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036530449', 'Emily Jaynes', NULL, '3-27-2023:  Emily called RCI for her 1095 &amp; was told MPB declined having RCI prepare them. &nbsp;Emily spoke to a Becky there, &amp; only after calling them 5 times was she able to get to someone. &nbsp;Jennifer happens to be at the main off this week, so I''ve asked her to please check w/Patti Tues &amp; let me know how to respond to Emily. &nbsp;Hopefully, Patti can clear this up for us.     - CA

&nbsp;[Best # to  call Emily back: 602-540-7309]', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-28 10:47:55', '2023-03-28 10:47:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097826002', 'Sharon McCormick', NULL, '03.28.2023 Sharon called trying to speak to a counselor. She thought she was calling the M&S EAP directly, and kept asking for a counselor and how that''s really all she is trying to do.
I finally understood where she was trying to land, and I guided her to the collaborative page with M&S. Except for she was already there, but not knowing where to go from there. I wanted to give her our code to access the page, but she was already singed in and viewing the different squares with hyperlinks. I was not sure how she got to that page without a code from us. 
I finally got Sharon to understand that the number on the top right of that page is the number to call to schedule with a counselor. She seemed a bit frantic 7 frustrated, and was not receiving me at the beginning, so I asked her to let us start from scratch in getting to that page again. Then her browser took her right to the M&S page, without any signage or code. I gave her the code anyways, for just in case she will need later, and suggested that she refer to MPower Benefits when they ask for  employer group.  NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-28 10:21:35', '2023-03-28 10:59:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116744001', 'David Young', NULL, 'Member Only $5000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 10:16:09', '2023-03-28 10:16:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116739002', 'Michael Backer', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $1000 IUA Direct', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 10:13:12', '2023-03-28 10:13:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116736048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118041001', 'Simon Buchard', NULL, 'email sent for Simon for return call', 'Chris Ferris', 'Chris Ferris', '2023-03-28 10:03:26', '2023-03-28 10:03:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Member submitted Change from to update address I will process &amp; notify Sedera.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 09:02:43', '2023-03-28 09:02:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084286002', 'Jacob Cranman', NULL, 'Member called me asking why he never received call back about updating his payment info.  I told him that I would send him PU email w/link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:39:57', '2023-03-28 08:39:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919395', 'Michael (Mikhail) Kaspin', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to update address I will update.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:30:04', '2023-03-28 08:30:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091646', 'Carol Lovejoy', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to update address after previously submitting on 11/14 (note below).  I updated in FTNI &amp; bank address.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:26:47', '2023-03-28 08:26:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, 'Member submitted Change form to update address I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:11:28', '2023-03-28 08:11:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116716003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109499009', 'Peter Walimire', NULL, 'Meridith had Carolee from Zenergy Physical Therapy reach out to us via SalesIQ, to which I was alerted to call Carolee. I called over to Carolee at Zenergy and she stated that Meridith that patient is in there for something to do with her Knee and having physical therapy. Meridith seems very confused and said the provider needs to verify her benefits with us MPowering Benefits. I explained to Carolee when she told me what this was all for, was that she needed to speak with Zion Health as this is something that is Injury/Illness related. Carolee then asked what Cost Sharing was and I stated that Meridith is to present herself as a cash paying patient and she is responsible for paying the first $1000 of her IUA, then everything thereafter is going to be shared through Zion Health. I told Carolee that I will transfer her over to Zion Health to verify benefits and gave her their phone number just in case they get disconnected. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-28 08:08:35', '2023-03-28 08:08:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116689001', 'Kathleen Weller', NULL, 'Member &amp; Fam $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:07:21', '2023-03-28 08:07:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116688002', 'Lilian Pontillo', NULL, 'Member Only Essentials', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 08:04:28', '2023-03-28 08:04:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116673002', 'Kevin Stanek', NULL, 'Member &amp; Fam $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 07:44:38', '2023-03-28 07:44:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116616002', 'Cora Lonning', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 07:42:05', '2023-03-28 07:42:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116702003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116614002', 'Sydney E LaMorte', NULL, 'Member &amp; Fam $2500 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-28 07:40:16', '2023-03-28 07:40:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116653020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108397002', 'Mary Rust', NULL, '03.27.2023 Mary is calling to learn why Walgreens rejected the RX request from CirrusMD.
Consulted with Cari via teams, she shared that only 30 day coupons will be prescribed from CirrusMD, not 90. 
She helped searched both RX requests that Ed is trying to get refills on:
1- Omprazole, 20mg, 1/day, 30 days
2- fluoxetine, 20mg, 1/day, 30 days
Mary then said they will set up a preventative wellness visit for Ed, where he can get 90 day prescriptions instead. I told her, once the doctor prescribes anything, the appt becomes diagnostic and Planstin will not cover it. They will need to figure out how to separate the diagnostic from preventative. I consulted with Cari again on that part, and she reiterated the member needs to contact the doctor''s office to see how they would like to handle that.
Cari coached to remind the member that the MEC plan is a gov''t plan.  By telling the doc''s office it must stay ''preventative'' to be paid for, it reminds them not to prescribe. Some members end up going in the next day, separately for the prescription.
I needed to call Mary back to offer her the 30 day coupons and the answer to the above information. 
I was able to generate and send Mary the RX quotes:
Below are the prices as of Monday 3.27.2023
WALMART:
Fluoxetine: 20mg, 30 Day Supply for 1/day = $4.00
Omprazole: 20mg, 30 Day Supply for 1/day =  $15.00
SAFEWAY:
Fluoxetine: 20mg, 30 Day Supply for 1/day = $7.33
Omprazole: 20mg, 30 Day Supply for 1/day =  $7.39
The totals for either pharmacy are: Walmart=$19, Safeway=$18.72. Please let me know your thoughts or if you need anything adjusted. We can reprice your RX quotes if anything changes. 
Since I emailed Mary, I decided to call her to let her know of the email and to see if she can call CirrusMD to see if Safeway will accept their call/the prescriptions.  If she still has issues, we''ll need to go from there. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-27 15:07:16', '2023-03-27 17:12:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116653015', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012474377', 'Lynette (Lynn) Arena', NULL, '03.27.2023 Lynn called to better understand how the screening process'' gets covered, re: the PHCS network, specifically colonoscopies. I reassured her, yes, all entities performing any screenings must be part of the PHCS network, and Planstin will then collaborate payment with the facility. 
