  ('zcrm_1579374000116639028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061768243', 'Haley Collins', NULL, '3-27-23 I talked with Haley and her mom Elizabeth Collins about Haley''s membership. Elizabeth thought Haley had the exact same membership as herself. But, Haley has CARE+ which doesn''t include chiro or wellness. I believe she chose CARE+ for the best price and bc of her young age.  I reviewed Haley''s membership with both of them. She was hoping for chiro to be paid for. I explained that it will be shared if it''s part of a Need for an accident, injury, illness scenario with pre-approval and after she meets her IUA. So, likely not worth the effort for chiro which is avg. $65. They seem to be back on track and understanding it better. She was excited to learn about WHLC for discounts on chiro. I told them to call MPB Concierge Team for help with getting the discounts.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-27 13:09:24', '2023-03-27 13:09:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116639023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034039274', 'Rochelle Booker', NULL, '3-27-23 Ricki called bc she has to complete the insurance info form for her daughter who will be going abroad. I told her she needs to use the info from the Apex/RCI card which she did. She asked if it''s considered a PPO. I believe so but I''m checking with Joan.  She put the ID # for the Member #. The rest she filled in. She''s all set for now. I explained this is the ACA compliant part that appeases proof of ins for gov and these types of needs for traveling abroad.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-27 12:59:09', '2023-08-28 15:10:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116623023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105872022', 'David Wyatt', NULL, 'Finally spoke to Katrina after playing phone tag with her for a week.  She had some questions around the submission of bill for both Preventative &amp; Injury/Illness.  She had a couple of offices visits &amp; a Procedure all of which she paid out of Pocket.  I gave her contact info for both Zion &amp; Planstin.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 12:27:04', '2023-03-27 12:27:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116639008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116383002', 'Liza Bakken', NULL, '3-27-23 Liza called because she doesn''t know how to reschedule her Welcome Call. She also remembered she had an abnormal pap she forgot to report. She wanted to understand how that will work. She had a procedure done and it all showed as normal, no problems. Her Dr. wants her to do a 6 month follow up pap which is right about now. She knows the procedure will be considered pre-x. But, getting a clean pap will be good on her record. I explained if they code it as diagnostic, it will be her responsibility to pay for. If it''s within the ACA guidelines and coded as wellness/preventative then it will be at no cost. If she does it at the 6-month time from the date of procedure, then it''s definitely her cost. She understands it''s truly up to the doctor and how they code it due to her recent experience and procedure.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-27 12:24:01', '2023-03-27 12:24:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116639003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116383002', 'Liza Bakken', NULL, '3-22-23 Liza is 55 and came to me via Andre MPitsos. She''s his physical therapist!  She was with C4 and thought her ins auto renewed and recently discovered it did not. So, she was able to get C4 to reinstate her plan. Then she just discovered today that she was still never billed for her plan and therefore, it never came into effect. So, she''s uninsured and has been since the first of the year. She''s super healthy, active living in the Aspen area. She watched my 9 min. video on my site and my interview. She had knee surgery in 2019 and no issues since. So, that''s prior to pre-x clause. She takes meds for high blood pressure and hormone replacement. I let her know of the exemption to pre-x clause for well managed high blood pressure, but hormone replacement issues will be considered pre-x. She understands. Her husband is 63 and super healthy. Liza has her own gymnastics school and also works as PT as a 1099. So, multiple self-employment jobs. She had Freedom Life in the past. She knew well enough to ask for immunizations as self pay and they would have been about $21 each. Instead Freedom Life encouraged her to go through them with their card. Then she got billed for $1200!  She was able to get it reduced to $900 and still was forced to pay $900 instead of the $21 per shot! She was irate, needless to say. So, she understands the value of self-pay. Her son is currently on Medicaid as an 18 year old. She''s enrolling in SECURE $1000/$625 ES for April 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-27 12:18:20', '2023-03-27 12:18:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116636008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043462286', 'Bryan Baker', NULL, 'No response. Sent email to reschedule welcome call after start date of April 1, 2023. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-03-27 12:16:41', '2023-03-27 12:16:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116622008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, '3/27/2023:  Bryan called.  He realized he''s let almost a year since Susan''s RA issue first DOS.  He was very kind &amp; acknowledged it could be an issue.  We decied he''s going to go ahead and get detailed inv &amp; pymt receipts all the way back (in case they will make a "1st time" exception - he agrees, even if they decline those early expenses, he''s tried &amp; no worse off).  He will call me when he''s ready to sub the ''med need'' to Zion.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-27 12:14:47', '2023-03-27 12:14:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116623013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098841002', 'Janice Saar', NULL, 'Member''s 4/23 payment declined 1st notice sent via email &amp; VM-3/27 3/30-2nd notice sent via email Final notice sent - 4/4  Member submitted Pmt update I will rerun', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 12:01:53', '2023-04-05 12:25:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116623003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098475002', 'Jennifer Corson', NULL, 'Member''s 4/23 payment declined 1st notice sent via email &amp; VM - 3/27 3/30-sent out 2nd notice 4/4- sent out final notice via VM &amp;email 4/11-per Lou member will not be able to pay at this time.  I will cancel for non Payment', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 11:54:43', '2023-04-11 08:58:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116570063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000076954036', 'Teresa Fox', NULL, '3-27-23 Terri cancelled her membership just now for April 1st. She got group ins for her private practice. I thought we set her up as a group but she said no. So, she''s just cancelling for herself, not her employees. She decided MCS was too complicated bc last year she had 3 incidents. One incident barely exceeded her $1000 IUA and the other two did not. So, she wound up paying for all of it anyhow. She felt like saying cash pay wasn''t totally honest and she wants to try reg ins again. It was too late for me to help her on that front as well. She took a while to call me back bc she got covid and she''s recovering from it now. She didn''t sound very good.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-27 11:45:01', '2023-03-27 11:45:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116619061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094713010', 'Susan Rosenfelder', NULL, 'Member''s 4/23 payment declined 1st notice sent via email &amp; VM - 3/27 3/30-Member submitted payment Update form I will rerun', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 11:37:59', '2023-03-30 09:40:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116558048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116388002', 'Sophie Campbell', NULL, '3-27-2023:  Sophie called.  Has no idea how the IUAs work.
     - Noticed she''s not even effective until 5/1/2023!
     - We went over IUAs in depth.
     - Sent ''Welcome Call'' invite - she''ll sched for after 5/1/2023
     - She thought from the info her advisor Misty Berryman sent over there was a 2mo waiting period for ''prev care''.  I let her know there is NO waiting period.  That we are curr trans to a new ''no ntwk'' req''d ''prev care'', yet unsure when that will happen.  She may make ''prev care'' appts for her kids at the end of May, knowing we will have to talk to see if the trans has happened, if she still needs to go in ntwk, if not how to present, etc.  I let her know ''prev care'' will be the only time she presents an ID card.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-27 11:16:43', '2023-03-27 11:31:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116558043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, '3-27-2023:  Amber called.  We walked thru the proc of sub a chg form for her new mailing address.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-27 11:04:01', '2023-03-27 11:04:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116558038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675121', 'Anthony Silva', NULL, '3/27/2023:  Anthony called looking for his "tax ID #".  Since it''s tax time, my assumption is he''s looking for the 1095.  I asked if he rec''d an e-mail from Planstin ~ 2/25/23.  He said he did, but it wouldn''t let him change his pw.  I think he was either on the wrong portal (MPB.Health), or didn''t realize it''s a diff company?  I went over how to use their link & that the Planstin portal will only be for getting this document (not pymt chgs, etc.).  
     Then went over the various components and why Planstin provides this form.  He seemed to understand.  He''s going to try again & will call Planstin (I gave him their #) if he has any further issues getting his tax form.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-27 10:46:51', '2023-03-27 10:46:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116558033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061768243', 'Haley Collins', NULL, '3-27-2023:  There seems to have been some confusion.  Nahla called Haley back (not Jennifer & I) when I came in so we could talk w/her together.
     - Haley & I went over her chiropractic desire.  I explained they will consider chiropractic as part of a larger need (gave the ex of an accident).  Told her she can certainly try to get pre-approval since it''s for pain, however, she might want to get that process started.  She knows IF they approve it, she''s resp for the 1k IUA & let her know I do not know how they will look at a visit prior to any approval (twds her IUA?).
         She snowboards a lot (lives in Silverthorne) and works as a dental asst, so says she started having pain just last week.  Let her know only Zion will be able to give her a definitive answer.
     - MAP: Counseling.  Haley was able to go online w/me to the MAP program.  We went over how the counseling works, the pattern, etc.  Also, went over their site, hours, etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-27 10:43:10', '2023-03-27 10:43:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116599057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061768243', 'Haley Collins', NULL, '03.27.2023 Haley called to see if her chiro apt TODAY will be covered. 
I shared that in order for alt med to be covered, WE would submit an alt med medical need request with a treatment plan from the service provider TO ZION, prior to the apt for approval.
She said she was in need to see the chiropractor today, as she has been for relieving ongoing body aches.
I consulted with Jen and Cari via teams, and they reiterated it would not be covered in that manner.
Haley proceeded to share it was a huge draw in for her to sign up with MPB, from speaking to Wendy, that her chiro visits would be covered.
Cari said that we call her back to discuss the matter in details and find solutions, since she was in the admin meeting. 
During our call with Haley and Cari, Cari went over Haley''s plan being mainly catastrophic. In order for the chiro visits to get covered would need to be part of large medical need request (i.e. if Haley broke her leg during a snow boarding activity - Haley shared she is an active person and does a lot of sports)
Haley asked about our MAP, and Cari guided her to our collaborative page with M&S, shared about the Impact Ste app, the various levels of hyperlinks and the contact and process information on receiving their counseling services.
After Cari exited the conference call, Haley also asked about getting coverage for prescriptions. I explained they would be covered if they were part of an open medical need. However, we do have a program that offers researching various pharm discount websites, including an international shopper, to generate a discount coupon and email it to the member. Haley paraphrased what I shared that led to knowing she understood. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-27 09:38:53', '2023-03-27 12:49:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116619021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116613002', 'Timothy Foley', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 08:44:11', '2023-03-27 08:44:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116619011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, 'Member submitted PU form.  I will update.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-27 08:35:02', '2023-03-27 08:35:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116539025', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037657007', 'Mary Evans', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 2952 Question : Can you assist with set up of a CIRRUS MD tele heath account?', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-03-26 16:10:04', '2023-03-26 16:10:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116602017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037657007', 'Mary Evans', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 2951 Question : my husband and I are on the same plan.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-03-26 15:14:37', '2023-03-26 15:14:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116570053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005011193', 'Andre Mpitsos', NULL, '3-25-23  Andre called me yesterday and we had a long talk about it.  It''s not in an email thread. He''s referred many clients to me over the years. This time he''s trying to refer his brother. His brother went directly to Zion''s site and sees he can get all of the benefits that "look" to be the same as what we offer for $268 vs $325 for SECURE or $295 DIRECT in his age bracket (Andre''s paying $344 in the same age bracket for the Bridge membership which included immediate sharing in the first year of membership).

Andre''s brother is very price sensitive and cares much less about any handholding or the actual value of the benefits. He is most interested in the cheapest price and seemingly the same exact benefits directly through Zion. Andre knows the value I''ve brought to him over the years and the support he gets with me any time there''s been a challenge in getting reimbursed or needing any kind of help. He also lives in an area where the cost is prohibitively expensive. This is why he''s willing to stay the course. But, most people aren''t that loyal and his brother sees no reason in paying more for what appears to be the same benefits.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-25 12:43:27', '2023-03-25 12:43:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116570048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, '3-24-23 Willa called back to add MEC  so upgrading to SECURE membership for May 1st, 2023. They are due to have a baby in June and want to make sure they have access to the baby well checks. Her friend is with Zion/MPB and had trouble with the network for their well visits. But, I let Willa know the network is getting removed now and should be all set by the time she needs it. I explained she will just need to make sure the office will bill to insurance and to check with them before to avoid any troubles once she has the baby. She''s excited to set up an HSA and I will have them send her the Welcome Call scheduler to get reminder about her new membership with SECURE from CARE+ and HSA information.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-24 16:33:02', '2023-03-24 16:33:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116570043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043462286', 'Bryan Baker', NULL, '3-23-23 Health Matching Account Enrollment Complete and starting immediately:

