  ('zcrm_1579374000116599006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992009', 'Jason Cooper', NULL, '03.24.2023 Martha called us, after a reciprocation of clarification requests re: her Prev. Med. Need Request that was denied by Zion.
With Cari conferenced in on GoTo, the following was covered, explained and given examples towards:
Cari asked ho did Jason''s derm apt go? A: They gave him injections. Found Nothing. Sensitive skin, when scratched, leaves a scar. So the injection was supposed to help not leave a scar.
CARI: derm is not covered unless it is cancerous, or needed treatment. No steroids are covered. MIGHT get the actual apt covered, solely. ITEMIZED BILL=$156
Cari explained that the $5000 IUA is not helpful, and gave an example of how a treatment of $2500 is out there, and her  plan can''t cover it bcz of her IUA. Plus members are responsible for 3 of those per year.
Cari explained how DPC works, and how Direct is limited with preventative, THEN she explained how the $250 offered for this plan can be used towards this appt of $156. Cari did explain it needs to be done on the front end, and prior to the appt. Member would present as cash-pay patient and will request a breakdown of how much the initial visit would cost.
Martha mentioned maybe go through the PCP for this issue, and dip into the $250 payment towards it. If accepted and used, it does not go towards the IUA. That would be double dipping.
ANOTHER QUESTION
$150 - Gastroenterology appt for her 15 YO son.
Need clarification if $250 per person: Is it per calendar year or when it was used?
Martha asked about immunizations, well child visit. CARI: explains that this plan was meant to have a DPC, YOU DON''T HAVE TO HAVE IT, but if you don''t it leaves you with lots of gaps.

Martha has some decision making to do and thought process to attain the right plan for her and her family. She will ask husband, derma visit, if he wants to use the $250 towards his skin treatment.
Will decide about her son''s gaster. visit how to pay.
How do I change plans? I sent her an MPB change form link. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-24 11:42:53', '2023-03-24 12:47:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116594011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011659075', 'Snatam Khalsa', NULL, '3-24-2023:  Snatam called again.  She''s super confused on how this works.  It took quite some time for her to be willing to tell me, her husb has a vein issue and she wants to take him to a PCP or a clinic.  Even w/me explaining that I need to understand ''why'' they need to see the doc to guide her because of the diff components (& you present in diff manners w/ea comp), it was hard to get the info from her.
     - Once she let me know they are going for a diagnosis, I was able to let her know how to present:  no ''ins'', no card to present, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' discount, get payment receipts & detailed inv - 6 mos deadline for sub expenses towards 5k IUA & we went over in detail how this works.  [She has so little understanding, I worry they do not understand IUA completely.  But, she was so confused I completely focused on their curr issue.]
        She said the doc''s off is having trouble understanding ''cash-pay''.  That could be someone new, or I let her know that could be a challenge if they don''t understand you are paying your own bills.
     - Told her when they need ''prev care'', call us & we will go over those guidelines, because they get handled in a very diff manner. (ie: their child''s annual school physical was the example I gave.  Let her know we need to keep the ''prev'' sep from diag/treatment because it changes the medical coding & can cause issues w/the billing of the ''prev care''.)     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-24 11:36:59', '2023-03-24 11:36:59'),
