  ('zcrm_1579374000116516013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043462286', 'Bryan Baker', NULL, '3-23-23 I called Bryan and told him at least 3-4 times I didn''t want to step on Ryan''s toes and he can call Ryan to see what he has to offer. I let him know Ryan isn''t offering this membership now and not sure what he has to offer. He then asked about dental. Sounds like he had something through Ryan as well. I told him to ask Ryan. But, he asked what we have through MPB. So, I shared the HMA with him. He really likes the HMA 2500 since he''s healthy but wants this for dental cleanings and anything else that arises moving forward. Then he asked again about our memberships and really wants to get something ASAP and said Ryan''s office hasn''t been great about responding lately. So, I let him know SECURE is the closest membership to what he had before and slightly better with the guidelines and the network limitation is getting lifted for wellness now moving forward. I made sure no new pre-x and he said no. I explained the IUA and he said he used to have some additional gap coverage through Ryan which he''d rather just pay the higher monthly for the lower IUA and not include another company in the mix. So, he chose SECURE $1000/$300 and HMA 2500 (starting today).  He''s hoping for SECURE for April 1st if possible after seeing how horrendous reg ins is going to be. I submitted a ticket request and will let him know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-23 16:49:25', '2023-03-23 17:07:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116520006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113967002', 'Lynette Phillips', NULL, '3-23-2023:  Lynette called from her doctor''s office asking about getting her RX refilled:  Estradiol tabs.  (Not a pill pack, so not bcs = hormone repl instead).  Did not think to see if she''s at her ''prev care'' appt.  She was in a big hurry in case they came back in the room.
     - Estradiol 1mg, #90 tabs - cheapest was Publix, showing a retail price of $7.50.  Next was Winn-Dixie w/a $10 retail price.  Cost+ was $14.30 w/s&h.  Since it''s showing ''retail price'', there was no coupon to send her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-23 16:45:35', '2023-03-23 16:45:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116516003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810847', 'Sally Hammond', NULL, '3-23-23 "Hi Wendy,

Thank you for getting this to our teams so we could resolve these matters for Sally and Peter. I did see that these billing matters had gone off track for the members. I am yet to receive a response from Sally today, but I forwarded her the following message through our Spruce communication platform:

Hello, Sally, this is Tomorr, once more. I have some billing updates that I want to provide to you because I do see that some of these matters had gone off track for you and Peter.

We have sent out member reimbursements for you and Peter in the amounts of $210 and $414 - this is done through our Melio process which you are able to complete with the links above.

I have closed your account balance of $240 with Carent Labs - the billing provider for Boulder Pathology. Additionally, I have closed Peter''s Labcorp account balance of $366.45 and Holy Cross account balance of $581. For brief explanation, I can see from our claims records that your Carent Labs service and Peter''s Holy Cross service were not processed correctly - therefore the Care Provider had appealed these respective initial payments. This is why you received these bills. I could see that Peter''s Labcorp service was accounted for yet still pending insurance - I escalated this and closed this account as well.

We apologize for the extended timeline necessary to resolve these matters for you and Peter - if you have any further concerns please reach out to our teams via phone or message. Thank you - we hope that you both have a wonderful upcoming weekend!

Tomorr

