  ('zcrm_1579374000116332003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078032158', 'Wenda Gao', NULL, '03.22.2023 Xuemei Zhong called in the attempt to collect a 1099 form towards her tax filing.
I was only familiar with the request of the 1095, so I referred her to her emails from Planstin.
She said she spoke to them, they had sent her the 1095C, and she needed the 1099HC. They referred her to us.
After consulting with Jen and Cari, both agreed MPB does not handout any tax forms. I guided Xuemei to contact her accountant to further explain and help attain the tax forms. She said she''s using TurboTax and it is asking for a 1099HC, the MPB EIN number and the Federal Identification number.  I shared this again with my team, via teams, and requested one of them to be part of the call, perhaps Xuemei could hear one of them, since she did not seem to receive what I was saying. It seemed as though, Xuemei did not want to pay an accountant to gain the information she needs to complete her taxes, at the same time, we could not help her with gaining them either and she wanted to speak to someone from our administration office.
I brought Cari in, who shared some basic tax form education, and who would supply each one (1095C, 1095A, 1099HC...). Cari repeatedly shared with her that she is asking questions that she should be directing to her accountant. Xuemei shared with Cari that she is using TurboTax. Then Cari recommended she contact TurboTax to attain service assistance with her filing.
There seem to either have been a disconnect with understanding the process for Xuemei OR she was not interested in hiring an accountant for any reason.
The call ended without Xuemei accomplishing her goal with our phone call, but does have direction to where to go for it. It doesn''t seem she was satisfied. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-22 13:16:17', '2023-03-22 13:31:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116326003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116324001', 'Tim Koch', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-22 12:29:32', '2023-03-22 12:29:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116321003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081509011', 'Tammy Goen', NULL, '03.22.2023 Tammy called wanted to speak to Patti re: a plan change from Care+ to Secure for preventative purposes. Tammy receive a notice of payment that reflected the old plan amount instead of the new plan amount for Secure. Her new plan is supposed to start next month
Given the practice of not transferring anyone to Patti, I consulted Jen and Cari via teams. Jen responded that Patti has not received a change form from Tammy. Cari confirmed via Cognito Forms that we do not have a form.
Patti was about to jump into a meeting, she said she would call Tammy back on (541) 815-8901 in an hour or so, I told Tammy.
Tammy said she completed one a while back in January. She also has called a couple of times after that, she said, but both times there was no mention of having the change form. 
She did have a concern regarding her medical need that has been open, Zion sent her a check for $531.25. She wants to clarify if it is part of the payment or was it issued by mistake.
After finishing with Tammy, I transferred her to Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-22 11:22:12', '2023-03-22 11:33:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116307013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003748040', 'Natalie Lampert', NULL, '3-22-23 Natalie and Jonathan Brumbaugh (Hiller) are engaged. Zion told them they can combine their membership already before getting married. I''ll get permission from Zion to make sure since this isn''t customary. They also want to give each other permission to speak on each other''s behalf. So, if can''t combine memberships then I need them to complete the form. MPB needs to submit the form to Zion somehow as well. They''ve been together for 5 years and living together since Sept. 2022.  They had a bad accident Nov. 26th, 2022 in a rental car. Natalie has MedPay which covers her for $25K and she had another accident in Sept. 2022 and had another $25K from MedPay. Neither accident was her fault. She''s all set with bills on her end. Jon is dealing with Zion for his costs. He''s exceeding his $1000 IUA. He''s opened the Need with Zion. But, they were waiting for a letter from Progressive stating they are covering some aspect which he sent multiple times and isn''t getting a response. So, some bills are threatening to go to collections already.  I''ll send him the Excel Tracking Sheet and inquire about the status of his Need.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-22 11:21:56', '2023-03-22 11:21:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116243047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109410009', 'Craig Schkade', NULL, '3-22-2023:  The above chat suggests they connect w/me via e-mail for answers to Craig''s questions.  I talked w/Jennifer & we both agree: the amount of information to answer these questions in the depth required, needs to be done via a phone conversation - not e-mail. 
     After they told him to, he sent his questions to my e-mail address since they provided it in the chat.  I replied, supplying him with the concierge hours and letting him know there will be soooo much we need to discuss, please call us.  I also let him know I''ve added Jennifer (my supervisor) to the e-mail thread, so she''s aware e-mails are being suggested.  They just don''t work well for the amount of info that will be needed to supplied:
     1)    My annual physical is 3/30/2023.  I have done my bloodwork.  What do I do to process this as my annual wellness visit?  Also, I''d like to consider having another doctor within the MPB system look at my lab results and give his opinion.
     2)    I see a dermatogolist at least once a year and he performs ''spot treatment'' on my face where there is a potential for future skin cancer (or takes a sample of which 3-4 times I''ve had low level basil cell).  But I''ve also applied the topical solution that ''peels your face''.  I''d like to consider doing that again soon.  Is their an option to get the medication thru MPB versus going to my doctor?     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-22 10:44:45', '2023-03-22 10:52:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116317048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106312002', 'Steven Welch', NULL, 'Steve called in for his log-in credentials for the MPB member portal and to find out how to upload his dental bills for reimbursement. It appears that Steve did not get my vm from 12/27/22 as he had asked the same question (see my answer below). I did send him his log-in credentials via Admin123. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-03-22 09:51:10', '2023-03-22 09:51:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116317038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094511002', 'Kelsey Kardos', NULL, 'Bobby and Kelsey are at the pediatrician''s office with their daughter, Zoey. She had a high fever and was not feeling well. Kelsey wanted to know how to upload bills and receipts to Zion and Bobby requested that I send the instructions via email. I will send the instructions and I advised Bobby not to worry about anything pertaining to this need until they are home and settled with Zoey. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-03-22 08:53:28', '2023-03-22 08:53:28'),
