  ('zcrm_1579374000116235021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081920010', 'Daniel Minerva', NULL, '3-21-2023:  Dan called.  He has high cholesterol & the doctor wants him to do an ultrasound and some lab tests to ck his levels.  He''s allergic to statins, so they are working to improve things via diet, etc.  
     - We walked thru using HCBB, Healthgrades.com, for finding providers to do the ultrasound and help w/this issue.  He''s going to go thru & find a provider he''s interested in.
     - He had an ultrasound at the beginning of the year & some bloodwork.  He''s going to gather those receipts & his coming ultrasound.  Then will call us/me to walk him thru how to sub a ''med need''.  He isn''t particularly tech savvy, so I think it will be imp to walk him thru the process & not just send him the link.
     - Since it''s high chol, I did not know how they will handle this need.  IF they consider it pre-x, he''s been working w/it for years, we walked thru worst case scenario = phase in process for sharing.  He''s in his 2nd yr of memb & realizes it could be 25k max this yr, etc...     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-21 11:50:19', '2023-03-21 13:02:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116235016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000070248151', 'Ray Skelton', NULL, '3-21-2023:  Ray called thinking he was taking off his ex-wife & child.  We went over, since he''s aged into Medicare this month = March 1, 2023, he''s no longer elig for our healthcare.  As the primary memb, the mo he becomes elig for Medicare, he''s no longer elig for our healthcare.  Therefore, since he''s primary on the acct, it''s no longer active, so no need to worry about taking them off.  Let him know we sent e-mails re: all of this so he''d be aware, he just doesn''t think he saw them.
     - He was removing them because they have other cov, so no concern on trying to sub a new application for his wife & daughter.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-21 11:44:32', '2023-03-30 02:36:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000116231008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080072002', 'James Romano', NULL, '03.14.23:  Was copied on Pattis'' email to James notifying him he will be aging out of his Care Plus plan as of 5.1.23.

Hi James Romano,

It looks like you will be turning 65 in the month of May. At this time you will no longer be eligible for membership in the Medical Cost Sharing Program with Zion.  However, you may maintain membership in the Healthcare Essentials product giving you ongoing access to your Telehealth membership with CirrusMD, Mental Health Services, MPB Pharmacy Benefit Plan, Personal Medical Records Vault and QR Life Code for emergency purpose and more. 
Please contact your Healthcare Advisor for assistance with converting your membership.

MPowering Benefits values you as our client and we hope you remain a member.  However, if you choose to cancel your entire membership, please fill out the following online form, 
MPowering Benefits Cancellation, so I can process your cancellation.  Please submit this to me between the 1st & 20th of April.   Feel free to contact your advisor if you have any questions. 

Thank you,
Patti Baron', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2023-03-21 11:41:43', '2023-03-21 11:51:36'),
