  ('zcrm_1579374000115847125', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086964002', 'Lani Cordova', NULL, 'Pronounced:  "Lawn-e"
3/16/2023:  Lani called my cell.  Her son Kimball hurt himself skiing today.  She couldn''t remember how to have him present, so we went over, no ''ins'' & no card to present, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, offer to pay 1k (IUA) and can they bill you bal so you can get the $ together.   She asked about ntwk & I reminded her that w/the catastrophic component you don''t have to worry about a ntwk.
     - Lani is going to call when she''s not out picking up her daughter (maybe tomorrow or early next week) so I can show her how to sub a ''med need'', then she may have her adult son learn how to do this.
     - Lani lives in an area where the PHCS ntwk did not work, so I told her to watch her e-mail for a new pdf Planstin card w/out the PHCS logo, as we will eventually be converting the ''prev care'' to no req''d ntwk either.  You''ll just need a doc willing to bill your ''prev care'' to Planstin for you.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-16 18:53:45', '2023-03-16 18:53:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115885085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114408009', 'Kim Scott', NULL, '03.16.2023 Kim called to kindly inquire and get clarification about the waiting periods on preventative care. Someone told her that there''s a waiting period. She called Planstin, and they told her no there isn''t a waiting period. So she called us to confirm or learn more prior to her making an appointment for a colonoscopy or mamm or child immunization.
I consulted with Cari to make sure I''m not mixing Zion''s guidelines with Planstin''s. And I reassured Kim with the information from Cari, that there''s no waiting period.
However, Kim requested that language on hand to refer to, something I would do as well, and I could not locate that language on Planstin site. Unfortunately, Kim was still not feeling confident in moving forward with her preventative appointments, so she decided she will wait the 6 month period she was told initially (who she does not remember the name to). NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-16 18:01:32', '2023-03-17 16:20:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115885056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098248002', 'Marcus Alig', NULL, '03.16.2023 Marcus called needing guidance on setting up his physical preventative appt. He asked if there''s a network involved, if so, how does he find a doctor there, how to present at the appt.
I guided him to the Post welcome Call email, to star it, and locate the Multiplan Link in there. He did both, and while there we searched for a list for practice together. I told him to confirm with the doctor''s office when he''s making the appt, if they are still part of the PHCS network. I told him he could nominate his present doctor if she/he is not on the list. If he sees a doctor not in network Preventative will not cover it. If the doctor orders a lab/test or anything outside of the PREVENTATIVE care, I told Marcus he''ll request them to bill it separately, and for that bill to present himself on it as a cash pay patient and request the cash-pay discount. Should the results go any further then we will open a medical need for this diagnostic.
He also wanted to know what blood work or other services/tests do they cover in the physical. I guided him to the healthcare.gov site > to all adults link, to view the preventative care by law (MEC). He specified on bloodwork, and I said right now, we are seeing they are only covering the BASIC lipid panel. I consulted with Cari via teams to help me find the language on the website, and she messaged me with it.
Marcus was wondering which card to use; MPB or Planstin, for the preventative appts. I explained the MPB card is a reference card. The Planstin card is what you will present to the doctors offices.
Marcus inquired about the MAP program. I guided him to the M&S collaborative page with us. I shared where their number is to call and start his counseling program and showed him the impact app information and the resources cubed on the front. -  NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-16 15:48:55', '2023-03-17 17:54:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115885048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105831009', 'Dariusz Szteborowski', NULL, '3.16.2023 Dariusz called, with the practice of following Cari''s above instructions to use the discounted lab prepaid sites, Jason Health.
