  ('zcrm_1579374000115889003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089048002', 'Gregory Von Berg', NULL, '03.15.2023 Initially, Gregory called to better understand how to present himself for a preventative appointment for colonoscopy. Email via CRM ''how to submit bills to Zion''
Emailed via outlook Provider list 
The only computer working now for him is at work, so he''ll have to wait till when he''s feeling better and at work to open the two emails.
Because he was diagnosed with Diverticulosis in the past, doctors are monitoring it so it does not develop into diverticulitis. I was consulting with Cari and Jen via teams on whether getting an MRI is part of the colonoscopy screening or would that need to be billed separately. Cari shared that there seems to be a new procedure, where they start with possibly an MRI, then only if they see spots, do the do the invasive colonoscopy. Then we got into the Diverticulitis being already diagnostic, and a medical need request is in order. Cari clarified that the Diverticulosis would be considered a diagnostic test.
I brought Cari in on the call to help smooth the edges on the process for Gregory.
Gregory was very confused about the plan, how it works and seemed overwhelmed with all the moving pieces with the services platform, preventative and medical cost sharing.
Cari - explained, preventative vs. diagnostic and how/why it changes, the details on IUA. It turns out his MRI was for his hip and his back. So the medical need request will reflect that specific issue. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-15 11:25:36', '2023-03-15 15:19:39'),
