  ('zcrm_1579374000115738013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006727', 'Charles Korb III', NULL, '3-13-23 Chuck is having a terrible experience with Redirect.
"What is going on with Redirect Health?  I was repairing my 88 years old mother''s sewer system and received a puncture wound in the left thigh from an old rusty nail on December 15, 2022.  It required me to contact Redirect Health who screened my situation and set up a follow-up "Virtual Doctor Appointment" with one of their Primary Care Physicians on 12/15/22.  The doctor confirmed my feeling that I needed a Tetanus Shot and a course of antibiotics.  She sent both prescriptions to me and a copy to the closest Walgreens which she chose as they were pre-approved and in the Redirect Health system.  The situation has been a real eye-opener on a number of fronts.  Firstly, for some unknown reason, Redirect Health suspended my membership close to a year ago and could not provide a reason for why they took this action.  They reactivated my membership which took 4 phone calls and a month of time.  It took another 2 weeks to receive my membership card which was never provided in the first place.  They have also failed to reimburse me for my out-of-pocket expenses which amounted to $15.99 for the Walgreens Medication and $55.99 for the ADACEK: Tet Tox-Diph-Acell, Pertussis A vaccination which I elected to get from COSTCO because Walgreens had a 7 day waiting list and wanted $105.00.  Upon responding to a Redirect Health request (via text) for bill copies, I scanned and texted them promptly but nobody on their end uploaded the receipts into their app. It took two calls over three weeks to discover that the bills were not processed properly.  They said it was fine for me to call in lieu of using the smartphone app if I preferred, which was my choice so I could keep track of things with a live contact.  The rep who sent the initial text was new and not aware they need to be uploaded by him into their app.  Wendy, I have made over a dozen phone calls to the Redirect Health 1(888) 407-7928 member number with poor results and spoken on each occasion directly to CS Reps as well as the Call Center Manager Ashly.  They have all provided me assurances that the situation had been escalated and that I would receive payment within 45 days.  At the end of every call I was told I would receive a follow-up call and an update by the end of the day.  To date, I have not fielded a single progress report follow up call from their organization.  Justifiably, my confidence level is less than zero at this point.  Last month it was communicated that the matter was closed out and payment would be forthcoming.  What the payment amount will be is still a mystery as now they are backpedaling on the prescription cost as they feel it was not a "Low Cost Pharmacy" and the $15.99 was less than my out-of-pocket copayment.  Previously, it was communicated that I would be reimbursed the full amount of $71.98 ($15.99 + $55.99).  Frankly, my last couple of contacts with Redirect Health have been very direct and I have asked if they are having cash-flow problems as they keep giving me the run-around.  Is MPowering Benefits aware of monetary problems at Redirect Health?  At this point I have put off my Annual Wellness Visit and have delayed initiating a Chiropractic Care Visit regiment because I don''t want to be left holding the proverbial bag if they don''t cover these costs.  Can you or the concierge team help me out with this situation?  Can we deduct what they owe me from this month''s auto-deduct payment?

Thanks again for your continued support and assistance.

Sincere best regards,

Chuck Korb"

I''m reaching out to Mike Bechtol.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-13 13:25:37', '2023-03-13 13:25:37'),
