  ('zcrm_1579374000115426008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130435013', 'Stephen Judy', NULL, '3-8-23 Steve is 57, self-employed. His wife is a nurse and has benefits. To add him the cost would be about the same as he''s paying now which is $446.18. He watched the video and my interview as well as completed the Questionnaire!  He was well versed before we started. No pre-x other than he takes Prozac for anxiety which will cost less than his current $30 co-pay for 90 days.  He has his colonoscopy at age 50 and it was clean. So, he won''t need it again until he turns 60. He understands HSA but doesn''t have one at the moment. He eats healthy, exercises, etc.  He''s choosing SECURE $1000/$325.  Completed enrollment and knows to do Welcome Call. Prefers to do it right away if allowed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-08 13:26:10', '2023-03-08 13:37:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115401048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115273002', 'Ostyn Mills', NULL, '3/7/23-Advisor called in and told me that member enrolled in the wrong IUA and wanted to change from $5000 to $1000.  I made change in A123', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-03-08 13:23:01', '2023-03-08 13:23:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115388024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104964002', 'Sandra Erickson', NULL, '03.08.2023 Sandra was transferred over from Planstin (..-..-7526), and is very unhappy. Although she was unhappy, she was kind, respectful and receptive in hearing the responses.
Sandra moved from CA to AZ. Sandra was mainly worried about attaining/keeping an HSA, even without having a business. Sandra also needed to change her address.
I consulted via teams with Jen and Cari, regarding the HSA differing per state. Cari responded with it''s federal, so not likely. 
If I were to have understood Sandra clearly, MPB mislead her on a plan that does not fit her wishes and life at the time in CA (HSA interest & Secure would''ve been the plan to go with, given her location at the time of signing). She seemed to have gotten the run-around through lack of communication, and alignment of information with the plans. 
By the time she reached me today, she had already been on the phone with Planstin for 45 minutes or so, and did not want to spend any more time on this matter today (due to her frustration perhaps). I offered her to speak to our sales department, but she was not interested nor in a place to discuss the matter at the time.
The notes in Admin could be more clear, as when I was reading them, first it says she signed up by herself without an advisor (still no advisor has been assigned, according to CRM), but then at the bottom says that she spoke with Tony. 
In the end of our call, unfortunately Sandra does not feel like she can trust us as a company, so she can drop her insurance, which is her ultimate goal. But now, she finds MPB to be disorganized, lacks communication, unprofessional and untrustworthy. 
She did share that she has an extensive amount of communication via email that maybe we can revisit with her to close the gaps in our services.

I hope we can turn this around. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-08 13:18:33', '2023-03-08 14:47:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115428003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109781008', 'Lauren Guida', NULL, 'Lauren responded back to me on SalesIQ from my greeting message, and she asked how she can start utilizing her MAP Mental Health Benefits. She knew she gets 12 a year, to which I explained/corrected her on how the sessions work with 4 a month, then a 2-month break, back to 4 a month with the 2-month break, so on and so forth. I sent her the link to the member portals and screenshotted the picture of the MSEAP Portal she is to click on, along with giving her the access code of MAP to use when she clicks the portal. She got in and started to call them to get all set up. She thanked me and is all set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-03-08 13:17:39', '2023-03-08 13:17:39'),
