  ('zcrm_1579374000115316023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '3-7-23 From an email I sent on behalf of Cami to Zion. 
"You can see the communications below. I''ve explained to Cami that her membership with Zion began 8/1/2020 and she was in the grandfathered group who had immediate sharing of pre-x at $25K in year one. Then the normal pre-x sharing schedule continues on. From my calculations, Cami is in her 3rd year of sharing which should be up to $50K, correct? She opened the Need in May of 2022 but never needed sharing, so never submitted any expenses. The only expenses that were shareable began in Sept. 2020. Again, it appears to me that her sharing should be up to $50K at this point.  Please confirm.

If she''s willing and able to wait until after Aug 1st 2023, that opens up sharing of $125K, correct? This is how I would see it and explain it to my clients. If it''s different, then we at MPB need to know. If all that isn''t true, what are the chances of getting the need shared through the Special Needs. This client has done everything in her power to avoid surgery and has paid for everything on her own. She''s received a 40% discount on all expenses thus far by paying cash. She''s truly the client that is doing her part. She also leads an association which is partnered with MPB and refers members to me/MPB constantly. 

Final question, if she does the surgery in year 3 with $50K sharing and then needs PT in year 4, does that give her sharing up to $125K as of Aug. 2023 for the remaining PT that she might need?"', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-07 18:59:01', '2023-03-07 18:59:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115257075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103573001', 'Adrian Kumpula', NULL, '3-7-2023:  Adrian called.  Katriina & he found out last week they were 8-weeks pregnant, but she miscarried yesterday.  The doc wants to do a surgical procedure & they needed to know how to proceed.  Since it''s base around a maternity need, I showed him how to start that & told him to put this is more urgent because the doc wants this done asap (says it''s dangerous to leave & better sooner than later). 
