  ('zcrm_1579374000115300008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073887102', 'Shelley Sanner', NULL, '03.07.2023 Shelley had a mammogram a few weeks ago, and a few additional procedures need to get done due to  one breast being dense. Additional mammogram imaging  (~$365), and then an ultra sound (~$426). Her PCP dated in order the coding of the initial visit to align with the medical need with Zion. 
                                                     **********************************************
Shelley and I reconnected today on the subject of whether we opened a medical need request or not.
We were discussing whether to open one before her stated procedures or after. Then Shelley shared that they recommending annual breast MRI''s due to the suspicion of her breast findings and being high risk. 
I consulted with Cari, and eventually brought her in on the call, with the notion that the annual breast MRI needs to be coded diagnostic. If it gets coded screening just to confirm anything, it won''t pass through the medical need, and preventative won''t cover it due to plan limitations. Cari reminded Shelley, that they also won''t cover anything more than a 2D imaging, try to cram all the appointments in a short period of time.  Cari asked if she opened an HSA, Shelley said not yet, and Cari also recommended she speak to her advisor, Jill Clark (JC) about an HMA. Cari went into a brief description of what that entails, including how it''s not like an HSA. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-07 11:10:36', '2023-03-07 13:25:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115298008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113582001', 'Jennifer Levine', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-03-07 11:04:46', '2023-03-07 11:04:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115300003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105482010', 'Mark Rosal', NULL, '03.07.2023 Mark called regarding a physical that needs to get done for his son, and was confused whether he should present his MPB card with the QR life code on there, or does he use something else.
I explained  that his plan is split into 3 branches: Preventative w/ Planstin that is what he will need to present at his son''s appointment, Medical Cost Sharing for high medical costs or catastrophes and what the QR Life code is for, and the Essentials. 
I coached Marc that all he will need for his preventative physical appointments is the Planstin card that most likely made it to him via email, and to make sure his services are done through the PHCS network. I downloaded a list of Pediatrics in the zip code 08840 and emailed it via Outlook.
Due to needing the physical ASAP, Mark might take his son to the present doctor, Maritza Santiago, who does not seem to be on the PHCS network. However, will consider the list for future. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-07 10:58:14', '2023-03-07 10:58:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115257007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109568001', 'Donald Whitfield', NULL, '3-7-2023:  Donald is super arguementative.  Does not listen.  He''s in a really bad space.  "Nobody at Zion cares that I''m over here waiting for my ACL to get fixed."
     - I called Zion, tt Ulises (male) - he sounds new & unsure.  He had me on hold a good long time & finally trans me to the processor Christina at 16.3 minutes.
       She says Pedmont Hosp & Pedmont Orthopedics - Corr fax #: 435-631-9478.  According to Christine:
