  ('zcrm_1579374000115020003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003967007', 'Jennilee Chapman', NULL, 'Jennilee called because she received an email stating her "subscription" has been cancelled. I wasn''t sure what she was referring to when she said "subscription" so I transferred her to Patti. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-03-02 08:12:34', '2023-03-02 08:12:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010656162', 'Darryl Lyles', NULL, '3-1-23 Darryl called bc he wants to understand the process better. He''s receiving a letter from his Dr. stating this health issue is acute and brand new. Dr. has No problem writing the letter. Darryl says there''s no way he''d live like this in pain for all those years. I let him know the $50K cap will be removed once they receive that letter. He''s working with HCBB and Amra in TN. They started with Valley View Hospital which was $68K but he pressed to go to the Surgical Center which will be $42K instead. He''s been incredible about wanting the highest quality care at a fair price, not pressing to do it immediately. He''s willing to wait an extra month to get it done more affordably. He just doesn''t want to wait until Aug. for the pre-x clause to increase to $125K. That shouldn''t be relevant once Zion receives the dr. note. He said surgical center wants 50% up front and 50% after and drs. want full amt up front.  He feels calmer and will call me if/when he needs more help. He learned that I worked with Andre MPtisos as well. Andre just had a knee replacement surgery. I think that is helping Darryl to feel more comfortable. He''s all set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 17:51:39', '2023-03-01 17:51:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058265123', 'Xiao Neng March', NULL, '3-1-23 Submitted as a ticket.
 I just received a call from Scott March for Xioa Neng March. They thought they cancelled her membership on Jan. 17th, 2023. But, there''s no cancellation form. He was just billed (yesterday) for 2 months since Dayra discovered he hadn''t been billed due to the changes on our end. So, in light of that he just called to make sure the membership is cancelled. I helped him complete the cancellation form now. His wife''s employer coverage began 2/1/23.  His only request is to be refunded for one month, if at all possible. Can we make this happen since MPB failed to bill him properly?', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 17:10:19', '2023-03-01 17:10:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114998040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058265123', 'Xiao Neng March', NULL, '03.01.2023 Scott called to cancel his wife''s, Xiao, membership with us and get reimbursed. He remembers speaking with Kitty to help him cancel a while back, but he''s been billed twice so far.
Scott was a bit frustrated and wanted me to fix the problem, but I told him although I am not able to complete the cancellation for him and reimburse him, I can forward him to the right party. He was still frustrated and did not want to transferred anywhere. I shared with him that someone was trying to connect with him back on 1/25 & 1/26. He asked who was it, and I said do you know who Wendy Scipione is? He said I think so, it sounds familiar. I said Yes Your Advisor. He proceeded to want to speak with her then, since she tried to contact him. I gave him her contact phone number, and Patti''s. THen I transferred him to her to leave a VM. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-01 16:58:57', '2023-03-01 16:59:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115007023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610497', 'Adam Burstein', NULL, '3-1-2023:  Adam called about his wife''s ''prev care'' labs.  We went over the only item we hear is consistently paid for his the basic LIPID panel.  He said they went to Quest because they were in-ntwk, but are having trouble because they can''t tell if Quest ever billed "us".  I let him know all of those items go thru the ''prev care'' TPA - Planstin & they would be the ones who could see if they''d rec''d the bill(s).  Did tell him I''ve had a few members lately saying Quest says they keep billing Planstin, then Planstin saying they never receive the bills.  Made sure he has their # in case he has to call them back, then trans him dir to Planstin.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-01 16:46:40', '2023-03-01 16:46:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115007018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081769002', 'Robert Henchel', NULL, '3-1-2023:  Rbt called.  He has a lump under his are & wanted to know how to handle.  It was a bit difficult, because Rbt kept talking over me.  
     - He orig thought he should have his ''prev care'' annual appt at the same time.  I went over how it''s best to separate the two & keep his ''prev care'' appt 100% prev due to a diagnosis/treatment during that visit can screwup the medical coding.  My sugg is to keep the two appts separate.  He seemed fine with that.
     - Went over how to present, ''cash-pay '', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, resp for 1k IUA, but keep pymt receipts, detailed inv, etc.  Even if not over 1k right away, but will be ongoing, 6mo deadline so call us for help sub a ''med need'' within first 4 mos.  [Even after I just said that, his response was: "so I should wait until I''ve hit 1k".]   I reiterated, "No, exactly the opposite.  You do NOT need to wait.  They have a deadline for starting the ''med need'' & including all of the expenses.  Your need doesn''t have to be complete by the 6mos mark, we just need to start it.  I think he understood, yet I wasn''t sure he was listening well enough to completely comprehend.  At the end, he mentioned going to the Urg Care since he''s doesn''t have a reg PCP & I said that''s a good starting point.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-01 16:40:47', '2023-03-01 16:40:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114998032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107128020', 'Tessa Bergman', NULL, '03.01.2023 Tessa called to learn how to proceed with having to see her doctor for a neck symptom that resulted in an X-ray and MRI. I guided her to begin a medical need, and to scan all her documents to get them ready to get uploaded.
I sent her an email, via CRM, on hot to submit medical need to Zion.
Together we filled out the form, till she needed to scan her docs. I told her to she can do that part at her own time, upload them and click SUBMIT. Give Zion around 78 hours to assign a processor and contact information. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-01 16:31:00', '2023-03-01 16:31:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000115007013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110261002', 'Lance Casey', NULL, '3-1-2023:  Lance called telehealth (CirrusMD?) and was told he should get a COVID test.  I sugg he call some of his local pharmacies to see if the gvmt is still helping cover those for uninsured people since he does not have ins that helps pay for that.  That seemed to suffice & he was Googling while we spoke.
     - Also dbl ck''s & it looks like you can still order the 4 free tests on the USPS.com site.  Found the specific site for him & gave him that info.  It won''t help for this time, but maybe it''ll help to have them around?     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-03-01 16:24:40', '2023-03-01 16:48:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114998021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038883009', 'Melissa Bajza', NULL, '03.01.2023 Melissa called frustrated regarding a preventative appt that resulted into diagnostic one, not being covered/paid yet going on 11 months. Melissa frequently shared her frustration, how it is on us MPB not her, and that she does not have the time anymore to deal with, therefore we need to take care of it and get back with her.
I shared this elevated issue with Jen and Cari via teams, and Cari guided me as I was speaking to Melissa. She did notice Melissa has not consulted with the Concierge team since 1/22. We do not have any record of her trying to get our assistance. 
I started a medical need with Melissa on the phone. Cari recommended I encourage her to upload the declined preventative care. Originally we didn''t realize how old the colonoscopy was on her old plan. &nbsp;Melissa seemed frustrated by not knowing pulling a polyp makes it a healthshare, rather than a preventative item.
Afterwards, I connected with Wendy via teams, and shared more details with me regarding her plan being under Redirect, and that Wendy placed the ball on their court by referring to an email confirmation about covering Melissa''s colon. procedure. &nbsp;NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-01 16:06:36', '2023-03-01 17:22:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115515002', 'Osha Waters', NULL, '2-28-23 Ossha is 49 turning 50 mid March 2023. Referred by Nancy Gentry. She''s had Golden Rule/UHC with an HSA through her husband. But, getting divorced now. She moved and missed a payment bc it mail wasn''t forwarded. So, her plan was cancelled unbeknownst to her. She''s doing part-time home schooling and working towards starting her own business soon. But, they don''t do their annual wellness visits. They only do alternative care. CARE+ is their best option and  employment doesn''t matter. She and kids are healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco.  They are paying $14,624 per year which is $1218.66 per month and that''s going up to $15,999 per year which is $1333.25 per month for the entire family. With CARE+ EC it will be $520/$1000 which is $6240 per year. Plus if husband joins separately, it''s $265/$1000 which is $3180. Therefore, $9420 for all 5 of them vs $15,999.  Also, she asked if virtual healthcare can address strep throat and asking for a strep test. I got an answer after we talked which is that CirrusMD cannot prescribe strep tests. They must go in person for that. Bummer!  I will let her know in email.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 15:57:41', '2023-03-01 15:59:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029364085', 'Kristy Tripp', NULL, '3-1-23 Kristy is submitting her need with Zion and cc''ed me on the email. I just wanted to make sure she started with the correct process and with the help of the MPB Concierge Team. I responded as such. Her bills are just exceeding her IUA for potential reimbursement, especially if it proceeds onward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 15:36:40', '2023-03-01 15:36:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114998013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105466010', 'Anna Marie Somera', NULL, '03.01.2023 Anna Marie called to attain a PHCS list for her physical/preventative care appointment.
She gave me 3 names (facilities and individuals) to search on the multi-plan, and none of them showed up on the list.
She said she would like to go through another set of names on her own, so I guided her to the post welcome call email and she was familiar and found the multi-plan link.
Anne Marie did revisit the concept of RPB versus PHCS Network with Planstin, and I told her there was a miscommunication between Planstin and our company. AO right now, they are pushing it another 6-10 weeks from now. She wanted assurance that is a solid date, and I told her given that I''m at the bottom of the communication line, it''s not  a date I can guarantee.
She asked how to connect back with me personally, and I said to ask for Nahla. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-03-01 15:02:03', '2023-03-01 15:02:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114977023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113576002', 'Kimberly Dare', NULL, 'Kimberly is such a lovely person. As we got into the depths of Kimberly''s welcome call, she realized that the plan that she has is not for her. She was looking for something with preventative care included and I suggested speaking with Karen about either the Secure or Direct plan. As we were continuing to speak, Kimberly has some underlying health issues that would not be shareable in her first year of membership as they are pre-x conditions. We also discussed her IUA, which she was under the impression she only had to meet one IUA in a year. Once we went over the specifics of how an IUA works, Kimberly had a better understanding. Kimberly feels that she needs a more extensive plan for her healthcare needs so she will be reaching out to Karen on her own to discuss other options. She was such a pleasure to speak with! JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-03-01 14:45:27', '2023-03-01 14:46:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038883009', 'Melissa Bajza', NULL, '3-1-23 UPDATE - Melissa aplogized for her frustration and behavior on the phone. I''m now awaiting a response from Redirect.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 14:41:58', '2023-03-01 14:41:58'),
