  ('zcrm_1579374000114671074', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048228151', 'Jennifer Wright', NULL, 'Member''s 3/23 payment declined 1st notice sent 2/27 - via email (vm not set up) 3/2 final notice sent', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-02-27 12:36:33', '2023-03-02 11:57:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114724008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044650083', 'Meghan Van Vleet', NULL, '02.27.2023 Meghan called again to let us know that she threw out her RCI card on accident. I consulted with Jen and Cari, since I''m not too familiar with RCI. Cari coached to let her know, she can request a new one from RCI: &nbsp;1-800-795-7772. I forwarded Meghan to RCI. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-27 12:33:25', '2023-02-27 12:33:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114709032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084530002', 'Paul Campanello', NULL, '2-27-2023:  Angie called.  She''s confusing her Planstin ''prev care'' &amp; her healthsharing.  Very challenging.  She says last week you told me for my shoulder issue I have to stay in the PHCS ntwk.  We did some education:  shoulder ''issue'' is NOT ''prev care'' = NO ntwk req''d.  "But you told me last week..."  I let her know I can see she called re: ''prev care'' last week, but didn''t see any notes on a shoulder issue.  Tried to go over diff w/her again.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-02-27 12:27:00', '2023-03-02 18:49:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114724003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106616001', 'Janet Banks', NULL, '02.27.2023 Janet called to get a PHCS lists for:  gyno & mammo. A few times, she asked if she would have to pay for the visits, and at first I said it depends on the plan that she has, then a few times after that, I repeated that it is part of her plan.
She had a situation where she visited a doctor, via telehealth, for a physical she said, and they ended up charging her.
Later in the conversation, Janet was combining; needing lists to make sure she''s in network, "why did they charge me almost $300?", a telehealth visit, we provided her with the list, she''s only doing what we tell her to do, they charged her through ''Scripts'' (I was unsure if she meant a name to an organization or prescriptions). ALL THE WHILE, Janet was at unease, frustrated due to situation and personal confusion on plan/services usage, which I understand.
I pulled Jennifer in to help with the communication and deciphering the actual problem for Janet. Both Cari and Jennifer are familiar with Janet''s struggles and approach of communication.
Jen''s call dropped close to the end of the call, cause the lines went silent. However, I was able to talk Janet off the ''ledge'', per-se, and divided the call into two situations and offered her an action item, and offered her a communication on our part. PARTS: 1-Call the previous office, Katherine Han, to clarify how they coded her billing. 2-Call the new offices in mind (from the PHCS lists I sent), and say "I''d like to make a preventative appointment that needs to remain preventative." "Are you and all the providers involved in the screening in the PHCS network?"
Janet was receptive, but seemed still a little concerned. OUR HOPES is that Janet finds ease and clarity in using her services and not overwhelmed. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-27 12:26:59', '2023-02-27 13:39:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114719013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060921716', 'Polly Tucker', NULL, '2-27-23 I returned Polly''s vm just now to help her better utilize her membership. She''s also part of WWSRA and just learned they are partnered with MPB as well. She wondering if their memberships are better than hers. They are the same. But, I''ll teach her how to maximize her membership when we talk.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-27 12:22:00', '2023-02-27 12:22:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114671069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103379002', 'Brian Robinson', NULL, 'Member''s 3/23 payment declined 1st notices sent via email &amp; VM - 2/27 Member submitted PU form I will rerun-3/6', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-02-27 12:18:33', '2023-03-06 09:59:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114671061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065297467', 'Sheila Sewell', NULL, 'Member''s 3/23 payment declined 1st notice sent via email &amp; VM - 2/27 (VM full) 3/1 email sent VM still full 3/1-member submitted PU form I will update &amp; Rerun.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-02-27 12:11:58', '2023-03-01 12:54:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114671056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066423001', 'Nicholas Palmer', NULL, 'Member''s 3/23 payment was declined. 1st notice sent via email &amp; VM-2/27 3rd notice sent 3/1 3/1-spoke to gal in his office and they had some fraud and had to close acct.  I directed them to link they will be updating today 3/6- Member submitted Payment update I will rerun', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-02-27 12:00:27', '2023-03-06 08:49:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114719008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114634022', 'Abram Dunaway', NULL, '2-27-23 I uploaded Abe''s Cobra notices in the Docs section in C4. He called and requested his March 1st start date. He should be all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-27 11:56:44', '2023-02-27 11:56:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114719003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044650083', 'Meghan Van Vleet', NULL, '2-27-23 Meghan called to better understand how to navigate the system. The providers keep pressing her on trying to submit bills to RCI for non-wellness. She learned they have discounted rates and was curious if it was better to let them bill RCI. I let her know that will complicate matters and it''s best to pull the card and be firm in needing the self-pay/cash pay price. Sounds like the prices have been reasonable thus far with an $83 Urgent Care bill, $40 vax bill and possibly a $250 visit for another time. That part I was unsure of. Son has recurring sinusitis, so she''s just trying to understand how to best proceed. Since it keeps coming back, I told her to create the Need in case the bills ever exceed her $1500 IUA. This will keep it within the 6 month time limit of submitting the Need and start the tracking process. She also wants to set up an HSA which I will send her instructions now. She was super grateful. She''s a naturopathic doctor and understands Super Bills and will ask for that moving forward since they don''t seem to want to provide an itemized bill.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-27 11:54:02', '2023-02-27 11:54:02'),
