  ('zcrm_1579374000114043071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058967035', 'Margaret Randolph', NULL, '02.16.2023 Margaret called to learn how to proceed through her DIRECT plan, to have a colonoscopy performed. I told her it is part of her plan, under Zion''s preventative care.
I was not too familiar with that preventative care service yet with MPB, so I consulted with Cari via teams.
She recommended that I send her the "Submitting a Med Need" e-mail for Zion.  Then take her in & show her the ''Preventative Care'' in the dropdown.  Once she has the appointment scheduled they''ll work out payment. So Margaret and I did just that. AND Zion responded immediately that they will be in contact.
Cari and I also shared the information about colonoscopies procedure coverage through Zion: COLONOSCOPIES Screening colonoscopies are available every 10 years beginning at age 45. In addition to a screening colonoscopy and the related anesthesia, diagnostic testing, including biopsies and pathology, performed as part of the screen are also shared. Any separate appointment or visit fees are not considered shareable as part of the colonoscopy service. The $5000 sharing cap applies to the total cost of the visit and all shareable services. We encourage members to have this service performed at an outpatient center and not in the hospital, as the centers usually charge less for their services." - NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-16 16:57:53', '2023-02-16 16:57:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113990052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111775018', 'Lori Sookhoo', NULL, '2-16-2023:  Lori called.  Has no idea what she''s signed up for.  Kept talking about her ins.  Did a little bit of education.  She was willing to sched her ''Welcome Call'' as a great place to start her understanding.  Can see it on the sched w/Jennifer on 2/20/23 at 3:30pm EST & knows Jennifer will call her on the phone she listed in the appt.
     - She does not think she''s rec''d her Planstin care (& thinks she would have deleted a pdf version because she didn''t know who Planstin is).  I let her know they will go over this in the Welcome Call.
     - [Does have her MPB.Health ref card though.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-02-16 16:45:52', '2023-02-16 16:45:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114043060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111619002', 'Lynne Diekmann', NULL, '02.16.2023 Lynne called to confirm what type of member she is, given her receipt of the fulfillment package.
I attempted to search for her on here, and Diekmann did not show up in our system at all. I looking in admin123 and that name is not there either. I double checked on the spelling of her last name again with Lynne, and I had it correct.
I consulted with Cari on the issue via teams, and she creatively looked her up under Dickman, and there she is on both CRM and Admin123. We confirmed her birthday, it also needs correction. The email is correct, and the address is correct. I brought Cari in on the call, as there was a legal concern raised due to the nature of the two needed corrections.
Lynne initially was interested to go in have a development on her skin to get looked at. What she is experiencing is an itchy mark on her face, and too small for possible having Telehealth involved.
To proceed to having her use the platform services, especially HCBB to search for any providers in her super remote area, her information with MPB needs correction: Last name spelling (from Dickman to DIEKMANN) and her date of birth (from 01-30-1963 to 10-30-1963), Lynne needs to speak directly to Patti to clear her profile and its inception. I direct transferred her to Patti to leave a message - NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-16 16:18:04', '2023-02-16 17:57:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113990046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111619002', 'Lynne Diekmann', NULL, '2-16-2023:  Lynne''s account is completely off.  Her last name sb: Diekmann, her dob is: 10/30/1963.  Sent Patti info via Teams chat so she can address.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-02-16 16:03:17', '2023-02-18 00:40:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113990038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108617019', 'Adriana Baudry', NULL, '2-16-2023:  Adriana called.  She has what they think may be a torn miniscus.  We went over this will be a healthshare ''med need'' so she''s resp for the 1k IUA.  Call us once you know more so we can start a ''med need'' - went over deadlines, getting it started so she'' has the approval, IF non- emerg surg > 5k call us prior to sched anything & we can see if Care Conn can get her a pkg she likes so she never sees a bill, etc.
     - HCBB: took her to her post ''Welcome Call'' e-mail & showed her how to use HCBB to find fair price & a good doc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-02-16 15:40:23', '2023-02-16 15:44:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114043052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000020299015', 'Brittany Perrotto', NULL, '02.16.2023 Brittany called because she tried using CirrusMD but is unable to. She did share that they have been with MPB for around 5 years, but changed plans 12/2023.
She emailed CirrusMD to confirm their emails are still working. CirrusMD confirmed that they are, but Brittany theorizes that they may not have made the connection with the change of accounts and reconnecting the emails. When using their emails, CirrusMD''s site says "your account has expired". When she tries re-registering via invitation link, it says email is already in use.
I consulted with Cari and Jen via teams, they both agreed that it is not a new issue with CirrusMD, and that Jen will check with John Kach. In addition, they both agreed that we open a CirrusMD ticket.
I asked Brittany for both of their unique emails, told her MPB is putting in a ticket and will get this sorted out ASAP, but to also lean on seeing a PCP or urgent care to care for their child''s health.
After speaking with Brittany, Cari coached me on putting in a ticket with CirrusMD via outlook email to their support team.  - NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-02-16 15:29:49', '2023-02-16 15:30:17'),
